B.aQ4=new A.c(B.h,["God created the heavens and the earth in seven days.",!1,"God created everything in six days and rested on the seventh day. The seventh day was a day of rest, not creation.","Genesis 2:2","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aLu=new A.c(B.h,["The first woman was created from the rib of Adam.",!0,"God caused Adam to fall into a deep sleep, took one of his ribs, and formed Eve from it.","Genesis 2:21-22","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aNC=new A.c(B.h,["The serpent in the Garden of Eden tempted Adam first.",!1,"The serpent spoke to Eve first, and she ate the forbidden fruit before giving some to Adam.","Genesis 3:1-6","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aLS=new A.c(B.h,["Cain was the first son of Adam and Eve.",!0,"Cain was the firstborn son of Adam and Eve, and Abel was the second.","Genesis 4:1-2","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aLC=new A.c(B.h,["Abel was a farmer and Cain was a shepherd.",!1,"It was the opposite: Abel kept flocks (shepherd) and Cain worked the soil (farmer).","Genesis 4:2","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aOK=new A.c(B.h,["Methuselah is the oldest person recorded in the Bible, living 969 years.",!0,"Methuselah lived 969 years, making him the longest-lived person mentioned in Scripture.","Genesis 5:27","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aM_=new A.c(B.h,["Noah took two of every animal onto the ark.",!1,"Noah took two of every unclean animal, but seven pairs of every clean animal and seven pairs of every kind of bird.","Genesis 7:2-3","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aP6=new A.c(B.h,["The rainbow was given as a sign of God's covenant never to flood the entire earth again.",!0,"After the flood, God set the rainbow in the clouds as a sign of His covenant with Noah and all living creatures.","Genesis 9:13-15","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aOy=new A.c(B.h,["The Tower of Babel was built in Egypt.",!1,"The Tower of Babel was built in the land of Shinar (Babylonia), not Egypt.","Genesis 11:2-4","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aN6=new A.c(B.h,["Abraham was originally called Abram.",!0,'God changed his name from Abram to Abraham, meaning "father of many nations."',"Genesis 17:5","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aLG=new A.c(B.h,["Lot's wife was turned into a pillar of sand.",!1,"Lot's wife was turned into a pillar of salt, not sand, when she looked back at Sodom.","Genesis 19:26","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aNv=new A.c(B.h,["Abraham was asked to sacrifice his son Isaac on Mount Moriah.",!0,"God tested Abraham by asking him to sacrifice Isaac on Mount Moriah, but provided a ram as a substitute.","Genesis 22:2","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aKt=new A.c(B.h,["Esau sold his birthright for a bowl of lentil stew.",!0,"Esau was so hungry he sold his birthright to his brother Jacob for bread and lentil stew.","Genesis 25:33-34","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aRx=new A.c(B.h,["Jacob had ten sons.",!1,"Jacob had twelve sons, who became the twelve tribes of Israel.","Genesis 35:22-26","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aLB=new A.c(B.h,["Joseph was sold into slavery by his brothers for twenty pieces of silver.",!0,"Joseph's brothers sold him to Midianite merchants for twenty shekels of silver.","Genesis 37:28","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aLO=new A.c(B.h,["Joseph interpreted Pharaoh's dream about seven fat cows and seven thin cows.",!0,"Joseph interpreted the dream as seven years of abundance followed by seven years of famine.","Genesis 41:25-30","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aP9=new A.c(B.h,["Benjamin was Joseph's older brother.",!1,"Benjamin was Joseph's younger brother. They shared the same mother, Rachel.","Genesis 35:24","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aPu=new A.c(B.h,["Moses was found in a basket on the Nile River by Pharaoh's daughter.",!0,"Moses' mother placed him in a papyrus basket among the reeds of the Nile, where Pharaoh's daughter found him.","Exodus 2:5-6","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aQO=new A.c(B.h,["God appeared to Moses in a burning tree.",!1,"God appeared to Moses in a burning bush, not a tree, on Mount Horeb.","Exodus 3:2","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aN7=new A.c(B.h,["There were ten plagues sent upon Egypt.",!0,"God sent ten plagues on Egypt to convince Pharaoh to release the Israelites from slavery.","Exodus 7-12","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aPm=new A.c(B.h,["The last plague of Egypt was a plague of darkness.",!1,"The last plague was the death of the firstborn. Darkness was the ninth plague.","Exodus 12:29","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aKw=new A.c(B.h,["Moses parted the Red Sea by striking it with his staff.",!1,"God instructed Moses to stretch out his hand over the sea; the Lord drove the sea back with a strong east wind.","Exodus 14:21","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aMk=new A.c(B.h,["The Israelites received manna from heaven while wandering in the wilderness.",!0,"God provided manna, a bread-like substance, daily for the Israelites during their wilderness journey.","Exodus 16:14-15","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aKb=new A.c(B.h,["The Ten Commandments were given on Mount Sinai.",!0,"God gave Moses the Ten Commandments on Mount Sinai, written on two stone tablets.","Exodus 20:1-17","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aL0=new A.c(B.h,["Aaron made a golden calf while Moses was on Mount Sinai.",!0,"While Moses was receiving the law, the people pressured Aaron into making a golden calf idol.","Exodus 32:2-4","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aOv=new A.c(B.h,['The first commandment is "You shall not steal."',!1,'The first commandment is "You shall have no other gods before me." "You shall not steal" is the eighth commandment.',"Exodus 20:3","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aQC=new A.c(B.h,["The Israelites wandered in the wilderness for 40 years.",!0,"Due to their disobedience and lack of faith, the Israelites wandered in the wilderness for 40 years.","Numbers 14:33-34","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aPD=new A.c(B.h,["Moses was allowed to enter the Promised Land.",!1,"Moses was not permitted to enter the Promised Land because he struck the rock at Meribah instead of speaking to it as God commanded.","Deuteronomy 34:4-5","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aLX=new A.c(B.h,["The Book of Leviticus contains laws about sacrifices and priestly duties.",!0,"Leviticus details laws regarding sacrifices, clean and unclean foods, and priestly responsibilities.","Leviticus 1:1-2","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aKv=new A.c(B.h,["Balaam's donkey spoke to him.",!0,"God opened the mouth of Balaam's donkey, which spoke to Balaam when it saw the angel of the Lord blocking the path.","Numbers 22:28","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aPb=new A.c(B.h,["The twelve spies all gave a positive report about the Promised Land.",!1,"Only Joshua and Caleb gave a positive report. The other ten spies gave a fearful, negative report.","Numbers 13:30-33","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aO5=new A.c(B.h,["Joshua led the Israelites across the Jordan River into the Promised Land.",!0,"After Moses died, Joshua was chosen by God to lead the Israelites into the Promised Land.","Joshua 3:14-17","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aP8=new A.c(B.h,["The walls of Jericho fell after the Israelites marched around them for three days.",!1,"The Israelites marched around Jericho for seven days. On the seventh day they marched seven times, then the walls fell.","Joshua 6:15-16, 20","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aKa=new A.c(B.h,["Rahab hid the Israelite spies on the roof of her house.",!0,"Rahab hid the two spies under stalks of flax on her roof to protect them from the king of Jericho.","Joshua 2:6","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aNi=new A.c(B.h,["Samson's strength came from his long hair.",!1,"Samson's strength came from God. His uncut hair was a sign of his Nazirite vow, not the source of his power.","Judges 16:17, 28","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aQE=new A.c(B.h,["Deborah was a judge and prophetess in Israel.",!0,"Deborah served as both a judge and a prophetess, leading Israel to victory over the Canaanites.","Judges 4:4","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aJC=new A.c(B.h,["Gideon defeated the Midianites with an army of 300 men.",!0,"God reduced Gideon's army from 32,000 to 300 men so that Israel would know the victory came from God.","Judges 7:7","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aLj=new A.c(B.h,["Ruth was from the land of Moab.",!0,"Ruth was a Moabite woman who chose to follow her mother-in-law Naomi back to Bethlehem.","Ruth 1:4, 16","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aP5=new A.c(B.h,["Ruth married Elimelech after returning to Bethlehem.",!1,"Ruth married Boaz, not Elimelech. Elimelech was Naomi's deceased husband.","Ruth 4:13","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aM8=new A.c(B.h,["Samuel was dedicated to God's service by his mother Hannah.",!0,"Hannah prayed for a son and promised to dedicate him to the Lord. She brought Samuel to the temple as a young boy.","1 Samuel 1:27-28","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aJA=new A.c(B.h,["Saul was the first king of Israel.",!0,"Saul, from the tribe of Benjamin, was anointed by Samuel as the first king of Israel.","1 Samuel 10:1","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aLE=new A.c(B.h,["David killed Goliath with a sword.",!1,"David killed Goliath with a stone from his sling. He then used Goliath's own sword to cut off his head.","1 Samuel 17:49-51","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aRM=new A.c(B.h,["David was the youngest of Jesse's sons.",!0,"David was the youngest of Jesse's eight sons and was tending sheep when Samuel came to anoint him.","1 Samuel 16:11","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aOl=new A.c(B.h,["Jonathan was David's enemy.",!1,"Jonathan, Saul's son, was David's closest friend. They made a covenant of friendship together.","1 Samuel 18:3","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aQl=new A.c(B.h,["David committed adultery with Bathsheba.",!0,"King David committed adultery with Bathsheba and arranged for her husband Uriah to be killed in battle.","2 Samuel 11:2-17","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aNe=new A.c(B.h,["Absalom was David's son who led a rebellion against him.",!0,"Absalom conspired against his father David and temporarily seized the throne of Israel.","2 Samuel 15:10-12","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aRa=new A.c(B.h,["Goliath was from the city of Jerusalem.",!1,"Goliath was from Gath, one of the five main cities of the Philistines.","1 Samuel 17:4","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aRd=new A.c(B.h,["Solomon asked God for wisdom.",!0,"When God offered Solomon anything he wanted, Solomon asked for wisdom to govern the people, which pleased God.","1 Kings 3:9-10","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aKR=new A.c(B.h,["Solomon built the first temple in Jerusalem.",!0,"Solomon built the first permanent temple for the Lord in Jerusalem, fulfilling his father David's desire.","1 Kings 6:1","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aR6=new A.c(B.h,["After Solomon's death, Israel was divided into two kingdoms.",!0,"Israel split into the northern kingdom (Israel) and the southern kingdom (Judah) after Solomon's death.","1 Kings 12:16-20","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aMt=new A.c(B.h,["Elijah was fed by eagles during a famine.",!1,"Elijah was fed by ravens, not eagles, who brought him bread and meat at the Kerith Ravine.","1 Kings 17:4-6","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aKP=new A.c(B.h,["Elijah challenged 450 prophets of Baal on Mount Carmel.",!0,"Elijah challenged 450 prophets of Baal to a contest on Mount Carmel, and God sent fire from heaven.","1 Kings 18:19-38","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aKO=new A.c(B.h,["Elijah was taken up to heaven in a chariot of fire.",!0,"Elijah was taken up to heaven by a whirlwind, with a chariot of fire and horses of fire appearing.","2 Kings 2:11","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aJQ=new A.c(B.h,["Elisha asked for a double portion of Elijah's spirit.",!0,"Before Elijah was taken up, Elisha asked for a double portion of his spirit, which was granted.","2 Kings 2:9","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aKD=new A.c(B.h,["Naaman was healed of leprosy by washing in the Jordan River five times.",!1,"Naaman was told to wash in the Jordan River seven times, not five, to be cleansed of his leprosy.","2 Kings 5:10, 14","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aOj=new A.c(B.h,["Hezekiah was a wicked king of Judah.",!1,"Hezekiah was one of the most righteous kings of Judah. He removed the high places and restored temple worship.","2 Kings 18:3-5","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aNm=new A.c(B.h,["Josiah became king of Judah at the age of eight.",!0,"Josiah became king when he was eight years old and reigned for thirty-one years in Jerusalem.","2 Kings 22:1","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aMo=new A.c(B.h,["Nehemiah rebuilt the walls of Jerusalem.",!0,"Nehemiah led the effort to rebuild the walls of Jerusalem after the Babylonian exile.","Nehemiah 2:17-18","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aPU=new A.c(B.h,["The walls of Jerusalem were rebuilt in 52 days under Nehemiah.",!0,"Despite opposition, the wall was completed in just 52 days through the dedication of the people.","Nehemiah 6:15","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aOY=new A.c(B.h,["Queen Esther was a Philistine woman.",!1,"Esther was a Jewish woman. She kept her Jewish identity hidden when she became queen of Persia.","Esther 2:7, 10","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aKV=new A.c(B.h,["Haman plotted to destroy all the Jews in the Persian Empire.",!0,"Haman devised a plan to annihilate all Jews throughout the Persian Empire because Mordecai would not bow to him.","Esther 3:5-6","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aNQ=new A.c(B.h,["The name of God is mentioned frequently in the book of Esther.",!1,"The book of Esther is notable for not explicitly mentioning God's name, though His providence is evident throughout.","Esther 1-10","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aPw=new A.c(B.h,["Job was a wealthy man from the land of Uz.",!0,"Job was described as the greatest man among all the people of the East, living in the land of Uz.","Job 1:1-3","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aQj=new A.c(B.h,["Job cursed God during his suffering.",!1,'Despite immense suffering, Job did not curse God. He said, "The Lord gave and the Lord has taken away; blessed be the name of the Lord."',"Job 1:21-22","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aPx=new A.c(B.h,["Job had three friends who came to comfort him.",!0,"Job's three friends were Eliphaz, Bildad, and Zophar, who came to sympathize with him.","Job 2:11","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aPk=new A.c(B.h,["The book of Psalms has 150 chapters.",!0,"The book of Psalms contains 150 individual psalms, making it the longest book in the Bible.","Psalm 1-150","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aOf=new A.c(B.h,["King David wrote all 150 Psalms.",!1,"While David wrote many psalms, other authors include Asaph, the sons of Korah, Solomon, and Moses.","Psalm 90:1 (Moses), Psalm 72:1 (Solomon)","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aOz=new A.c(B.h,['Psalm 23 begins with "The Lord is my shepherd."',!0,"Psalm 23, written by David, opens with the famous line about God being a shepherd to His people.","Psalm 23:1","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aME=new A.c(B.h,["Psalm 119 is the longest chapter in the Bible.",!0,"Psalm 119 has 176 verses, making it the longest chapter in the entire Bible.","Psalm 119","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aRw=new A.c(B.h,["The book of Proverbs was written entirely by King Solomon.",!1,"While Solomon wrote much of Proverbs, it also includes sayings from Agur, King Lemuel, and other wise men.","Proverbs 30:1, 31:1","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aNZ=new A.c(B.h,['Ecclesiastes says "There is nothing new under the sun."',!0,"The Teacher in Ecclesiastes declares that all things are wearisome and there is nothing truly new.","Ecclesiastes 1:9","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aOZ=new A.c(B.h,["The Song of Solomon is a love poem.",!0,"The Song of Solomon is a poetic celebration of love between a bride and bridegroom.","Song of Solomon 1:1-2","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aK5=new A.c(B.h,["The shortest chapter in the Bible is Psalm 117.",!0,"Psalm 117 has only two verses, making it the shortest chapter in the Bible.","Psalm 117:1-2","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aQ5=new A.c(B.h,["Isaiah prophesied that the Messiah would be born of a virgin.",!0,"Isaiah prophesied that a virgin would conceive and bear a son called Immanuel.","Isaiah 7:14","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aQp=new A.c(B.h,['Jeremiah is known as the "weeping prophet."',!0,"Jeremiah is often called the weeping prophet because of his deep sorrow over Judah's sin and coming judgment.","Jeremiah 9:1","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aPW=new A.c(B.h,["Ezekiel saw a vision of a valley of dry bones that came to life.",!0,"God showed Ezekiel a valley of dry bones and breathed life into them, symbolizing the restoration of Israel.","Ezekiel 37:1-10","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aQd=new A.c(B.h,["Daniel was thrown into a den of bears.",!1,"Daniel was thrown into a den of lions, not bears, for praying to God instead of King Darius.","Daniel 6:16","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aNt=new A.c(B.h,["Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego were thrown into a fiery furnace.",!0,"These three men were thrown into a fiery furnace for refusing to worship King Nebuchadnezzar's golden image.","Daniel 3:19-23","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aNd=new A.c(B.h,["Daniel interpreted the writing on the wall for King Nebuchadnezzar.",!1,"Daniel interpreted the writing on the wall for King Belshazzar, not Nebuchadnezzar.","Daniel 5:25-28","Prophets"],t.R)
