B.aNq=new A.c(B.h,["The New Testament was originally written in Greek.",!0,"The New Testament books were written in Koine Greek, the common language of the Roman Empire.","Matthew - Revelation","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aMg=new A.c(B.h,["There are 27 books in the New Testament.",!0,"The New Testament contains 27 books, from Matthew through Revelation.","Matthew - Revelation","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aMv=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus healed a man who had been blind from birth.",!0,"Jesus spat on the ground, made mud, and put it on the blind man's eyes, then told him to wash in the Pool of Siloam.","John 9:1-7","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aON=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus turned stones into bread during His temptation.",!1,"Satan tempted Jesus to turn stones into bread, but Jesus refused, quoting Scripture.","Matthew 4:3-4","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aMO=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus healed Peter's mother-in-law of a fever.",!0,"Jesus touched Peter's mother-in-law's hand, and the fever left her. She got up and began to serve them.","Matthew 8:14-15","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aPj=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus fed 4,000 people on a separate occasion from the feeding of the 5,000.",!0,"Jesus performed two separate feeding miracles: one feeding 5,000 and another feeding 4,000.","Matthew 15:32-38","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aQe=new A.c(B.h,["Elisha parted the Jordan River using Elijah's cloak.",!0,"After Elijah was taken up, Elisha struck the Jordan with Elijah's cloak and the water divided.","2 Kings 2:14","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aOW=new A.c(B.h,["Moses turned the Nile River into blood as the first plague.",!0,"The first plague upon Egypt was turning the water of the Nile into blood.","Exodus 7:20","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aQg=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus said the greatest commandment is to love your neighbor as yourself.",!1,"Jesus said the greatest commandment is to love the Lord your God with all your heart, soul, and mind. Loving your neighbor is the second.","Matthew 22:37-39","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aQP=new A.c(B.h,['The Golden Rule states: "Do unto others as you would have them do unto you."',!0,"Jesus taught this principle as a summary of how to treat others.","Matthew 7:12","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aLA=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus said it is easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle than for a rich man to enter heaven.",!0,"Jesus used this vivid imagery to illustrate how difficult it is for the wealthy to enter the kingdom of God.","Matthew 19:24","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aN5=new A.c(B.h,["The Lord's Prayer is found in the book of Acts.",!1,"The Lord's Prayer is found in the Gospels of Matthew and Luke, not in Acts.","Matthew 6:9-13","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aJO=new A.c(B.h,['The Beatitudes begin with "Blessed are the poor in spirit."',!0,"The first Beatitude states that the poor in spirit are blessed, for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.","Matthew 5:3","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aLa=new A.c(B.h,["Paul listed faith, hope, and love as the three greatest virtues.",!0,"Paul wrote that faith, hope, and love remain, but the greatest of these is love.","1 Corinthians 13:13","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aP_=new A.c(B.h,["Ruth was the great-grandmother of King David.",!0,"Ruth married Boaz, they had Obed, who fathered Jesse, who fathered David.","Ruth 4:21-22","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aO0=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus was descended from the tribe of Judah.",!0,"Jesus' genealogy traces through the tribe of Judah, fulfilling the prophecy that the scepter would not depart from Judah.","Matthew 1:2-3, Hebrews 7:14","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aRj=new A.c(B.h,["Abraham had only one son.",!1,"Abraham had at least two sons: Ishmael through Hagar and Isaac through Sarah.","Genesis 16:15, 21:2-3","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aMq=new A.c(B.h,["Isaac was the father of Jacob and Esau.",!0,"Isaac and Rebekah had twin sons: Esau (the firstborn) and Jacob.","Genesis 25:24-26","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aOR=new A.c(B.h,["Rachel was Jacob's first wife.",!1,"Leah was Jacob's first wife. Laban tricked Jacob into marrying Leah before Rachel.","Genesis 29:23-25","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aMb=new A.c(B.h,["Isaiah prophesied more than 700 years before Christ's birth.",!0,"Isaiah ministered around 740-681 BC, making his messianic prophecies about 700+ years before Jesus' birth.","Isaiah 1:1","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aL7=new A.c(B.h,["The prophet Joel spoke about the outpouring of the Holy Spirit.",!0,"Joel prophesied that God would pour out His Spirit on all people, which Peter quoted at Pentecost.","Joel 2:28-29","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aP2=new A.c(B.h,["Nahum prophesied against the city of Babylon.",!1,"Nahum prophesied against Nineveh, the capital of Assyria, not Babylon.","Nahum 1:1","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aQJ=new A.c(B.h,["Daniel interpreted King Nebuchadnezzar's dream about a great statue.",!0,"Daniel interpreted Nebuchadnezzar's dream of a statue made of different metals, representing successive kingdoms.","Daniel 2:31-45","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aNA=new A.c(B.h,["The Ark of the Covenant contained the Ten Commandments, Aaron's staff, and a jar of manna.",!0,"The Ark held the stone tablets of the covenant, Aaron's rod that budded, and a golden jar of manna.","Hebrews 9:4","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aRR=new A.c(B.h,["The walls of Jericho fell because the Israelites used battering rams.",!1,"The walls fell after the Israelites marched around the city and blew their trumpets as God commanded.","Joshua 6:20","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aNz=new A.c(B.h,["David played the harp to soothe King Saul.",!0,"When a tormenting spirit came upon Saul, David would play the harp and Saul would feel better.","1 Samuel 16:23","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aOV=new A.c(B.h,["The book of Lamentations was written by Jeremiah.",!0,"Lamentations is traditionally attributed to Jeremiah, mourning the destruction of Jerusalem.","Lamentations 1:1","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aO4=new A.c(B.h,["Cain was cursed to wander the earth after killing Abel.",!0,"God cursed Cain to be a restless wanderer on the earth as punishment for murdering his brother Abel.","Genesis 4:12","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aOm=new A.c(B.h,["Sarah was 90 years old when she gave birth to Isaac.",!0,"Sarah was 90 years old and Abraham was 100 when their son Isaac was born, as God had promised.","Genesis 17:17, 21:5","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aKW=new A.c(B.h,["The Bible mentions dinosaurs by name.",!1,'The word "dinosaur" does not appear in the Bible, though some interpret descriptions of creatures like behemoth and leviathan as large animals.',"Job 40:15-24","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aKQ=new A.c(B.h,["Paul was bitten by a snake on the island of Malta and survived.",!0,"A viper fastened onto Paul's hand, but he shook it off and suffered no harm, astonishing the islanders.","Acts 28:3-5","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aLN=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus turned five stone jars of water into wine at the wedding in Cana.",!1,"There were six stone water jars, not five, that Jesus had filled with water and turned into wine.","John 2:6","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aQc=new A.c(B.h,["The parable of the talents is about musical ability.",!1,"A talent was a unit of money. The parable is about stewardship and using what God has entrusted to us.","Matthew 25:14-30","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aLv=new A.c(B.h,["Herod the Great ordered the massacre of infants in Bethlehem.",!0,"Herod ordered the killing of all male children two years old and under in Bethlehem to eliminate the newborn king.","Matthew 2:16","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aL9=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus had brothers named James, Joseph, Simon, and Judas.",!0,"The Gospels record that Jesus had brothers named James, Joseph, Simon, and Judas.","Matthew 13:55","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aNy=new A.c(B.h,["The book of James was written by James the brother of John.",!1,"The book of James is traditionally attributed to James the brother of Jesus, not James the son of Zebedee.","James 1:1","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aOk=new A.c(B.h,["Lydia was a seller of purple cloth and one of the first European converts.",!0,"Lydia, a dealer in purple cloth from the city of Thyatira, was baptized by Paul in Philippi.","Acts 16:14-15","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aQz=new A.c(B.h,["Priscilla and Aquila were tentmakers like Paul.",!0,"Paul stayed and worked with Priscilla and Aquila because they shared the same trade of tentmaking.","Acts 18:2-3","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aQF=new A.c(B.h,["The Israelites crossed the Red Sea on dry ground.",!0,"God parted the waters so the Israelites could cross the Red Sea on dry ground with walls of water on both sides.","Exodus 14:22","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aRp=new A.c(B.h,["Moses received the Ten Commandments on Mount Nebo.",!1,"Moses received the Ten Commandments on Mount Sinai. Mount Nebo is where Moses viewed the Promised Land before his death.","Exodus 19:20, Deuteronomy 34:1","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aLV=new A.c(B.h,["Enoch never died but was taken by God.",!0,"Enoch walked faithfully with God and then was no more, because God took him. He did not experience death.","Genesis 5:24","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aMz=new A.c(B.h,["The first five books of the Bible are called the Pentateuch.",!0,"The Pentateuch, also called the Torah, consists of Genesis, Exodus, Leviticus, Numbers, and Deuteronomy.","Genesis - Deuteronomy","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aMW=new A.c(B.h,["The apostle John wrote five books of the New Testament.",!0,"John wrote the Gospel of John, 1 John, 2 John, 3 John, and Revelation.","John, 1-3 John, Revelation","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aJw=new A.c(B.h,["Paul wrote the book of Hebrews.",!1,"The authorship of Hebrews is unknown and debated. While Paul was once suggested, the style differs significantly from his other letters.","Hebrews 1:1","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aPG=new A.c(B.h,['The shortest verse in the Bible is "Jesus wept."',!0,'John 11:35, "Jesus wept," is the shortest verse in the Bible in the English translation.',"John 11:35","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aMN=new A.c(B.h,["Noah was 500 years old when the flood came.",!1,"Noah was 600 years old when the flood waters came upon the earth.","Genesis 7:6","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aR8=new A.c(B.h,["The plague of frogs was the second plague upon Egypt.",!0,"After the water was turned to blood (first plague), God sent a plague of frogs as the second plague.","Exodus 8:2-6","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aQX=new A.c(B.h,["King Ahab was married to Jezebel.",!0,"Ahab married Jezebel, a Phoenician princess who promoted Baal worship in Israel.","1 Kings 16:31","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aPi=new A.c(B.h,["The valley of the shadow of death is mentioned in Psalm 22.",!1,"The valley of the shadow of death is mentioned in Psalm 23, the Shepherd Psalm, not Psalm 22.","Psalm 23:4","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aQK=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus performed His first miracle at a funeral.",!1,"Jesus' first miracle was at a wedding in Cana, where He turned water into wine.","John 2:1-11","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aN0=new A.c(B.h,["The parable of the sower is found in all three Synoptic Gospels.",!0,"The parable of the sower is recorded in Matthew 13, Mark 4, and Luke 8.","Matthew 13:3-23, Mark 4:3-20, Luke 8:5-15","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aQq=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus raised a widow's son from the dead in the town of Nain.",!0,"Jesus touched the coffin and told the young man to get up, and he came back to life in the town of Nain.","Luke 7:11-15","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aMr=new A.c(B.h,["The Holy Spirit appeared as a flame over Jesus' head at His baptism.",!1,"The Holy Spirit descended on Jesus in the form of a dove at His baptism, not as a flame.","Matthew 3:16","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aKc=new A.c(B.h,["Paul was stoned and left for dead in the city of Lystra.",!0,"Jews from Antioch and Iconium persuaded the crowd to stone Paul. They dragged him outside the city, thinking he was dead.","Acts 14:19","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aJD=new A.c(B.h,["The Bible says money is the root of all evil.",!1,'The verse actually says "the love of money" is the root of all kinds of evil, not money itself.',"1 Timothy 6:10","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aMY=new A.c(B.h,["Lot lived in the city of Sodom.",!0,"Lot chose to live near and eventually in Sodom, despite its wickedness.","Genesis 13:12, 19:1","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aOi=new A.c(B.h,["Jacob wrestled with an angel and was renamed Israel.",!0,'Jacob wrestled with a divine being all night and received the name Israel, meaning "he struggles with God."',"Genesis 32:28","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aQ_=new A.c(B.h,["The tabernacle was a permanent stone structure.",!1,"The tabernacle was a portable tent structure that the Israelites carried through the wilderness.","Exodus 26:1","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aLc=new A.c(B.h,["King Nebuchadnezzar of Babylon destroyed the first temple in Jerusalem.",!0,"Nebuchadnezzar's forces destroyed Solomon's temple in 586 BC when they conquered Jerusalem.","2 Kings 25:8-9","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aQZ=new A.c(B.h,["Ezra was a priest and scribe who led a group of exiles back to Jerusalem.",!0,"Ezra was a priest and teacher of the Law who led a second group of Jewish exiles from Babylon back to Jerusalem.","Ezra 7:6","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aMl=new A.c(B.h,["The prophet Elijah raised a widow's son from the dead.",!0,"Elijah prayed over the widow of Zarephath's dead son, and God restored the boy to life.","1 Kings 17:21-22","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aLT=new A.c(B.h,["Zephaniah prophesied during the reign of King Solomon.",!1,"Zephaniah prophesied during the reign of King Josiah of Judah, not Solomon.","Zephaniah 1:1","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aRy=new A.c(B.h,["Haggai encouraged the rebuilding of the temple after the Babylonian exile.",!0,"Haggai urged the returned exiles to prioritize rebuilding the temple in Jerusalem.","Haggai 1:8","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aRK=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus told the parable of the ten virgins.",!0,"Jesus told of ten virgins waiting for the bridegroom; five were wise with oil and five were foolish without.","Matthew 25:1-13","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aPg=new A.c(B.h,["Simon of Cyrene carried Jesus' cross.",!0,"The soldiers forced Simon of Cyrene to carry the cross for Jesus on the way to Golgotha.","Matthew 27:32","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aKT=new A.c(B.h,["Barabbas was released instead of Jesus.",!0,"The crowd chose to release the prisoner Barabbas instead of Jesus when Pilate offered the choice.","Matthew 27:26","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aRq=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus appeared to two disciples on the road to Emmaus after His resurrection.",!0,"The risen Jesus walked and talked with two disciples on the road to Emmaus, though they did not recognize Him at first.","Luke 24:13-31","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aOE=new A.c(B.h,["Matthias was chosen to replace Judas as one of the twelve apostles.",!0,"After Judas' death, the apostles cast lots and Matthias was chosen to replace him among the twelve.","Acts 1:26","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aKg=new A.c(B.h,["The day of Pentecost occurred ten days after Jesus' ascension.",!0,"Jesus ascended 40 days after His resurrection, and Pentecost came 50 days after the resurrection (10 days after the ascension).","Acts 1:3, 2:1","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aJT=new A.c(B.h,["Peter raised Dorcas (Tabitha) from the dead.",!0,'Peter prayed and said "Tabitha, get up," and she opened her eyes and sat up, restored to life.',"Acts 9:40-41","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aRb=new A.c(B.h,["The island of Cyprus was visited by Paul on his first missionary journey.",!0,"Paul and Barnabas sailed to Cyprus at the start of their first missionary journey and preached across the island.","Acts 13:4","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aOI=new A.c(B.h,["God created light on the first day of creation.",!0,'On the first day, God said "Let there be light," and there was light. He separated light from darkness.',"Genesis 1:3-5","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aNK=new A.c(B.h,["Man was created on the fifth day of creation.",!1,"Man was created on the sixth day of creation. On the fifth day, God created sea creatures and birds.","Genesis 1:26-27","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aJP=new A.c(B.h,["Adam named all the animals in the Garden of Eden.",!0,"God brought all the animals to Adam to see what he would name them, and whatever Adam called each creature, that was its name.","Genesis 2:19-20","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aLK=new A.c(B.h,["The forbidden fruit in the Garden of Eden is identified as an apple in the Bible.",!1,"The Bible never specifies what kind of fruit it was. It simply says the fruit of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil.","Genesis 3:6","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aNU=new A.c(B.h,["Seth was born to Adam and Eve after Abel was killed.",!0,"After Cain killed Abel, Eve gave birth to Seth, saying God had granted her another child in place of Abel.","Genesis 4:25","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aOn=new A.c(B.h,["Enoch was the father of Methuselah.",!0,"Enoch fathered Methuselah when he was 65 years old, and Methuselah went on to become the longest-lived person in the Bible.","Genesis 5:21","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aN1=new A.c(B.h,["The flood lasted for forty days and forty nights of rain only.",!1,"While it rained for forty days and forty nights, the floodwaters remained on the earth for 150 days before receding.","Genesis 7:12, 7:24","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aKx=new A.c(B.h,["Noah sent out a raven before sending a dove from the ark.",!0,"Noah first sent out a raven which flew back and forth. Then he sent out a dove to see if the waters had receded.","Genesis 8:7-8","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aNR=new A.c(B.h,["Abraham was born in the city of Ur of the Chaldeans.",!0,"Abraham (Abram) originally came from Ur of the Chaldeans before God called him to go to a new land.","Genesis 11:31","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aLi=new A.c(B.h,["Abraham and Lot were brothers.",!1,"Lot was Abraham's nephew, not his brother. Lot was the son of Haran, Abraham's brother.","Genesis 12:5","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aPZ=new A.c(B.h,["God made a covenant with Abraham involving the cutting of animals in half.",!0,"God instructed Abraham to bring a heifer, goat, ram, dove, and pigeon. The animals were cut in half, and a smoking firepot passed between the pieces.","Genesis 15:9-17","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aKp=new A.c(B.h,["Ishmael was the son of Abraham and Sarah.",!1,"Ishmael was the son of Abraham and Hagar, Sarah's Egyptian servant. Isaac was the son of Abraham and Sarah.","Genesis 16:15","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aQU=new A.c(B.h,["Circumcision was the sign of God's covenant with Abraham.",!0,"God commanded Abraham and all males in his household to be circumcised as a sign of the covenant between them.","Genesis 17:10-11","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aP3=new A.c(B.h,["Rebekah was chosen as a wife for Isaac at a well.",!0,"Abraham's servant prayed at a well and Rebekah appeared, fulfilling the sign he had asked God for.","Genesis 24:15-20","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aLq=new A.c(B.h,["Jacob deceived his father Isaac by wearing goat skins on his arms.",!0,"Rebekah helped Jacob put goat skins on his hands and neck so blind Isaac would think he was the hairy Esau.","Genesis 27:16","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aQG=new A.c(B.h,["Jacob dreamed of a ladder reaching to heaven while fleeing to Egypt.",!1,"Jacob dreamed of the ladder at Bethel while fleeing to Haran (to his uncle Laban), not to Egypt.","Genesis 28:12-13","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aKk=new A.c(B.h,["Jacob worked seven years to marry Rachel but was given Leah instead.",!0,"Laban tricked Jacob by giving him Leah on the wedding night. Jacob then worked another seven years for Rachel.","Genesis 29:20-27","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aMd=new A.c(B.h,["Joseph's coat of many colors was given to him by his mother.",!1,"The richly ornamented robe was given to Joseph by his father Jacob, which made his brothers jealous.","Genesis 37:3","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aKU=new A.c(B.h,["Joseph was falsely accused by Potiphar's wife and thrown into prison.",!0,"Potiphar's wife tried to seduce Joseph, and when he refused, she falsely accused him, leading to his imprisonment.","Genesis 39:7-20","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aPE=new A.c(B.h,["Joseph interpreted dreams for Pharaoh's butler and baker while in prison.",!0,"Joseph correctly interpreted the dreams of the cupbearer (butler) and the baker while all three were in prison.","Genesis 40:8-22","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aKh=new A.c(B.h,["Moses killed an Egyptian who was beating a Hebrew slave.",!0,"Moses saw an Egyptian beating a Hebrew and, after looking around, struck and killed the Egyptian and hid him in the sand.","Exodus 2:11-12","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aQ2=new A.c(B.h,["Moses fled to Midian after killing the Egyptian.",!0,"When Pharaoh heard about it and tried to kill Moses, Moses fled to the land of Midian.","Exodus 2:15","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aRN=new A.c(B.h,['God told Moses His name was "I AM WHO I AM."',!0,'When Moses asked God His name, God replied "I AM WHO I AM," revealing His eternal self-existence.',"Exodus 3:14","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aPJ=new A.c(B.h,["Moses' staff turned into a snake as a sign from God.",!0,"God told Moses to throw his staff on the ground, and it became a snake. When Moses picked it up, it became a staff again.","Exodus 4:2-4","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aQR=new A.c(B.h,["The plague of locusts was the third plague upon Egypt.",!1,"Locusts were the eighth plague. The third plague was gnats (or lice).","Exodus 10:12-15","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aM1=new A.c(B.h,["The Passover lamb's blood was placed on the doorposts to protect the Israelites.",!0,"God instructed the Israelites to put lamb's blood on their doorposts so the destroyer would pass over their homes.","Exodus 12:7, 12-13","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aLU=new A.c(B.h,["The Israelites ate unleavened bread during the first Passover because they had time to let the dough rise.",!1,"The bread was unleavened because they left Egypt in such haste that the dough did not have time to rise.","Exodus 12:39","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aKS=new A.c(B.h,["Pharaoh's army was drowned in the Red Sea.",!0,"When Pharaoh's army pursued the Israelites into the parted sea, God caused the waters to return and drown the entire army.","Exodus 14:27-28","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aQb=new A.c(B.h,["God provided quail for the Israelites to eat in the wilderness.",!0,"When the Israelites complained about having no meat, God sent quail in the evening and manna in the morning.","Exodus 16:12-13","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aLp=new A.c(B.h,["Moses struck a rock at Horeb and water came out.",!0,"At Horeb, God told Moses to strike the rock with his staff, and water came out for the people to drink.","Exodus 17:6","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aNB=new A.c(B.h,["The golden calf was made from Egyptian gold that the Israelites had stolen.",!1,"The golden calf was made from gold earrings the Israelites contributed. The gold was given to them by the Egyptians when they left Egypt.","Exodus 32:2-4, 12:35-36","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aJY=new A.c(B.h,["Moses' face shone after speaking with God on Mount Sinai.",!0,"After speaking with God, Moses' face was radiant. He wore a veil over his face because the Israelites were afraid to come near him.","Exodus 34:29-30","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aNP=new A.c(B.h,["The Day of Atonement (Yom Kippur) is described in the book of Leviticus.",!0,"Leviticus 16 details the Day of Atonement, when the high priest made atonement for the sins of all Israel.","Leviticus 16:29-34","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aMX=new A.c(B.h,["The scapegoat was sacrificed on the altar on the Day of Atonement.",!1,"The scapegoat was not sacrificed. The sins of the people were symbolically placed on it, and it was sent into the wilderness.","Leviticus 16:21-22","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aRF=new A.c(B.h,["The Year of Jubilee occurred every fifty years in Israel.",!0,"Every fiftieth year was a Jubilee, when slaves were freed, debts forgiven, and land returned to its original owners.","Leviticus 25:10-11","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aLe=new A.c(B.h,["Korah led a rebellion against Moses and was swallowed by the earth.",!0,"Korah and his followers rebelled against Moses and Aaron. The ground opened up and swallowed them alive.","Numbers 16:31-33","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aM6=new A.c(B.h,["Moses was forbidden from entering the Promised Land because he worshiped the golden calf.",!1,"Moses was forbidden because he struck the rock at Meribah instead of speaking to it as God commanded, failing to honor God before the people.","Numbers 20:11-12","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aM5=new A.c(B.h,["God sent fiery serpents among the Israelites as punishment for their complaining.",!0,"When the Israelites spoke against God and Moses, God sent venomous snakes that bit the people. Moses made a bronze serpent for healing.","Numbers 21:6-9","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aKy=new A.c(B.h,["The Levites received a portion of the Promised Land like the other tribes.",!1,"The tribe of Levi did not receive a land inheritance. They were given cities to live in and were supported by tithes.","Numbers 18:20-24","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aMS=new A.c(B.h,["Moses recited the law to the Israelites before they entered the Promised Land.",!0,"The book of Deuteronomy records Moses' final speeches, restating the law for the new generation before they entered Canaan.","Deuteronomy 1:1-5","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aQr=new A.c(B.h,['The Shema, "Hear, O Israel: The Lord our God, the Lord is one," is found in Deuteronomy.',!0,"The Shema is a central declaration of faith in Judaism found in Deuteronomy, commanding Israel to love God with all their heart, soul, and strength.","Deuteronomy 6:4-5","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aRB=new A.c(B.h,["Moses died on Mount Sinai.",!1,"Moses died on Mount Nebo, where God showed him the Promised Land. Mount Sinai is where he received the Ten Commandments.","Deuteronomy 34:1-5","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aR4=new A.c(B.h,["The Jordan River stopped flowing when the priests carrying the Ark stepped into it.",!0,"When the priests' feet touched the water, the Jordan stopped flowing and the Israelites crossed on dry ground.","Joshua 3:15-17","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aPs=new A.c(B.h,["Joshua set up twelve stones at Gilgal to commemorate crossing the Jordan.",!0,"Twelve stones were taken from the Jordan riverbed and set up at Gilgal as a memorial for future generations.","Joshua 4:20-24","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aQI=new A.c(B.h,["Achan was punished for hiding plunder from the battle of Jericho.",!0,"Achan took devoted items from Jericho against God's command, causing Israel's defeat at Ai. He and his family were stoned.","Joshua 7:20-25","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aOF=new A.c(B.h,["Joshua commanded the sun to stand still during a battle against the Amorites.",!0,"Joshua prayed, and the sun stood still over Gibeon and the moon over the Valley of Aijalon for about a full day.","Joshua 10:12-13","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aKm=new A.c(B.h,["The Gibeonites deceived Joshua into making a peace treaty with them.",!0,"The Gibeonites dressed in worn-out clothes and carried stale bread, pretending they had traveled from far away to trick Joshua into a treaty.","Joshua 9:3-15","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aPK=new A.c(B.h,["Ehud was a left-handed judge who assassinated King Eglon of Moab.",!0,"Ehud, a left-handed Benjamite, hid a double-edged sword on his right thigh and used it to kill the obese King Eglon.","Judges 3:15-22","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aR2=new A.c(B.h,["Jael killed the Canaanite general Sisera by driving a tent peg through his temple.",!0,"After Sisera fled from battle and took refuge in Jael's tent, she drove a tent peg through his temple while he slept.","Judges 4:21","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aMR=new A.c(B.h,["Gideon tested God by putting out a fleece twice.",!0,"Gideon asked God for two signs using a wool fleece: first that only the fleece would be wet, then that only the ground would be wet.","Judges 6:36-40","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aKC=new A.c(B.h,["Gideon's 300 men defeated the Midianites using swords and shields.",!1,"They used trumpets, empty jars, and torches. They blew the trumpets, broke the jars, and the Midianites fled in confusion.","Judges 7:16-22","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aRE=new A.c(B.h,["Jephthah made a rash vow that affected his daughter.",!0,"Jephthah vowed to sacrifice whatever came out of his house first if God gave him victory. His daughter came out first.","Judges 11:30-35","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aMs=new A.c(B.h,["Samson killed a thousand men with the jawbone of a horse.",!1,"Samson killed a thousand Philistines with the jawbone of a donkey, not a horse.","Judges 15:15-16","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aR1=new A.c(B.h,["Samson destroyed the Philistine temple by pushing apart the two central pillars.",!0,"Blinded and imprisoned, Samson pushed the two central pillars apart, collapsing the temple on himself and thousands of Philistines.","Judges 16:29-30","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aJy=new A.c(B.h,["Naomi told Ruth and Orpah to return to their mothers' houses after their husbands died.",!0,"After the deaths of her sons, Naomi urged both daughters-in-law to return to Moab. Orpah left, but Ruth stayed.","Ruth 1:8-14","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aO_=new A.c(B.h,["Boaz allowed Ruth to glean in his fields.",!0,"Boaz showed kindness to Ruth and instructed his workers to let her glean freely and even leave extra grain for her.","Ruth 2:8-9, 15-16","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aKK=new A.c(B.h,["Hannah prayed for a son at the tabernacle in Shiloh.",!0,"Hannah wept and prayed silently at the tabernacle in Shiloh, asking God for a son and vowing to dedicate him to the Lord.","1 Samuel 1:9-11","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aN9=new A.c(B.h,["Eli the priest initially thought Hannah was drunk when she was praying.",!0,"Hannah was praying silently, moving her lips but making no sound. Eli saw this and accused her of being drunk.","1 Samuel 1:13-14","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aQi=new A.c(B.h,["The Ark of the Covenant was captured by the Babylonians during Samuel's time.",!1,"The Ark was captured by the Philistines, not the Babylonians. It caused plagues among the Philistines until they returned it.","1 Samuel 4:11, 5:1-6","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aMy=new A.c(B.h,["Saul was chosen as king partly because he was taller than anyone else in Israel.",!0,"Saul was described as an impressive young man, standing a head taller than anyone else among the Israelites.","1 Samuel 9:2","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aNV=new A.c(B.h,["Saul disobeyed God by sparing King Agag and the best livestock of the Amalekites.",!0,"God commanded Saul to destroy everything, but Saul spared Agag and the best animals. Samuel rebuked him saying obedience is better than sacrifice.","1 Samuel 15:8-9, 22","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aMn=new A.c(B.h,["David was anointed king by the prophet Nathan.",!1,"David was first anointed king by the prophet Samuel, not Nathan. Nathan was a prophet during David's reign.","1 Samuel 16:13","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aKr=new A.c(B.h,["Goliath's height was about six cubits and a span, roughly nine feet tall.",!0,"Goliath is described as six cubits and a span tall, which is approximately nine feet (over 2.7 meters).","1 Samuel 17:4","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aNb=new A.c(B.h,["David spared Saul's life twice when he had the opportunity to kill him.",!0,"David spared Saul in a cave at En Gedi and again in Saul's camp, cutting his robe and taking his spear and water jug.","1 Samuel 24:4-7, 26:7-12","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aQ8=new A.c(B.h,["Jonathan warned David of Saul's plans to kill him by shooting arrows.",!0,"Jonathan devised a plan using arrows as a signal to warn David whether it was safe or he needed to flee from Saul.","1 Samuel 20:18-22, 35-42","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aRe=new A.c(B.h,["Saul and his sons died in battle against the Egyptians.",!1,"Saul and his sons, including Jonathan, died in battle against the Philistines on Mount Gilboa.","1 Samuel 31:1-6","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aPt=new A.c(B.h,["David danced before the Lord when the Ark of the Covenant was brought to Jerusalem.",!0,"David danced before the Lord with all his might as the Ark was brought into Jerusalem with shouts and trumpet blasts.","2 Samuel 6:14-15","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aP4=new A.c(B.h,["Nathan the prophet confronted David about his sin with Bathsheba using a parable.",!0,'Nathan told David a story about a rich man who stole a poor man\'s lamb. When David was outraged, Nathan said "You are the man."',"2 Samuel 12:1-7","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aJx=new A.c(B.h,["Solomon settled a dispute between two women claiming to be the mother of a baby by threatening to cut the child in half.",!0,"Solomon proposed dividing the child with a sword. The real mother begged him to give the baby to the other woman, revealing the truth.","1 Kings 3:24-27","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aO8=new A.c(B.h,["Solomon's temple took twenty years to build.",!1,"Solomon's temple took seven years to build, not twenty. His own palace took thirteen years.","1 Kings 6:38, 7:1","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aNu=new A.c(B.h,["The Queen of Sheba visited Solomon to test him with hard questions.",!0,"The Queen of Sheba traveled to Jerusalem to test Solomon's wisdom with difficult questions and was overwhelmed by all she saw.","1 Kings 10:1-3","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aL_=new A.c(B.h,["Jeroboam set up golden calves at Dan and Bethel after the kingdom split.",!0,"To prevent the northern tribes from worshiping in Jerusalem, Jeroboam made two golden calves and placed them at Dan and Bethel.","1 Kings 12:28-29","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aNG=new A.c(B.h,["Elijah was fed by a widow of Zarephath whose jar of flour and jug of oil never ran out.",!0,"During the famine, God miraculously sustained Elijah and the widow: her jar of flour was not used up and her jug of oil did not run dry.","1 Kings 17:14-16","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aQY=new A.c(B.h,["Elijah fled to Mount Sinai after Jezebel threatened to kill him.",!0,"After Jezebel threatened his life, Elijah fled to Horeb (Mount Sinai), where God spoke to him in a gentle whisper.","1 Kings 19:3-12","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aNo=new A.c(B.h,["God spoke to Elijah in a mighty earthquake at Mount Horeb.",!1,"God was not in the wind, earthquake, or fire, but spoke to Elijah in a still, small voice (a gentle whisper).","1 Kings 19:11-12","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aPN=new A.c(B.h,["Naboth was killed so that Ahab could take his vineyard.",!0,"Jezebel arranged false witnesses to accuse Naboth of blasphemy. He was stoned to death, and Ahab took his vineyard.","1 Kings 21:13-16","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aJV=new A.c(B.h,["Elisha healed the poisoned stew at Gilgal by adding flour to the pot.",!0,"When deadly gourds were mistakenly added to a pot of stew, Elisha threw flour into the pot and made it safe to eat.","2 Kings 4:38-41","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aMU=new A.c(B.h,["Elisha raised the Shunammite woman's son from the dead.",!0,"Elisha prayed and lay upon the dead child, and the boy sneezed seven times and opened his eyes.","2 Kings 4:32-35","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aQD=new A.c(B.h,["Elisha made an axe head float on water.",!0,"When a borrowed axe head fell into the Jordan, Elisha threw a stick into the water and the iron axe head floated to the surface.","2 Kings 6:5-6","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aL3=new A.c(B.h,["Jehu was anointed king of Israel and destroyed the house of Ahab.",!0,"Jehu was anointed by a prophet at Elisha's command and carried out God's judgment against the house of Ahab and Jezebel.","2 Kings 9:6-10","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aLm=new A.c(B.h,["Jezebel was thrown from a window and eaten by dogs.",!0,"Jezebel was thrown from a window by her own servants at Jehu's command, and dogs ate her body, fulfilling Elijah's prophecy.","2 Kings 9:33-36","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aJF=new A.c(B.h,["Hezekiah's life was extended by fifteen years after he prayed to God.",!0,"When Hezekiah was told he would die, he prayed and wept. God heard him and added fifteen years to his life.","2 Kings 20:1-6","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aKq=new A.c(B.h,["The Book of the Law was found in the temple during King Josiah's reign.",!0,"During temple repairs, Hilkiah the priest found the Book of the Law, leading Josiah to institute sweeping religious reforms.","2 Kings 22:8-11","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aQf=new A.c(B.h,["The northern kingdom of Israel was conquered by the Babylonians.",!1,"The northern kingdom of Israel was conquered by the Assyrians in 722 BC. The southern kingdom of Judah was later conquered by the Babylonians.","2 Kings 17:6","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aNl=new A.c(B.h,["David organized the Levites into divisions for temple service.",!0,"David organized the Levites, priests, musicians, and gatekeepers into divisions for service in the temple Solomon would build.","1 Chronicles 23:1-6","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aMB=new A.c(B.h,["Cyrus king of Persia allowed the Jews to return to Jerusalem and rebuild the temple.",!0,"In his first year, Cyrus issued a decree allowing the Jewish exiles to return to Jerusalem and rebuild the temple of God.","Ezra 1:1-3","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aMG=new A.c(B.h,["Zerubbabel led the first group of exiles back to Jerusalem.",!0,"Zerubbabel, a descendant of David, led the first group of about 42,360 Jewish exiles back to Jerusalem.","Ezra 2:1-2, 64","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aMm=new A.c(B.h,["The rebuilt second temple was grander than Solomon's original temple.",!1,"Many of the older people who had seen Solomon's temple wept when they saw the foundation of the new one, because it did not compare.","Ezra 3:12","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aJJ=new A.c(B.h,["Nehemiah was a cupbearer to the Persian king before going to Jerusalem.",!0,"Nehemiah served as cupbearer to King Artaxerxes of Persia, a trusted position, before requesting permission to rebuild Jerusalem's walls.","Nehemiah 1:11, 2:1","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aKi=new A.c(B.h,["Sanballat and Tobiah opposed Nehemiah's efforts to rebuild the walls.",!0,"Sanballat the Horonite and Tobiah the Ammonite mocked and plotted against Nehemiah's wall-building project.","Nehemiah 2:19, 4:1-3","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aOp=new A.c(B.h,["Ezra read the Book of the Law to all the people at the Water Gate.",!0,"Ezra stood on a high wooden platform and read the Law of Moses to the assembled people from early morning until midday.","Nehemiah 8:1-3","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aOJ=new A.c(B.h,["Esther was raised by her uncle Mordecai.",!0,"After her parents died, Esther was brought up by her cousin Mordecai, who had adopted her as his own daughter.","Esther 2:7","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aOg=new A.c(B.h,["Esther became queen after Queen Vashti was removed for disobedience.",!0,"Queen Vashti refused to appear before King Ahasuerus at his banquet, and Esther was chosen as her replacement.","Esther 1:12, 2:17","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aLh=new A.c(B.h,["Mordecai saved the king's life by uncovering an assassination plot.",!0,"Mordecai learned of a plot by two of the king's officers to assassinate King Ahasuerus and reported it through Esther.","Esther 2:21-23","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aJv=new A.c(B.h,["The Jewish festival of Purim celebrates the events described in the book of Esther.",!0,"Purim was established to celebrate the Jews' deliverance from Haman's plot, named after the \"pur\" (lot) Haman cast.","Esther 9:26-28","Old Testament"],t.R)
B.aJU=new A.c(B.h,["Job lost all his children in a single day.",!0,"A great wind struck the house where all of Job's sons and daughters were feasting, and they all perished.","Job 1:18-19","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aRJ=new A.c(B.h,["Job's wife told him to curse God and die.",!0,'When Job was afflicted with painful sores, his wife said to him, "Are you still maintaining your integrity? Curse God and die!"',"Job 2:9","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aOc=new A.c(B.h,["God answered Job from a burning bush.",!1,"God answered Job out of a storm (whirlwind), not a burning bush. The burning bush was how God appeared to Moses.","Job 38:1","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aNw=new A.c(B.h,["God restored Job's fortunes and gave him twice as much as he had before.",!0,"After Job prayed for his friends, God restored his prosperity and gave him twice what he originally possessed.","Job 42:10","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aJI=new A.c(B.h,["Elihu was the youngest of Job's friends and the last to speak.",!0,"Elihu waited to speak because he was younger. After the three friends fell silent, Elihu addressed Job in chapters 32-37.","Job 32:4-6","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aLH=new A.c(B.h,["Psalm 1 describes the blessed man as being like a tree planted by streams of water.",!0,"The righteous person is compared to a tree planted by streams of water, which yields fruit in season and whose leaf does not wither.","Psalm 1:3","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aLd=new A.c(B.h,["Psalm 51 was written by David after his sin with Bathsheba.",!0,"The superscription of Psalm 51 states it was written when Nathan the prophet came to David after his adultery with Bathsheba.","Psalm 51:1 (superscription)","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aNx=new A.c(B.h,['Psalm 22 opens with the words "The Lord is my shepherd."',!1,'Psalm 22 opens with "My God, my God, why have you forsaken me?" It is Psalm 23 that begins with "The Lord is my shepherd."',"Psalm 22:1","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aMI=new A.c(B.h,["Psalm 139 says God knit us together in our mother's womb.",!0,"David praised God saying He created his inmost being and knit him together in his mother's womb.","Psalm 139:13","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aOH=new A.c(B.h,["Psalm 90 is attributed to Moses.",!0,'Psalm 90 is titled "A prayer of Moses the man of God," making it the only psalm attributed to Moses.',"Psalm 90:1 (superscription)","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aOL=new A.c(B.h,["Proverbs 31 describes the virtuous woman.",!0,"Proverbs 31:10-31 is an acrostic poem describing a wife of noble character who is worth far more than rubies.","Proverbs 31:10-31","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aMM=new A.c(B.h,["The book of Proverbs teaches that the fear of the Lord is the beginning of knowledge.",!0,"Proverbs opens with the principle that reverence for God is the foundation and starting point of all true knowledge.","Proverbs 1:7","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aKJ=new A.c(B.h,["Ecclesiastes was written by King David.",!1,'Ecclesiastes is traditionally attributed to Solomon, who identifies himself as "the Teacher, son of David, king in Jerusalem."',"Ecclesiastes 1:1","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aJu=new A.c(B.h,["Ecclesiastes teaches that there is a time for everything under heaven.",!0,"The famous passage declares there is a season for everything: a time to be born and a time to die, a time to plant and a time to uproot.","Ecclesiastes 3:1-8","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aRk=new A.c(B.h,['The Song of Solomon is addressed to a bride called "the Rose of Sharon."',!1,"The bride calls herself the Rose of Sharon, but the book is a dialogue between the bride, the bridegroom, and the daughters of Jerusalem.","Song of Solomon 2:1","Wisdom"],t.R)
B.aND=new A.c(B.h,["Isaiah saw the Lord seated on a high throne with seraphim above Him.",!0,'In his calling vision, Isaiah saw the Lord on a throne, high and exalted, with six-winged seraphim above Him calling "Holy, holy, holy."',"Isaiah 6:1-3","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aRC=new A.c(B.h,["Isaiah's lips were cleansed with a burning coal from the altar.",!0,"A seraphim took a live coal from the altar with tongs and touched Isaiah's lips, purifying him from sin.","Isaiah 6:6-7","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aQo=new A.c(B.h,["Isaiah prophesied that a child would be called Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace.",!0,"Isaiah foretold that a child would be born to reign on David's throne, bearing these four messianic titles.","Isaiah 9:6","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aK7=new A.c(B.h,["Jeremiah was told by God not to marry or have children.",!0,"God commanded Jeremiah not to take a wife or have children in that place, as a sign of the coming destruction.","Jeremiah 16:1-2","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aQa=new A.c(B.h,["Jeremiah was thrown into a cistern filled with water.",!1,"Jeremiah was lowered into a cistern that had no water in it, only mud. He sank into the mud at the bottom.","Jeremiah 38:6","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aRL=new A.c(B.h,["Jeremiah prophesied that the Babylonian exile would last seventy years.",!0,"Jeremiah declared that the people would serve the king of Babylon for seventy years before God would bring them back.","Jeremiah 29:10","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aO2=new A.c(B.h,["The book of Lamentations contains five poems mourning the destruction of Jerusalem.",!0,"Lamentations has five chapters, each a separate poem lamenting the fall of Jerusalem and the suffering of its people.","Lamentations 1-5","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aMJ=new A.c(B.h,["Ezekiel was a prophet who ministered in Jerusalem throughout his career.",!1,"Ezekiel prophesied while in exile in Babylon by the Kebar River, not in Jerusalem.","Ezekiel 1:1-3","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aO3=new A.c(B.h,["Ezekiel was commanded by God to lie on his side for 390 days.",!0,"God told Ezekiel to lie on his left side for 390 days to bear the sin of Israel, and then on his right side for 40 days for Judah.","Ezekiel 4:4-6","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aMQ=new A.c(B.h,["Ezekiel saw a vision of a wheel within a wheel.",!0,"In his opening vision, Ezekiel described seeing wheels beside the living creatures, with a wheel intersecting a wheel.","Ezekiel 1:15-16","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aPX=new A.c(B.h,["Daniel and his friends refused to eat the king's food and asked for vegetables and water.",!0,"Daniel resolved not to defile himself with the royal food and wine. He and his friends ate only vegetables and drank water.","Daniel 1:8, 12","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aPL=new A.c(B.h,["King Nebuchadnezzar lived like a wild animal for seven years as God's punishment.",!0,"Because of his pride, Nebuchadnezzar was driven from people and lived like a wild animal, eating grass for seven periods of time.","Daniel 4:32-33","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aOG=new A.c(B.h,["Daniel was thrown into the lions' den for worshiping a golden statue.",!1,"Daniel was thrown into the lions' den for continuing to pray to God in defiance of a decree forbidding prayer to anyone except King Darius.","Daniel 6:7-16","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aOT=new A.c(B.h,["A fourth figure appeared in the fiery furnace with Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego.",!0,"Nebuchadnezzar saw four men walking in the fire unbound and unharmed. He said the fourth looked like a son of the gods.","Daniel 3:25","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aN4=new A.c(B.h,["Hosea's wife Gomer was unfaithful to him.",!0,"Gomer was unfaithful and returned to her former ways, but God commanded Hosea to love her again, picturing God's love for Israel.","Hosea 3:1","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aK1=new A.c(B.h,["Joel described a devastating plague of locusts as God's judgment.",!0,"Joel used a locust plague as a picture of God's coming judgment, calling the people to repentance.","Joel 1:4-7","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aPe=new A.c(B.h,["Amos was a professional prophet trained in the schools of the prophets.",!1,"Amos was not a prophet by profession. He was a shepherd and tender of sycamore-fig trees whom God called to prophesy.","Amos 7:14","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aK0=new A.c(B.h,["Obadiah prophesied against the nation of Edom.",!0,"The entire book of Obadiah is a prophecy against Edom (the descendants of Esau) for their hostility toward Israel.","Obadiah 1:1","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aMH=new A.c(B.h,["Jonah was sent to preach to the city of Babylon.",!1,"Jonah was sent to preach to Nineveh, the capital of Assyria, not Babylon.","Jonah 1:2","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aPd=new A.c(B.h,["The people of Nineveh repented after hearing Jonah's message.",!0,"From the king to the least of the people, Nineveh believed God, proclaimed a fast, and turned from their evil ways.","Jonah 3:5-8","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aNf=new A.c(B.h,["Nahum prophesied the destruction of Nineveh.",!0,"Nahum prophesied the complete destruction of Nineveh, the Assyrian capital, which fell in 612 BC.","Nahum 1:1, 3:7","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aPn=new A.c(B.h,["Habakkuk concluded his book by saying he would rejoice in the Lord even when the fig tree does not bud.",!0,"Despite hardship, Habakkuk declared he would rejoice in God his Savior even if crops failed and flocks perished.","Habakkuk 3:17-18","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aKe=new A.c(B.h,["Zephaniah prophesied during the reign of King Hezekiah.",!1,"Zephaniah prophesied during the reign of King Josiah, not Hezekiah.","Zephaniah 1:1","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aJB=new A.c(B.h,["Zechariah saw a vision of a flying scroll.",!0,"Zechariah saw a vision of a flying scroll that was thirty feet long and fifteen feet wide, representing a curse going out over the land.","Zechariah 5:1-2","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aOd=new A.c(B.h,["Malachi rebuked the priests for offering blind and lame animals as sacrifices.",!0,"Malachi condemned the priests for dishonoring God by offering defective animals that they would not dare offer to a human governor.","Malachi 1:8","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aKz=new A.c(B.h,["Malachi prophesied that Elijah would come before the great day of the Lord.",!0,"Malachi ends with God's promise to send the prophet Elijah before the coming of the great and dreadful day of the Lord.","Malachi 4:5","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aPh=new A.c(B.h,["The prophet Micah said God requires only three things: to act justly, love mercy, and walk humbly with God.",!0,"Micah declared what the Lord requires: to act justly, to love mercy, and to walk humbly with your God.","Micah 6:8","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aLy=new A.c(B.h,["Haggai prophesied before the Babylonian exile began.",!1,"Haggai prophesied after the exile, encouraging the returned exiles to rebuild the temple.","Haggai 1:1-2","Prophets"],t.R)
B.aNn=new A.c(B.h,["The genealogy in Matthew traces Jesus' lineage back to Abraham.",!0,"Matthew's Gospel begins with a genealogy tracing Jesus' ancestry from Abraham through David to Joseph.","Matthew 1:1-17","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aJE=new A.c(B.h,["The wise men followed a comet to find baby Jesus.",!1,"The Bible says the wise men followed a star, not a comet.","Matthew 2:2","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aNr=new A.c(B.h,['Jesus said "Blessed are the meek, for they shall inherit the earth" in the Sermon on the Mount.',!0,"This is one of the Beatitudes that Jesus taught in the Sermon on the Mount.","Matthew 5:5","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aPB=new A.c(B.h,["In the Sermon on the Mount, Jesus taught that anger against a brother is as serious as murder.",!0,"Jesus said anyone who is angry with a brother or sister will be subject to judgment, equating it with the seriousness of murder.","Matthew 5:21-22","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aQ6=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus taught His disciples to pray in public so that everyone would see their devotion.",!1,"Jesus taught the opposite: to pray in secret, and the Father who sees in secret will reward you.","Matthew 6:5-6","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aM2=new A.c(B.h,['Jesus said "Do not worry about tomorrow, for tomorrow will worry about itself."',!0,"This teaching about not worrying is part of the Sermon on the Mount.","Matthew 6:34","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aPI=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus compared a wise builder to one who builds his house on sand.",!1,"The wise builder builds on the rock; the foolish builder builds on sand.","Matthew 7:24-27","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aK9=new A.c(B.h,["A Roman centurion came to Jesus asking for his daughter to be healed, and Jesus marveled at his faith.",!1,"The centurion asked Jesus to heal his servant, not his daughter. Jesus marveled at the centurion's great faith.","Matthew 8:5-13","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aOw=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus told the parable of the wheat and the tares to describe the end of the world.",!1,"Jesus told the parable to describe the kingdom of heaven, not the end of the world specifically, though it does include teaching about the final harvest.","Matthew 13:24-30","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aRV=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus said the kingdom of heaven is like a mustard seed, the largest of all seeds.",!1,"Jesus said the mustard seed is the smallest of all seeds, yet it grows into the largest of garden plants.","Matthew 13:31-32","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aMp=new A.c(B.h,["John the Baptist was beheaded at the request of Herodias' daughter.",!0,"Herodias' daughter pleased Herod with her dancing, and at her mother's prompting she asked for John the Baptist's head on a platter.","Matthew 14:6-11","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aOr=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus said that if you have faith the size of an olive, you can move mountains.",!1,"Jesus said faith the size of a mustard seed, not an olive, can move mountains.","Matthew 17:20","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aQ1=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus told Peter to forgive his brother seven times.",!1,"Peter suggested seven times, but Jesus replied seventy-seven times (or seventy times seven), meaning forgiveness should be unlimited.","Matthew 18:21-22","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aLJ=new A.c(B.h,["In the parable of the unmerciful servant, the servant owed his master ten thousand talents.",!0,"The servant owed an enormous debt of ten thousand talents, yet after being forgiven refused to forgive a fellow servant who owed him a small amount.","Matthew 18:23-35","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aL5=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus cursed a fig tree because it bore rotten fruit.",!1,"Jesus cursed the fig tree because it had no fruit at all, only leaves.","Matthew 21:18-19","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aR5=new A.c(B.h,["In the parable of the wedding banquet, the king invited people from the streets after the original guests refused.",!0,"When those originally invited refused to come, the king sent servants to invite anyone they could find on the streets.","Matthew 22:1-14","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aNW=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus said to render unto Caesar the things that are God's.",!1,"Jesus said \"Render unto Caesar the things that are Caesar's, and unto God the things that are God's,\" distinguishing between the two.","Matthew 22:21","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aPP=new A.c(B.h,["In the parable of the sheep and goats, the sheep are placed on the left and the goats on the right.",!1,"It is the opposite: the sheep are on the right and the goats on the left.","Matthew 25:31-33","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aKu=new A.c(B.h,["At the Last Supper, Jesus instituted the practice of communion with bread and wine.",!0,"Jesus broke bread and shared the cup with His disciples, saying the bread was His body and the wine His blood of the new covenant.","Matthew 26:26-28","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aJH=new A.c(B.h,["The Great Commission commands believers to make disciples of all nations.",!0,"Jesus told His disciples to go and make disciples of all nations, baptizing them and teaching them to obey His commands.","Matthew 28:19-20","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aMA=new A.c(B.h,["The Gospel of Mark begins with the birth narrative of Jesus.",!1,"Mark's Gospel has no birth narrative. It begins with John the Baptist's ministry and Jesus' baptism.","Mark 1:1-11","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aOD=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus healed a paralyzed man who was lowered through the roof by his friends.",!0,"Four men could not get their paralyzed friend to Jesus through the crowd, so they dug through the roof and lowered him down.","Mark 2:1-12","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aM3=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus cast a legion of demons out of a man, and the demons entered a herd of sheep.",!1,"The demons entered a herd of pigs (swine), not sheep. The pigs then rushed down a steep bank into the sea and drowned.","Mark 5:1-13","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aPc=new A.c(B.h,["A woman who had been bleeding for twelve years was healed by touching Jesus' cloak.",!0,"The woman touched the edge of Jesus' garment and was immediately healed of her condition.","Mark 5:25-34","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aRI=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus sent out the twelve disciples in groups of four to preach and heal.",!1,"Jesus sent them out two by two, not in groups of four.","Mark 6:7","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aQB=new A.c(B.h,["On the Mount of Transfiguration, Jesus appeared with Moses and Abraham.",!1,"Jesus appeared with Moses and Elijah, not Abraham, on the Mount of Transfiguration.","Mark 9:2-4","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aML=new A.c(B.h,['Jesus said "Let the little children come to me, and do not hinder them."',!0,"When the disciples tried to keep children away, Jesus rebuked them and welcomed the children.","Mark 10:14","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aN8=new A.c(B.h,["Blind Bartimaeus called out to Jesus as He entered Jerusalem and was healed.",!1,"Bartimaeus called out to Jesus as He was leaving Jericho, not entering Jerusalem.","Mark 10:46-52","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aRr=new A.c(B.h,["Luke addressed his Gospel to a man named Theophilus.",!0,"Luke wrote his Gospel as an orderly account for Theophilus so that he might know the certainty of the things he had been taught.","Luke 1:1-4","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aLY=new A.c(B.h,["Zechariah was struck blind because he doubted the angel Gabriel's message.",!1,"Zechariah was struck mute (unable to speak), not blind, because he doubted the angel's message about the birth of John.","Luke 1:18-20","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aRs=new A.c(B.h,["Mary visited her relative Elizabeth, who was pregnant with John the Baptist.",!0,"When Mary greeted Elizabeth, the baby (John) leaped in Elizabeth's womb, and Elizabeth was filled with the Holy Spirit.","Luke 1:39-45","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aK_=new A.c(B.h,["Simeon recognized the infant Jesus as the Messiah when He was presented at the temple.",!0,"Simeon had been promised by the Holy Spirit that he would not die before seeing the Lord's Christ. He recognized Jesus when Mary and Joseph brought Him to the temple.","Luke 2:25-35","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aJK=new A.c(B.h,["As a twelve-year-old, Jesus was found by His parents teaching in the marketplace.",!1,"Jesus was found in the temple, sitting among the teachers, listening and asking questions.","Luke 2:41-49","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aL6=new A.c(B.h,["In the parable of the lost sheep, the shepherd leaves fifty sheep to find the one that is lost.",!1,"The shepherd leaves ninety-nine sheep, not fifty, to go after the one that is lost.","Luke 15:3-7","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aQS=new A.c(B.h,["The parable of the rich man and Lazarus teaches that Lazarus went to a place of torment after death.",!1,"It was the rich man who went to a place of torment. Lazarus was carried by angels to Abraham's side.","Luke 16:19-31","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aKL=new A.c(B.h,["Jesus healed the ear of the high priest's servant that Peter had cut off.",!0,"When Peter struck the servant of the high priest and cut off his right ear, Jesus touched the ear and healed it.","Luke 22:50-51","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aR9=new A.c(B.h,['On the cross, Jesus said to the repentant thief "Today you will be with me in paradise."',!0,"One of the criminals crucified with Jesus repented, and Jesus promised him paradise that very day.","Luke 23:42-43","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aMi=new A.c(B.h,['Jesus said "Father, forgive them, for they know not what they do" while in the Garden of Gethsemane.',!1,"Jesus spoke these words while on the cross, not in the Garden of Gethsemane.","Luke 23:34","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aLZ=new A.c(B.h,['The Gospel of John identifies the "beloved disciple" by name as John.',!1,"The Gospel never names the beloved disciple directly; tradition identifies him as John, but the text itself does not.","John 21:20-24","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aNp=new A.c(B.h,['Jesus said "I am the bread of life" after feeding the five thousand.',!0,"After the feeding of the five thousand, Jesus declared Himself the bread of life, saying whoever comes to Him will never go hungry.","John 6:35","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aKs=new A.c(B.h,['Jesus said "I am the light of the world" in the Gospel of Luke.',!1,'Jesus declared "I am the light of the world" in the Gospel of John, not Luke.',"John 8:12","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aPa=new A.c(B.h,['Jesus said "I am the resurrection and the life" to Mary Magdalene.',!1,"Jesus said this to Martha, the sister of Lazarus, not to Mary Magdalene.","John 11:25-26","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aKf=new A.c(B.h,['Jesus said "I am the true vine, and my Father is the gardener."',!0,"Jesus used the vine metaphor to teach that believers must remain connected to Him to bear fruit.","John 15:1","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aOP=new A.c(B.h,["When Jesus was arrested, Peter drew a sword and cut off the ear of a soldier named Marcus.",!1,"The servant's name was Malchus, not Marcus, and he was a servant of the high priest, not a soldier.","John 18:10","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aNh=new A.c(B.h,['Jesus told Peter to "Feed my sheep" three times after the resurrection.',!0,"Jesus asked Peter three times if he loved Him and each time told him to feed or tend His sheep, restoring Peter after his three denials.","John 21:15-17","Gospels"],t.R)
B.aOq=new A.c(B.h,["At Pentecost, the Holy Spirit appeared as tongues of fire that rested on each disciple.",!0,"Tongues of fire separated and rested on each of the believers gathered in the upper room.","Acts 2:3","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aP0=new A.c(B.h,["Peter healed a lame man at the Golden Gate of the temple.",!1,"Peter healed the lame man at the Beautiful Gate, not the Golden Gate.","Acts 3:1-8","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aPV=new A.c(B.h,["Gamaliel was a Pharisee who advised the Sanhedrin to leave the apostles alone.",!0,"Gamaliel, a respected teacher of the law, warned the council that if the apostles' work was from God, they could not stop it.","Acts 5:34-39","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aLk=new A.c(B.h,["Stephen saw a vision of Jesus sitting at the right hand of God before being stoned.",!1,"Stephen saw Jesus standing at the right hand of God, not sitting. This is the only place in the New Testament where Jesus is described as standing.","Acts 7:55-56","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aQ3=new A.c(B.h,["Saul was blinded for seven days after his encounter with Jesus on the road to Damascus.",!1,"Saul was blind for three days, not seven, until Ananias came and laid hands on him.","Acts 9:9","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aNs=new A.c(B.h,["Cornelius, a Roman centurion, was the first recorded Gentile convert in Acts.",!0,"God sent Peter to Cornelius' household, where the Holy Spirit fell on the Gentiles, confirming that salvation was for all people.","Acts 10:1-48","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aQx=new A.c(B.h,["King Herod Agrippa I was struck down by an angel because he persecuted the apostles.",!1,"Herod was struck down specifically because he accepted worship as a god and did not give praise to the true God.","Acts 12:21-23","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aQk=new A.c(B.h,["An angel freed Peter from prison by breaking down the prison walls.",!1,"The angel caused Peter's chains to fall off and led him past the guards through the iron gate, which opened by itself.","Acts 12:6-10","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aPl=new A.c(B.h,["At the Council of Jerusalem, it was decided that Gentile believers must be circumcised.",!1,"The council decided that Gentile believers did not need to be circumcised, but should abstain from food polluted by idols, from sexual immorality, from the meat of strangled animals, and from blood.","Acts 15:19-20","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aNa=new A.c(B.h,["Paul and Barnabas had a sharp disagreement over John Mark and parted company.",!0,"Barnabas wanted to take John Mark on their second journey, but Paul disagreed because Mark had deserted them earlier. They split up.","Acts 15:36-41","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aLr=new A.c(B.h,["Paul received a vision of a man from Macedonia asking for help.",!0,"In a night vision, Paul saw a man of Macedonia standing and begging him to come and help them, which led Paul into Europe.","Acts 16:9-10","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aOC=new A.c(B.h,["The Bereans were criticized for questioning Paul's teaching instead of accepting it immediately.",!1,"The Bereans were actually praised as more noble because they examined the Scriptures daily to verify what Paul taught.","Acts 17:10-11","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aNJ=new A.c(B.h,['Paul preached about the "unknown god" at the Colosseum in Rome.',!1,"Paul preached about the unknown god at the Areopagus (Mars Hill) in Athens, not in Rome.","Acts 17:22-23","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aNL=new A.c(B.h,["A young man named Eutychus fell from a third-story window during Paul's sermon and died, but Paul raised him back to life.",!0,"Eutychus fell asleep during Paul's lengthy sermon and fell from the window. Paul went down and embraced him, and the young man was restored to life.","Acts 20:7-12","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aPy=new A.c(B.h,["Paul appealed to Caesar, which resulted in his journey to Rome.",!0,"As a Roman citizen, Paul exercised his right to appeal to Caesar, which led to his voyage to Rome.","Acts 25:11-12","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aLw=new A.c(B.h,["Paul was shipwrecked on his way to Rome and landed on the island of Cyprus.",!1,"Paul was shipwrecked on the island of Malta, not Cyprus.","Acts 28:1","Acts & Letters"],t.R)
B.aRh=new A.c(B.h,['Paul wrote in Romans that "all have sinned and fall short of the glory of God."',!0,"This is one of the key verses in Paul's letter to the Romans, establishing that all people are sinners in need of God's grace.","Romans 3:23","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aJR=new A.c(B.h,['Paul wrote that "the wages of sin is death, but the gift of God is eternal life."',!0,"This verse contrasts the consequence of sin with the free gift God offers through Jesus Christ.","Romans 6:23","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aOS=new A.c(B.h,["Romans 8:28 says that all things work together for good for those who love money.",!1,"The verse says all things work together for good for those who love God and are called according to His purpose.","Romans 8:28","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aLL=new A.c(B.h,["Paul taught in Romans that believers should be conformed to the pattern of this world.",!1,"Paul urged believers not to conform to the pattern of this world but to be transformed by the renewing of their minds.","Romans 12:2","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aQT=new A.c(B.h,["Paul wrote 1 Corinthians to address divisions and moral issues in the church at Corinth.",!0,"The letter addresses factions, immorality, lawsuits among believers, marriage questions, and other issues in the Corinthian church.","1 Corinthians 1:10-11","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aKn=new A.c(B.h,["In 1 Corinthians 12, Paul compares the church to a building.",!1,"In 1 Corinthians 12, Paul compares the church to a body with many members, each having different gifts and functions.","1 Corinthians 12:12-27","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aLP=new A.c(B.h,["Paul wrote that the greatest of faith, hope, and love is love.",!0,"In the famous love chapter, Paul declares that the greatest of these three enduring virtues is love.","1 Corinthians 13:13","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aKo=new A.c(B.h,["Paul said that even if Christ has not been raised, the Christian faith still has value.",!1,"Paul argued the opposite: if Christ has not been raised, faith is futile and believers are to be pitied above all people.","1 Corinthians 15:14","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aQV=new A.c(B.h,["Paul wrote that God loves a reluctant giver.",!1,"Paul wrote that God loves a cheerful giver, not a reluctant one.","2 Corinthians 9:7","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aMT=new A.c(B.h,['Paul described a "thorn in the flesh" that God refused to remove despite his prayers.',!0,'Paul asked the Lord three times to remove it, but God replied "My grace is sufficient for you, for my power is made perfect in weakness."',"2 Corinthians 12:7-9","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aKd=new A.c(B.h,["Paul said that anyone who is in Christ is a new creation.",!0,'Paul wrote "If anyone is in Christ, the new creation has come: The old has gone, the new is here."',"2 Corinthians 5:17","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aQA=new A.c(B.h,["Paul rebuked Peter publicly in Antioch for withdrawing from Gentile believers.",!0,"Paul opposed Peter to his face because Peter had been eating with Gentiles but withdrew when certain men came from James.","Galatians 2:11-14","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aOo=new A.c(B.h,["The fruit of the Spirit listed in Galatians includes ten attributes.",!1,u.ix,"Galatians 5:22-23","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aM4=new A.c(B.h,["Paul wrote to the Galatians that a person is justified by faith in Christ, not by works of the law.",!0,"A central theme of Galatians is that justification comes through faith in Jesus Christ and not by observing the law.","Galatians 2:16","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aKA=new A.c(B.h,["Paul wrote that believers are saved by grace through faith, not by works.",!0,"This foundational teaching states that salvation is a gift of God, not earned by human effort.","Ephesians 2:8-9","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aOU=new A.c(B.h,["The armor of God described in Ephesians includes the sword of the Spirit, which is the Word of God.",!0,"Paul lists the full armor of God and identifies the sword of the Spirit as the Word of God.","Ephesians 6:17","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aJM=new A.c(B.h,["The armor of God in Ephesians includes a helmet of righteousness.",!1,"The helmet is the helmet of salvation, not righteousness. The breastplate is of righteousness.","Ephesians 6:14-17","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aLR=new A.c(B.h,["Paul described the church as the body of Christ with Christ as the head.",!0,"Paul taught that Christ is the head of the church, which is His body, and that all believers are members of it.","Ephesians 1:22-23","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aQm=new A.c(B.h,["Paul wrote the letter to the Philippians while he was on a missionary journey.",!1,'Paul wrote Philippians while in prison, making it one of his "prison epistles."',"Philippians 1:12-14","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aQu=new A.c(B.h,['Paul wrote "To live is Christ and to die is loss."',!1,'Paul wrote "To live is Christ and to die is gain," not loss, expressing that death would bring him into Christ\'s presence.',"Philippians 1:21","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aPo=new A.c(B.h,['The Christ hymn in Philippians says Jesus "made himself nothing" by taking the nature of a servant.',!0,"Paul describes how Christ, being in the form of God, emptied Himself and took the form of a servant, being made in human likeness.","Philippians 2:6-7","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aKX=new A.c(B.h,["Paul wrote in Colossians that Jesus is the image of the invisible God and the firstborn over all creation.",!0,"This passage affirms Christ's supremacy and His role in creation, stating that all things were created through Him and for Him.","Colossians 1:15-16","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aQ0=new A.c(B.h,["Paul wrote Colossians primarily to address conflicts between Jewish and Gentile believers.",!1,"Paul wrote Colossians primarily to warn against false teachings including the worship of angels, legalistic practices, and human philosophy.","Colossians 2:8-23","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aMD=new A.c(B.h,["Paul wrote to the Thessalonians that the day of the Lord will come like a flood.",!1,"Paul wrote that the day of the Lord will come like a thief in the night, not like a flood.","1 Thessalonians 5:2","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aRP=new A.c(B.h,['Paul encouraged the Thessalonians to "pray without ceasing."',!0,"Paul instructed them to rejoice always, pray continually, and give thanks in all circumstances.","1 Thessalonians 5:17","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aRH=new A.c(B.h,["Paul taught that believers who are alive will rise first when the Lord returns.",!1,"Paul taught that the dead in Christ will rise first, then those who are alive will be caught up together with them.","1 Thessalonians 4:16-17","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aLD=new A.c(B.h,['Paul warned the Thessalonians about a "man of lawlessness" who would appear before Christ\'s return.',!0,"Paul taught that the day of the Lord would not come until the man of lawlessness is revealed, who will oppose God and exalt himself.","2 Thessalonians 2:3-4","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aJW=new A.c(B.h,['Paul wrote to the Thessalonians "If a man will not work, he shall not eat."',!0,"Paul gave this instruction to address idleness in the church, urging believers to work diligently.","2 Thessalonians 3:10","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aLg=new A.c(B.h,["Paul called Timothy his true son in the faith.",!0,"Paul addressed Timothy as his true child in the faith, reflecting their close spiritual relationship.","1 Timothy 1:2","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aPv=new A.c(B.h,["Paul wrote that money itself is the root of all evil.",!1,"Paul wrote that the love of money, not money itself, is a root of all kinds of evil.","1 Timothy 6:10","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aNH=new A.c(B.h,['Paul instructed Timothy to "fight the good fight of faith."',!0,"Paul urged Timothy to fight the good fight, take hold of eternal life, and guard what had been entrusted to him.","1 Timothy 6:12","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aR7=new A.c(B.h,["Paul wrote 2 Timothy during his first imprisonment in Rome.",!1,"Second Timothy was written during Paul's final (second) imprisonment in Rome, not his first. It is considered his last letter.","2 Timothy 4:6-8","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aOs=new A.c(B.h,['Paul wrote that "all Scripture is inspired by God and useful for teaching."',!0,"Paul affirmed that all Scripture is God-breathed and useful for teaching, rebuking, correcting, and training in righteousness.","2 Timothy 3:16","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aPS=new A.c(B.h,["Paul told Timothy that God gave believers a spirit of fear.",!1,"Paul wrote the opposite: God has not given us a spirit of fear, but of power, love, and self-discipline.","2 Timothy 1:7","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aMP=new A.c(B.h,["Paul left Titus in Crete to appoint elders in every town.",!0,"Paul instructed Titus to set in order what was left undone and appoint elders in every city on the island of Crete.","Titus 1:5","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aMK=new A.c(B.h,["Paul asked Philemon to punish Onesimus for running away.",!1,"Paul asked Philemon to receive Onesimus back as a beloved brother in Christ, not to punish him.","Philemon 1:15-16","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aNY=new A.c(B.h,["Onesimus was a runaway slave who became useful to Paul while Paul was in prison.",!0,"Onesimus had fled from Philemon and encountered Paul in prison, where he became a believer and assisted Paul.","Philemon 1:10-11","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aRn=new A.c(B.h,["The book of Hebrews describes Jesus as a high priest in the order of Aaron.",!1,"Hebrews describes Jesus as a high priest in the order of Melchizedek, not Aaron.","Hebrews 5:6","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aKG=new A.c(B.h,['Hebrews 11 is often called the "faith chapter" because it lists many Old Testament heroes of faith.',!0,"Hebrews 11 recounts the faith of Abel, Enoch, Noah, Abraham, Sarah, Moses, Rahab, and many others.","Hebrews 11:1-40","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aPO=new A.c(B.h,['Hebrews defines faith as "the substance of things hoped for, the evidence of things not seen."',!0,'This classic definition of faith opens the great "hall of faith" chapter in Hebrews.',"Hebrews 11:1","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aMw=new A.c(B.h,["The book of Hebrews teaches that Jesus offered Himself as a sacrifice that must be repeated annually.",!1,"Hebrews teaches the opposite: unlike the repeated animal sacrifices, Jesus offered Himself once for all as a perfect sacrifice.","Hebrews 10:10","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aLb=new A.c(B.h,["Hebrews says that the Word of God is sharper than any double-edged sword.",!0,"The Word of God is described as living and active, sharper than any two-edged sword, piercing to the division of soul and spirit.","Hebrews 4:12","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aRU=new A.c(B.h,["James wrote that the tongue is like a small rudder that steers a large ship.",!0,"James used several metaphors for the tongue, including a small rudder that guides a large ship, illustrating its power despite its small size.","James 3:4-5","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aNO=new A.c(B.h,["James wrote that if anyone lacks wisdom, they should ask God who gives generously.",!0,"James encourages believers to ask God for wisdom, promising that God gives generously to all without finding fault.","James 1:5","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aPq=new A.c(B.h,["James taught that a person is justified by faith alone, apart from works.",!1,"James explicitly wrote that a person is justified by works and not by faith alone, emphasizing that genuine faith produces action.","James 2:24","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aLl=new A.c(B.h,["James called the testing of faith a cause for sorrow.",!1,"James wrote to consider trials as pure joy, because the testing of faith produces perseverance.","James 1:2-3","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aP1=new A.c(B.h,['Peter described believers as "a royal priesthood, a holy nation."',!0,"Peter wrote that believers are a chosen people, a royal priesthood, a holy nation, God's special possession.","1 Peter 2:9","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aNg=new A.c(B.h,["Peter wrote that the devil prowls around like a roaring bear seeking someone to devour.",!1,"Peter wrote that the devil prowls around like a roaring lion, not a bear, seeking someone to devour.","1 Peter 5:8","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aOh=new A.c(B.h,["Peter wrote that with the Lord a day is like a thousand years and a thousand years like a day.",!0,"Peter used this to explain that the Lord is not slow in keeping His promise of return but is patient, wanting everyone to come to repentance.","2 Peter 3:8-9","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aRt=new A.c(B.h,['John wrote that "if we confess our sins, He is faithful and just to forgive us."',!0,"John assured believers that God is faithful and just to forgive sins and cleanse from all unrighteousness when sins are confessed.","1 John 1:9","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aJL=new A.c(B.h,['John wrote that "perfect faith drives out fear."',!1,"John wrote that perfect love, not faith, drives out fear.","1 John 4:18","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aOX=new A.c(B.h,["John wrote that we love God because we first chose Him.",!1,'John wrote "We love because He first loved us," emphasizing that God\'s love for us came first.',"1 John 4:19","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aQv=new A.c(B.h,['Second John is addressed to "the chosen lady and her children."',!0,"The letter is addressed to the elect lady and her children, which may refer to a specific woman or symbolically to a church.","2 John 1:1","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aRm=new A.c(B.h,["Third John praises a man named Diotrephes for his hospitality.",!1,"Diotrephes is criticized for refusing to welcome traveling believers and putting people out of the church. Gaius is the one praised for hospitality.","3 John 1:5-10","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aL1=new A.c(B.h,["Jude describes himself as the brother of James.",!0,"Jude identifies himself as a servant of Jesus Christ and a brother of James, likely the James who was Jesus' brother.","Jude 1:1","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aKY=new A.c(B.h,["Jude mentions that the archangel Michael disputed with Satan about the body of Moses.",!0,'Jude records that Michael the archangel, when contending with the devil about the body of Moses, did not pronounce a blasphemous judgment but said "The Lord rebuke you."',"Jude 1:9","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aMC=new A.c(B.h,["The book of Revelation was written to ten churches in Asia Minor.",!1,"Revelation contains letters to seven churches in Asia Minor: Ephesus, Smyrna, Pergamum, Thyatira, Sardis, Philadelphia, and Laodicea.","Revelation 1:11","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aJX=new A.c(B.h,["The church of Laodicea was rebuked for being lukewarm.",!0,"Jesus said to the Laodicean church that because they were lukewarm, neither hot nor cold, He was about to spit them out of His mouth.","Revelation 3:15-16","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aOM=new A.c(B.h,["In Revelation, twenty-four elders sit on thrones around the throne of God.",!0,"John saw twenty-four other thrones surrounding God's throne, with twenty-four elders dressed in white and wearing golden crowns.","Revelation 4:4","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aPH=new A.c(B.h,["The Lamb in Revelation is described as having seven horns and seven eyes.",!0,"The Lamb had seven horns and seven eyes, which are the seven spirits of God sent out into all the earth.","Revelation 5:6","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aPp=new A.c(B.h,["The first horseman of the Apocalypse rides a black horse.",!1,"The first horseman rides a white horse. The sequence is white, red, black, and pale.","Revelation 6:1-8","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aK4=new A.c(B.h,["Revelation describes 144,000 sealed servants of God from the ten tribes of Israel.",!1,"The 144,000 are from the twelve tribes of Israel, not ten, with 12,000 from each tribe.","Revelation 7:4-8","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aRl=new A.c(B.h,["The two witnesses in Revelation prophesy for 1,260 days.",!0,"God gives power to His two witnesses to prophesy for 1,260 days, clothed in sackcloth.","Revelation 11:3","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aP7=new A.c(B.h,["The woman in Revelation 12 is described as clothed with the moon and standing on the sun.",!1,"The woman is clothed with the sun, with the moon under her feet and a crown of twelve stars on her head.","Revelation 12:1","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aNS=new A.c(B.h,["The battle of Armageddon is mentioned in the book of Revelation.",!0,"The kings of the earth are gathered to a place called Armageddon in Hebrew for the great battle of the day of God Almighty.","Revelation 16:16","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aK3=new A.c(B.h,["Babylon the Great in Revelation is described as a city built on twelve hills.",!1,"Babylon the Great is described as sitting on seven hills, not twelve.","Revelation 17:9","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aMx=new A.c(B.h,["In Revelation, Satan is bound for a thousand years and thrown into the Abyss.",!0,"An angel seized the dragon (Satan), bound him for a thousand years, and threw him into the Abyss.","Revelation 20:1-3","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aQL=new A.c(B.h,["The New Jerusalem described in Revelation has ten gates.",!1,"The New Jerusalem has twelve gates, three on each side, with the names of the twelve tribes of Israel on them.","Revelation 21:12-13","New Testament"],t.R)
B.aJG=new A.c(B.h,["Revelation describes a river of the water of life flowing from the throne of God.",!0,"John saw the river of the water of life, clear as crystal, flowing from the throne of God and of the Lamb.","Revelation 22:1","New Testament"],t.R)
