B.Z={category:0,icon:1,fact:2}
B.aVk=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Numbers","\ud83d\udd22","The Bible contains 66 books \u2014 39 in the Old Testament and 27 in the New Testament \u2014 written by about 40 authors over 1,500 years."],t.w)
B.aVM=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Numbers","\ud83d\udd22","Psalm 119 is the longest chapter in the Bible with 176 verses. It is an acrostic poem with 22 sections, one for each letter of the Hebrew alphabet."],t.w)
B.aVJ=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Numbers","\ud83d\udd22","Psalm 117 is the shortest chapter in the Bible with only 2 verses, yet it contains a powerful call for all nations to praise the Lord."],t.w)
B.aVb=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Numbers","\ud83d\udd22",'The middle chapter of the Bible is Psalm 118. The middle verse is Psalm 118:8 \u2014 "It is better to take refuge in the Lord than to trust in humans."'],t.w)
B.aVC=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Numbers","\ud83d\udd22",'The word "Lord" appears over 7,000 times in the Bible. The word "God" appears about 4,300 times.'],t.w)
B.aVL=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Numbers","\ud83d\udd22","There are 1,189 chapters in the Bible \u2014 929 in the Old Testament and 260 in the New Testament."],t.w)
B.aVN=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Numbers","\ud83d\udd22",'The longest verse in the Bible is Esther 8:9, which contains 90 words in English. The shortest is John 11:35 \u2014 "Jesus wept."'],t.w)
B.aVQ=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Numbers","\ud83d\udd22","The number 40 appears 146 times in the Bible. It rained 40 days, Moses spent 40 years in the desert, Jesus was tempted for 40 days."],t.w)
B.aV_=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Numbers","\ud83d\udd22","The number 7 appears over 700 times in the Bible and symbolizes completeness and perfection \u2014 God rested on the 7th day of creation."],t.w)
B.aV3=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Numbers","\ud83d\udd22","The number 12 is used 187 times in the Bible. There were 12 tribes of Israel, 12 apostles, and 12 gates in the New Jerusalem."],t.w)
B.aVc=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Numbers","\ud83d\udd22","The Bible contains over 3,200 verses with fulfilled prophecies. Some scholars estimate about 2,500 prophecies appear in the Bible, with about 2,000 already fulfilled."],t.w)
B.aV0=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Numbers","\ud83d\udd22","The book of Isaiah has 66 chapters \u2014 matching the 66 books of the Bible. The first 39 chapters focus on judgment (like the 39 OT books) and the last 27 on comfort (like the 27 NT books)."],t.w)
B.aVi=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Geography","\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f","The Sea of Galilee is actually a freshwater lake, only 13 miles long and 8 miles wide. It sits 700 feet below sea level, making it one of the lowest freshwater lakes on Earth."],t.w)
B.aVs=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Geography","\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f","The Dead Sea, at 1,412 feet below sea level, is the lowest point on Earth. Its salt content is nearly 10 times that of the ocean, making it impossible for fish to survive."],t.w)
B.aVS=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Geography","\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f","The Jordan River flows 156 miles from Mount Hermon to the Dead Sea. Though narrow and shallow, it's one of the most significant rivers in biblical history."],t.w)
B.aVA=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Geography","\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f","Mount Sinai, where Moses received the Ten Commandments, is traditionally identified as Jebel Musa in Egypt's Sinai Peninsula, standing at 7,497 feet."],t.w)
B.aVF=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Geography","\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f","Ancient Jericho is considered one of the oldest continuously inhabited cities in the world, dating back over 10,000 years. It sits about 850 feet below sea level."],t.w)
B.aVo=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Geography","\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f",'Bethlehem, where Jesus was born, is only about 6 miles south of Jerusalem. Its name means "House of Bread" in Hebrew.'],t.w)
B.aVK=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Geography","\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f",'Nazareth, where Jesus grew up, was a tiny village of only 200\u2013400 people in the first century. That\'s why Nathanael asked, "Can anything good come from Nazareth?"'],t.w)
B.aVx=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Geography","\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f","The Garden of Gethsemane, where Jesus prayed before His arrest, is located at the foot of the Mount of Olives. Ancient olive trees still stand there today."],t.w)
B.aV6=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Geography","\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f","Paul's missionary journeys covered approximately 10,000 miles across the Roman Empire \u2014 mostly on foot and by sailing ship."],t.w)
B.aVB=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Geography","\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f","Mount Ararat, where Noah's Ark is said to have rested, is the highest peak in modern Turkey at 16,854 feet. It's a dormant volcanic mountain."],t.w)
B.aVy=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Geography","\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f","The seven churches of Revelation \u2014 Ephesus, Smyrna, Pergamum, Thyatira, Sardis, Philadelphia, and Laodicea \u2014 were all located in modern-day Turkey."],t.w)
B.aVP=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible Geography","\ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f","The city of Capernaum on the Sea of Galilee served as Jesus' home base during His Galilean ministry. Peter's house there has been excavated by archaeologists."],t.w)
B.aV7=new A.c(B.Z,["Fun Fact","\ud83d\udca1",'Methuselah lived to be 969 years old, making him the oldest person recorded in the Bible. His name means "when he dies, it shall come" \u2014 and the flood came the year he died.'],t.w)
B.aVG=new A.c(B.Z,["Fun Fact","\ud83d\udca1","The Bible never says there were three wise men. Matthew 2 mentions three gifts \u2014 gold, frankincense, and myrrh \u2014 but not the number of Magi."],t.w)
B.aVm=new A.c(B.Z,["Fun Fact","\ud83d\udca1","Goliath was approximately 9 feet 9 inches tall (about 3 meters). The stone David used to defeat him likely traveled at around 100 mph from his sling."],t.w)
B.aVt=new A.c(B.Z,["Fun Fact","\ud83d\udca1","The walls of Jericho were so thick that Rahab's house was built right into them. She helped the Israelite spies and later became an ancestor of Jesus."],t.w)
B.aVW=new A.c(B.Z,["Fun Fact","\ud83d\udca1","King Solomon had 700 wives and 300 concubines (1 Kings 11:3). Despite being the wisest man, his marriages to foreign women led him astray from God."],t.w)
B.aV9=new A.c(B.Z,["Fun Fact","\ud83d\udca1","The prophet Elijah was fed by ravens during a famine (1 Kings 17:4-6). Ravens are considered unclean animals in Jewish law, making this an unusual miracle."],t.w)
B.aV1=new A.c(B.Z,["Fun Fact","\ud83d\udca1","Samson killed 1,000 Philistines with the jawbone of a donkey (Judges 15:15). In his final act, he destroyed a temple, killing more people in death than in life."],t.w)
B.aVT=new A.c(B.Z,["Fun Fact","\ud83d\udca1","Noah's Ark was approximately 450 feet long, 75 feet wide, and 45 feet high \u2014 roughly the size of a modern aircraft carrier."],t.w)
B.aVn=new A.c(B.Z,["Fun Fact","\ud83d\udca1","The Bible was the first major book printed using movable type. Johannes Gutenberg printed it around 1455, and it revolutionized the spread of knowledge."],t.w)
B.aVd=new A.c(B.Z,["Fun Fact","\ud83d\udca1",'Jonah wasn\'t swallowed by a whale \u2014 the Bible says "great fish." The Hebrew word "dag gadol" literally means "great fish." Jesus later referenced this event as a sign of His own resurrection.'],t.w)
B.aVz=new A.c(B.Z,["Fun Fact","\ud83d\udca1","The apostle Paul was shipwrecked at least 3 times, beaten with rods 3 times, whipped 5 times, and stoned once \u2014 yet continued preaching fearlessly."],t.w)
B.aVu=new A.c(B.Z,["Fun Fact","\ud83d\udca1","King David was a musician, warrior, poet, and king. He wrote about half of the 150 Psalms, many while fleeing from enemies or praising God after victories."],t.w)
B.aVl=new A.c(B.Z,["Fun Fact","\ud83d\udca1","The first person to see the risen Jesus was Mary Magdalene (John 20:16). In a culture where women's testimony wasn't considered valid in court, God chose a woman as the first witness."],t.w)
B.aVa=new A.c(B.Z,["Fun Fact","\ud83d\udca1","The oldest person to have a child in the Bible was Abraham, who was 100 years old when Isaac was born. Sarah was 90."],t.w)
B.aVf=new A.c(B.Z,["Fun Fact","\ud83d\udca1","Jesus performed His first miracle at a wedding in Cana, turning approximately 120-180 gallons of water into the finest wine."],t.w)
B.aVv=new A.c(B.Z,["Fun Fact","\ud83d\udca1","The feeding of the 5,000 is the only miracle (besides the resurrection) recorded in all four Gospels \u2014 Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John."],t.w)
B.aUY=new A.c(B.Z,["Character Spotlight","\ud83d\udc64","Moses spent 40 years as an Egyptian prince, 40 years as a shepherd in Midian, and 40 years leading Israel through the wilderness \u2014 three complete chapters of life."],t.w)
B.aUZ=new A.c(B.Z,["Character Spotlight","\ud83d\udc64","Joseph was sold into slavery at 17, imprisoned for years, and became Egypt's prime minister at 30. He waited 13 years between God's promise and its fulfillment."],t.w)
B.aVe=new A.c(B.Z,["Character Spotlight","\ud83d\udc64","Ruth, a Moabite widow, chose to follow her mother-in-law Naomi and the God of Israel. She became the great-grandmother of King David and an ancestor of Jesus."],t.w)
B.aVj=new A.c(B.Z,["Character Spotlight","\ud83d\udc64","Daniel served faithfully under four different kings in Babylon and Persia \u2014 Nebuchadnezzar, Belshazzar, Darius, and Cyrus \u2014 spanning roughly 70 years."],t.w)
B.aV4=new A.c(B.Z,["Character Spotlight","\ud83d\udc64","Esther risked her life to save her people by approaching the king uninvited \u2014 a crime punishable by death. Her bravery saved the entire Jewish nation from genocide."],t.w)
B.aVr=new A.c(B.Z,["Character Spotlight","\ud83d\udc64","Peter denied Jesus three times before the rooster crowed, yet became the rock upon which Christ built His church and preached the sermon at Pentecost that converted 3,000."],t.w)
B.aVI=new A.c(B.Z,["Character Spotlight","\ud83d\udc64","Paul (formerly Saul) went from being Christianity's greatest persecutor to its greatest missionary. He wrote 13 of the 27 New Testament books."],t.w)
B.aVq=new A.c(B.Z,["Character Spotlight","\ud83d\udc64","Deborah was the only female judge of Israel. She was a prophetess, judge, and military leader who led Israel to victory over the Canaanites."],t.w)
B.aVE=new A.c(B.Z,["Character Spotlight","\ud83d\udc64","Nehemiah was a cupbearer to the Persian king \u2014 a position of great trust. He left this comfortable life to rebuild Jerusalem's walls in just 52 days."],t.w)
B.aVR=new A.c(B.Z,["Character Spotlight","\ud83d\udc64","Abraham left his homeland at age 75 when God called him. He waited 25 years for the promised son Isaac, becoming the father of faith for three world religions."],t.w)
B.aVU=new A.c(B.Z,["Character Spotlight","\ud83d\udc64","Gideon started with an army of 32,000 men, but God reduced it to just 300 \u2014 so that Israel would know the victory came from God alone, not human strength."],t.w)
B.aVp=new A.c(B.Z,["Character Spotlight","\ud83d\udc64","Elijah called fire down from heaven, outran a chariot, and was taken to heaven in a whirlwind \u2014 yet struggled with depression and wanted to die after a great victory."],t.w)
B.aVw=new A.c(B.Z,["Character Spotlight","\ud83d\udc64",'Mary, the mother of Jesus, was likely a teenager (12-14 years old) when the angel Gabriel announced she would bear the Messiah. She said, "I am the Lord\'s servant."'],t.w)
B.aVV=new A.c(B.Z,["Character Spotlight","\ud83d\udc64","John the Baptist lived in the wilderness, wore camel hair clothing, and ate locusts and wild honey. Jesus said no one born of woman was greater than John."],t.w)
B.aVO=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible & Language","\ud83d\udcdc","The Old Testament was written primarily in Hebrew, with small portions in Aramaic. The New Testament was written entirely in Greek \u2014 the common language of the Roman Empire."],t.w)
B.aV5=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible & Language","\ud83d\udcdc",'The word "Bible" comes from the Greek word "biblia" meaning "books." It\'s literally a library \u2014 a collection of 66 books written across 3 continents.'],t.w)
B.aV8=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible & Language","\ud83d\udcdc",'The word "Gospel" means "good news." The four Gospels \u2014 Matthew, Mark, Luke, and John \u2014 each present Jesus from a unique perspective.'],t.w)
B.aVD=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible & Language","\ud83d\udcdc",'"Amen" is a Hebrew word meaning "so be it" or "truly." It\'s one of the few words used in virtually every language on earth without translation.'],t.w)
B.aV2=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible & Language","\ud83d\udcdc",'The word "Hallelujah" is Hebrew for "Praise the Lord." It appears 24 times in the Bible \u2014 23 times in Psalms and once in Revelation.'],t.w)
B.aVH=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible & Language","\ud83d\udcdc","The Bible has been translated into over 3,500 languages, making it by far the most translated book in human history."],t.w)
B.aVh=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible & Language","\ud83d\udcdc","Hebrew is read right to left, and ancient Hebrew had no vowels \u2014 only consonants. Readers had to know the language well enough to fill in the vowels."],t.w)
B.aVg=new A.c(B.Z,["Bible & Language","\ud83d\udcdc",'Many common English phrases come from the Bible: "the writing on the wall" (Daniel 5), "a drop in the bucket" (Isaiah 40:15), and "the salt of the earth" (Matthew 5:13).'],t.w)
