B.azQ=new A.c(B.o,["Matthew 5:3",'"Blessed are the poor in spirit, for theirs is the kingdom of heaven."','Jesus begins the Sermon on the Mount by turning worldly values upside down. "Poor in spirit" means recognizing our own spiritual bankruptcy before God \u2014 that we have nothing to offer and everything to receive. This humility is the doorway into the kingdom.',"In the Beatitudes, who does Jesus say the kingdom of heaven belongs to?",B.akj,"The poor in spirit"],t.R)
B.akM=A.a(s(["His miracles","His righteousness","His blessings","His mercy"]),t.s)
B.awv=new A.c(B.o,["Matthew 6:33",'"But seek first his kingdom and his righteousness, and all these things will be given to you as well."',"Jesus said this in the context of worrying about food and clothing. His solution is not to stop caring about needs, but to reorder our priorities. When God's kingdom is our first pursuit, He takes responsibility for the rest.","Matthew 6:33 says we should seek first God's kingdom and what else?",B.akM,"His righteousness"],t.R)
B.aar=A.a(s(["Eyes","Path","Mind","Heart"]),t.s)
B.avC=new A.c(B.o,["Psalm 119:105",'"Your word is a lamp for my feet, a light on my path."',"A lamp for the feet illuminates just the next step \u2014 not the whole road ahead. God rarely shows us the entire journey. He gives us enough light for today, asking us to trust Him for tomorrow.","Psalm 119:105 describes God's word as a lamp for our feet and a light for our what?",B.aar,"Path"],t.R)
B.amH=A.a(s(["We are strong","God will be with us","Victory is guaranteed","Our enemies are weak"]),t.s)
B.avF=new A.c(B.o,["Joshua 1:9",'"Have I not commanded you? Be strong and courageous. Do not be afraid; do not be discouraged, for the Lord your God will be with you wherever you go."','God did not tell Joshua to "feel" courageous \u2014 He commanded him to "be" courageous. Courage in Scripture is often a choice before it is a feeling. The reason we can choose it: God is with us.',"In Joshua 1:9, what reason does God give for why we should not be afraid?",B.amH,"God will be with us"],t.R)
