B.avx=new A.c(B.o,["2 Timothy 3:16-17",'"All Scripture is God-breathed and is useful for teaching, rebuking, correcting and training in righteousness, so that the servant of God may be thoroughly equipped for every good work."','God-breathed \u2014 Paul\'s word for this is "theopneustos." The Bible is not merely a human record of religious experience; it carries the very breath of God. This is why it has power to change us, not just inform us.',"According to 2 Timothy 3:16, all Scripture is what?",B.a86,"God-breathed"],t.R)
B.akT=A.a(s(["Fasting","Prayer and petition","Worship","Scripture reading"]),t.s)
B.ayk=new A.c(B.o,["Philippians 4:6-7",'"Do not be anxious about anything, but in every situation, by prayer and petition, with thanksgiving, present your requests to God. And the peace of God, which transcends all understanding, will guard your hearts and your minds in Christ Jesus."','The antidote to anxiety is not willpower \u2014 it\'s prayer. Specifically, Paul adds "with thanksgiving" \u2014 gratitude for what God has already done shifts our focus from what we fear to who we trust.',"Philippians 4:6 says we should not be anxious, but instead present our requests to God through what?",B.akT,"Prayer and petition"],t.R)
