B.awR=new A.c(B.o,["Romans 5:8",'"But God demonstrates his own love for us in this: While we were still sinners, Christ died for us."','The most remarkable word in this verse is "while." Not after we got our act together. Not when we deserved it. While we were still in our sin \u2014 that is when God acted. Grace is defined by its timing.',"Romans 5:8 says Christ died for us while we were still what?",B.abN,"Sinners"],t.R)
B.a7s=A.a(s(["Beautifully","Wonderfully","Perfectly","Carefully"]),t.s)
B.az2=new A.c(B.o,["Psalm 139:14",'"I praise you because I am fearfully and wonderfully made; your works are wonderful, I know that full well."',"David wrote this knowing God had seen him in his mother's womb (v.13). Our worth is not determined by what others see or what we achieve \u2014 it is grounded in the fact that we were made intentionally, carefully, and wonderfully by God.","Psalm 139:14 says we are fearfully and how else made?",B.a7s,"Wonderfully"],t.R)
