B.auL=new A.c(B.o,["Colossians 3:23",'"Whatever you do, work at it with all your heart, as working for the Lord, not for human masters."',"Paul wrote this to slaves \u2014 people with the least glamorous, least recognized work imaginable. Yet he elevated every task by changing its audience. When we work for God, there is no ordinary work.","Colossians 3:23 says we should work as if working for whom?",B.akY,"The Lord"],t.R)
B.a9e=A.a(s(["Avoid them","Pray for them only","Love them","Forgive them secretly"]),t.s)
B.azm=new A.c(B.o,["Luke 6:27",'"But to you who are listening I say: Love your enemies, do good to those who hate you."',"This command separates Christian ethics from every other moral system. Loving those who love us costs nothing. Loving enemies \u2014 people who have genuinely wronged us \u2014 requires a supernatural source of love.","In Luke 6:27, what does Jesus command us to do to our enemies?",B.a9e,"Love them"],t.R)
B.a4m=A.a(s(["God spoke to Adam","God rested","God created the heavens and the earth","God made man"]),t.s)
B.awU=new A.c(B.o,["Genesis 1:1",'"In the beginning God created the heavens and the earth."',"The Bible's opening statement answers the most fundamental question: where did everything come from? Before time, before matter, before anything \u2014 God was. And everything that exists, exists because He chose to create it.","What is the very first thing recorded in the Bible in Genesis 1:1?",B.a4m,"God created the heavens and the earth"],t.R)
