B.axQ=new A.c(B.o,["Genesis 1:27",'"So God created man in his own image, in the image of God he created him; male and female he created them."',"Every human being carries the divine image, giving each person inherent dignity and worth. This truth calls us to treat ourselves and others with profound respect, knowing we reflect something of our Creator.","In whose image was man created?",B.a6H,"God's image"],t.R)
B.a7h=A.a(s(["His country, kindred, and father's house","His flocks and herds","The city of Ur only","His wife and children"]),t.s)
B.awh=new A.c(B.o,["Genesis 12:1",'"Now the Lord said to Abram, Go from your country and your kindred and your father\'s house to the land that I will show you."',"God called Abram to leave everything familiar and step into the unknown. Faith often requires us to release what is comfortable and trust God with an uncertain path, believing His plans are greater than our own.","What did God tell Abram to leave?",B.a7h,"His country, kindred, and father's house"],t.R)
B.a9V=A.a(s(["Bethel","The Lord Will Provide","Mount Sinai","Beersheba"]),t.s)
B.ax6=new A.c(B.o,["Genesis 22:14",'"So Abraham called the name of that place, The Lord will provide; as it is said to this day, On the mount of the Lord it shall be provided."',"After God provided the ram in place of Isaac, Abraham named the place Jehovah Jireh. In our most difficult trials, God reveals Himself as our provider, meeting needs in ways we could never anticipate.","What name did Abraham give the place where God provided a ram?",B.a9V,"The Lord Will Provide"],t.R)
B.a8h=A.a(s(["Abraham","Isaac","Jacob","Joseph"]),t.s)
B.aul=new A.c(B.o,["Genesis 28:15",'"Behold, I am with you and will keep you wherever you go, and will bring you back to this land. For I will not leave you until I have done what I have promised you."',"God spoke these words to Jacob during his dream at Bethel, promising His constant presence. No matter where life takes us, God's faithfulness follows. He completes every promise He makes.","Who did God make this promise to at Bethel?",B.a8h,"Jacob"],t.R)
B.ae3=A.a(s(["Moses","Jacob","Joseph","Benjamin"]),t.s)
B.av7=new A.c(B.o,["Genesis 50:20",'"As for you, you meant evil against me, but God meant it for good, to bring it about that many people should be kept alive, as they are today."',"Joseph spoke these words to his brothers who had sold him into slavery. God's sovereignty can transform even the worst human intentions into instruments of blessing and salvation.","Who spoke these words to his brothers?",B.ae3,"Joseph"],t.R)
