B.aS9=new A.c(B.v,["The descendants of Jacob had gone down to Egypt during the time of Joseph and had grown into a mighty nation. A new Pharaoh arose who did not know Joseph and feared the growing Israelite population. He enslaved them, forcing them to build great cities like Pithom and Rameses under brutal conditions.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aU6=new A.c(B.v,["When slavery was not enough to slow their growth, Pharaoh issued a terrible decree: every Hebrew baby boy was to be thrown into the Nile River. One brave Levite mother, Jochebed, could not bear to obey. She hid her infant son for three months, then made a watertight basket from bulrushes and placed him in the reeds at the river's edge.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUB=new A.c(B.v,["The baby's sister Miriam watched from a distance. When Pharaoh's daughter came to bathe and discovered the basket, her heart was moved with compassion. Miriam cleverly offered to find a Hebrew woman to nurse the baby \u2014 and brought the baby's own mother. So Jochebed nursed her own son, paid by Pharaoh's household.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSX=new A.c(B.v,['When the child was old enough, he was brought to Pharaoh\'s daughter who adopted him as her own son. She named him Moses, meaning "drawn out of the water." Little did she know that this baby, drawn from the Nile, would one day draw all of Israel out of Egypt.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.amF=A.a(s([B.aS9,B.aU6,B.aUB,B.aSX]),t.o)
B.l={question:0,options:1,answer:2,explanation:3,bibleReference:4}
B.ahZ=A.a(s(["100 years","200 years","400 to 430 years","600 years"]),t.s)
B.aF0=new A.c(B.l,["Approximately how long were the Israelites in Egypt?",B.ahZ,"400 to 430 years","God told Abraham his descendants would be strangers in a land for 400 years; Exodus 12:40 records the stay as 430 years.","Genesis 15:13, Exodus 12:40"],t.M)
B.amh=A.a(s(["They had built a large army",u.cD,"They refused to pay taxes","They had taken Egyptian land"]),t.s)
B.aCA=new A.c(B.l,["Why did Pharaoh begin to fear the Israelites in Egypt?",B.amh,u.cD,"A new Pharaoh feared the Israelites had become so numerous that in a war they might join Egypt's enemies and fight against Egypt.","Exodus 1:9-10"],t.M)
B.aoJ=A.a(s(["They were to be sold as slaves","They were to be taken from their mothers",u.c8,"They were to be sent to the desert"]),t.s)
B.aBV=new A.c(B.l,["What did Pharaoh order done to all Hebrew baby boys?",B.aoJ,u.c8,"Pharaoh commanded all his people that every Hebrew son born must be thrown into the Nile, though daughters could live.","Exodus 1:22"],t.M)
B.adW=A.a(s(["Miriam","Deborah","Jochebed","Zipporah"]),t.s)
B.aGf=new A.c(B.l,["What was the name of Moses' mother?",B.adW,"Jochebed","Moses' mother was Jochebed, a daughter of Levi, who hid her son for three months before placing him in the basket.","Exodus 6:20"],t.M)
B.a50=A.a(s(["A wooden boat","A clay jar","A basket made from bulrushes","A woven blanket"]),t.s)
B.aGj=new A.c(B.l,["What was baby Moses placed in to float on the Nile?",B.a50,"A basket made from bulrushes","Jochebed made a basket from papyrus reeds (bulrushes), coated it with tar and pitch to make it waterproof, and placed baby Moses in it.","Exodus 2:3"],t.M)
B.a59=A.a(s(["His mother Jochebed","His brother Aaron","His sister Miriam","A family servant"]),t.s)
B.aE_=new A.c(B.l,["Who watched over baby Moses' basket in the reeds of the Nile?",B.a59,"His sister Miriam","Moses' sister stood at a distance to see what would happen to her baby brother in the basket among the reeds.","Exodus 2:4"],t.M)
B.aqT=A.a(s(["A Hebrew midwife","Pharaoh's daughter","An Egyptian soldier","A Levite woman"]),t.s)
B.aBZ=new A.c(B.l,["Who discovered the basket containing baby Moses?",B.aqT,"Pharaoh's daughter","Pharaoh's daughter came to the Nile to bathe, saw the basket among the reeds, and when she opened it she saw the baby crying and felt sorry for him.","Exodus 2:5-6"],t.M)
B.a6G=A.a(s(["Pharaoh's daughter herself","An Egyptian noblewoman","His own mother Jochebed","A Hebrew midwife"]),t.s)
B.aGz=new A.c(B.l,["Who nursed baby Moses after he was rescued from the Nile?",B.a6G,"His own mother Jochebed","Through Miriam's clever suggestion, Pharaoh's daughter hired a Hebrew nurse who was actually Moses' own mother, so she nursed her own son.","Exodus 2:8-9"],t.M)
B.anp=A.a(s(["Deliverer of Israel","God has heard","Drawn out of the water","Child of the Nile"]),t.s)
B.aEh=new A.c(B.l,["What does the name Moses mean?",B.anp,"Drawn out of the water",'Pharaoh\'s daughter gave him the name Moses saying, "I drew him out of the water" \u2014 the name reflecting the miraculous circumstances of his rescue.',"Exodus 2:10"],t.M)
B.a4a=A.a(s(["Caleb and Deborah","Joshua and Rahab","Aaron and Miriam","Levi and Leah"]),t.s)
B.aDm=new A.c(B.l,["Who were Moses' brother and sister?",B.a4a,"Aaron and Miriam","Moses' older brother was Aaron, who would become his spokesman, and his older sister was Miriam, who watched over him as a baby.","Exodus 4:14, Exodus 15:20"],t.M)
B.a5P=A.a(s([B.aF0,B.aCA,B.aBV,B.aGf,B.aGj,B.aE_,B.aBZ,B.aGz,B.aEh,B.aDm]),t.J)
B.aIF=new A.c(B.ak,["slavery_and_birth","Slavery in Egypt and Moses' Birth","Easy",!1,30,6,B.amF,B.a5P],t.M)
B.aT7=new A.c(B.v,["Moses had fled Egypt forty years earlier after killing an Egyptian who was beating a Hebrew slave. He settled in the land of Midian, married Zipporah, and became a shepherd for his father-in-law Jethro. Far from the palaces of Egypt where he had been raised, Moses now lived a quiet, humble life tending flocks among the desert hills.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTf=new A.c(B.v,['One day, while leading the flock to the far side of the wilderness, Moses came to Horeb \u2014 the mountain of God. There he saw an astonishing sight: a bush that was on fire, yet was not burning up. Curious, Moses turned aside to investigate this strange phenomenon, and as he drew near, a voice called out from within the flames: "Moses! Moses!"',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTn=new A.c(B.v,["God revealed Himself as the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, and told Moses to remove his sandals, for he was standing on holy ground. He had heard the cries of His people suffering in Egypt and had chosen Moses to go to Pharaoh and lead the Israelites out of slavery. Moses was overwhelmed and afraid, protesting that he was not capable of such a task.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTw=new A.c(B.v,['God patiently answered every objection Moses raised. When Moses asked God\'s name, God replied: "I AM WHO I AM." When Moses said he was not eloquent, God appointed his brother Aaron to be his spokesman. God showed Moses signs \u2014 turning his staff into a snake and making his hand leprous and whole again \u2014 to convince Pharaoh and the Israelites that the Lord had truly sent him.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.a4U=A.a(s([B.aT7,B.aTf,B.aTn,B.aTw]),t.o)
B.afz=A.a(s(["20 years","30 years","40 years","50 years"]),t.s)
B.aDk=new A.c(B.l,["How many years had Moses been living in Midian before the burning bush encounter?",B.afz,"40 years","Moses fled Egypt at age 40 and spent 40 years in Midian as a shepherd before God appeared to him at the burning bush, making him 80 years old at the time of his call.","Acts 7:30, Exodus 7:7"],t.M)
B.a6p=A.a(s(["Mount Sinai","Mount Carmel","Mount Horeb","Mount Nebo"]),t.s)
B.aDZ=new A.c(B.l,["What is the name of the mountain where Moses encountered the burning bush?",B.a6p,"Mount Horeb","The burning bush appeared to Moses at Horeb, the mountain of God. Horeb and Sinai are different names used in Scripture for the same sacred mountain.","Exodus 3:1"],t.M)
B.acn=A.a(s(["It produced no smoke","It was not consumed by the fire","It glowed with seven colors","It grew taller as Moses watched"]),t.s)
B.aC6=new A.c(B.l,["What was remarkable about the burning bush?",B.acn,"It was not consumed by the fire","Moses noticed that although the bush was on fire, it did not burn up. This miraculous sign drew his attention and led him to approach, where God spoke to him.","Exodus 3:2-3"],t.M)
B.agT=A.a(s(["Drawing water from a well","Praying on a hillside","Tending his father-in-law's flock","Traveling to a nearby city"]),t.s)
B.aBK=new A.c(B.l,["What was Moses doing when he first saw the burning bush?",B.agT,"Tending his father-in-law's flock","Moses was shepherding the flock of his father-in-law Jethro (also called Reuel) when he led the flock to the far side of the wilderness and came to Horeb.","Exodus 3:1"],t.M)
B.akd=A.a(s(["The Lord of Hosts","I AM WHO I AM","The Almighty God","The God of Heaven"]),t.s)
B.aCx=new A.c(B.l,["What name did God give Himself when Moses asked?",B.akd,"I AM WHO I AM",'When Moses asked for God\'s name to tell the Israelites, God replied "I AM WHO I AM," and said to tell them "I AM has sent me to you." This reveals God\'s eternal, self-existent nature.',"Exodus 3:14"],t.M)
B.alX=A.a(s(["He did not know the Egyptian language","He was too young and inexperienced",u.L,"He had taken a vow of silence"]),t.s)
B.aAv=new A.c(B.l,["What excuse did Moses give for not being able to speak to Pharaoh?",B.alX,u.L,"Moses protested that he was not eloquent and was slow of speech and tongue, suggesting he was not a skilled orator. God responded that He would help Moses speak and teach him what to say.","Exodus 4:10"],t.M)
B.amj=A.a(s(["Miriam, his sister","Aaron, his brother","Jethro, his father-in-law","Joshua, his servant"]),t.s)
B.aD0=new A.c(B.l,["Who did God appoint to help Moses speak to Pharaoh?",B.amj,"Aaron, his brother","God appointed Aaron, Moses' brother, to be his spokesman. Aaron would speak to the people while Moses would tell Aaron what God had said, and God would help them both.","Exodus 4:14-16"],t.M)
B.a7D=A.a(s(["Wash his hands in a nearby stream","Bow his face to the ground","Remove his sandals from his feet","Cover his face with his cloak"]),t.s)
B.aFm=new A.c(B.l,["What did God instruct Moses to do before approaching the burning bush?",B.a7D,"Remove his sandals from his feet",'God told Moses: "Do not come any closer. Take off your sandals, for the place where you are standing is holy ground." This act signified reverence before God\'s holy presence.',"Exodus 3:5"],t.M)
B.aqu=A.a(s(["It brought water out of a rock","It divided a river",u.nY,"It blossomed with flowers overnight"]),t.s)
B.aDA=new A.c(B.l,["What miracle did God perform with Moses' staff as a sign?",B.aqu,u.nY,"God told Moses to throw his staff on the ground, and it became a snake. Moses ran from it, but God told him to grab it by the tail and it became a staff again. This was a sign to authenticate Moses before Pharaoh and the Israelites.","Exodus 4:3-4"],t.M)
B.aiC=A.a(s(["Tribe of Judah","Tribe of Levi","Tribe of Reuben","Tribe of Joseph"]),t.s)
B.aBt=new A.c(B.l,["Which tribe did Moses belong to, according to the book of Exodus?",B.aiC,"Tribe of Levi","Moses was a descendant of Levi. His parents were Amram and Jochebed, both from the tribe of Levi. His brother Aaron and sister Miriam were also Levites.","Exodus 2:1-2, Exodus 6:20"],t.M)
B.anH=A.a(s([B.aDk,B.aDZ,B.aC6,B.aBK,B.aCx,B.aAv,B.aD0,B.aFm,B.aDA,B.aBt]),t.J)
B.aJf=new A.c(B.ak,["burning_bush","The Burning Bush","Easy",!1,30,6,B.a4U,B.anH],t.M)
B.aTl=new A.c(B.v,["After forty years in Midian, God spoke to Moses from a burning bush and commissioned him to return to Egypt and demand that Pharaoh release the Israelites. Moses, with his brother Aaron, stood before Pharaoh. But God had said Pharaoh's heart would be hardened, and through this, God would demonstrate His supreme power over Egypt and all its gods.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTi=new A.c(B.v,["Pharaoh repeatedly refused to let Israel go. Each refusal was met with a devastating plague \u2014 turning the Nile to blood, filling the land with frogs, then gnats, then swarms of flies, then disease upon livestock. Each plague targeted one of Egypt's gods, showing that the God of Israel was Lord over all creation.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSr=new A.c(B.v,["The plagues intensified with painful boils on all the Egyptians, then a storm of hail mixed with fire that destroyed crops and livestock remaining in the fields, then locusts that devoured everything the hail had left, then a darkness so thick it could be felt \u2014 three days of absolute blackness over the land of Egypt.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSP=new A.c(B.v,["The final and most devastating plague was the death of the firstborn \u2014 from Pharaoh's own son to the firstborn of the prisoner in the dungeon. God instructed the Israelites to slaughter a lamb and paint its blood on their doorposts. The destroyer would pass over any house marked with blood. This night became the Passover \u2014 a feast Israel would celebrate forever.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.ahs=A.a(s([B.aTl,B.aTi,B.aSr,B.aSP]),t.o)
B.ajE=A.a(s(["Frogs covering the land","Water turning to blood","Darkness for three days","A plague of locusts"]),t.s)
B.aD4=new A.c(B.l,["What was the first plague God sent upon Egypt?",B.ajE,"Water turning to blood","In the first plague, Aaron struck the Nile with his staff and all the water in Egypt turned to blood, killing the fish and making the water undrinkable.","Exodus 7:20-21"],t.M)
B.abi=A.a(s(["Gnats","Flies","Frogs","Locusts"]),t.s)
B.aBi=new A.c(B.l,["What was the second plague sent upon Egypt?",B.abi,"Frogs","The second plague brought frogs up from the Nile in massive numbers to cover all of Egypt \u2014 the land, the houses, the beds, and even the ovens.","Exodus 8:2-6"],t.M)
B.age=A.a(s(["Second plague","Third plague \u2014 gnats or lice","Fourth plague","Sixth plague"]),t.s)
B.aEa=new A.c(B.l,["Which plague involved tiny insects that came upon the people and animals of Egypt?",B.age,"Third plague \u2014 gnats or lice","In the third plague, Aaron struck the dust of the earth and it became gnats (or lice) on people and animals throughout Egypt.","Exodus 8:16-17"],t.M)
B.ab_=A.a(s(["Third plague","Fourth plague","Fifth plague \u2014 pestilence on livestock","Seventh plague"]),t.s)
B.aAF=new A.c(B.l,["Which plague brought death to the livestock and animals of Egypt?",B.ab_,"Fifth plague \u2014 pestilence on livestock","The fifth plague was a severe pestilence on Egypt's livestock \u2014 horses, donkeys, camels, cattle, sheep and goats all died, but Israel's animals were untouched.","Exodus 9:3-6"],t.M)
B.afR=A.a(s(["Fourth plague","Fifth plague","Sixth plague","Seventh plague"]),t.s)
B.aEb=new A.c(B.l,["Which plague caused painful sores and boils on people and animals?",B.afR,"Sixth plague","The sixth plague brought festering boils that broke out on people and animals throughout Egypt, even affecting the magicians so they could not stand before Moses.","Exodus 9:9-10"],t.M)
B.ajG=A.a(s(["Burning ash and smoke","Hail mixed with fire","Acid rain and lightning","Flaming stones"]),t.s)
B.aBA=new A.c(B.l,["What fell from the sky in the seventh plague?",B.ajG,"Hail mixed with fire","The seventh plague was the worst hailstorm in Egypt's history \u2014 hail with lightning flashing through it struck down people, animals, and crops across Egypt.","Exodus 9:23-24"],t.M)
B.a9L=A.a(s(["Darkness","Frogs","Gnats","Locusts"]),t.s)
B.aCy=new A.c(B.l,["What covered all the land of Egypt in the eighth plague?",B.a9L,"Locusts","The eighth plague brought locusts that covered the whole land and devoured every plant and all the fruit of the trees left by the hail.","Exodus 10:14-15"],t.M)
B.yq=A.a(s(["One day","Two days","Three days","Seven days"]),t.s)
B.aFE=new A.c(B.l,["How long did the thick darkness of the ninth plague last over Egypt?",B.yq,"Three days","The ninth plague was total darkness over Egypt for three days \u2014 a darkness so dense it could be felt, though the Israelites had light in their homes.","Exodus 10:22-23"],t.M)
B.afG=A.a(s(["Staying indoors all night","Wearing white garments",u.b6,"Burning incense in their homes"]),t.s)
B.aFF=new A.c(B.l,["What protected the Israelites from the tenth and final plague \u2014 the death of the firstborn?",B.afG,u.b6,"God instructed each Israelite family to slaughter a lamb and paint its blood on the top and sides of their doorframes; the destroyer would pass over those homes.","Exodus 12:7, 12:13"],t.M)
B.a5B=A.a(s(["The Feast of Tabernacles","The Feast of Firstfruits","The Feast of Weeks","The Passover"]),t.s)
B.aCI=new A.c(B.l,["What annual feast was established to commemorate the final plague and Israel's deliverance?",B.a5B,"The Passover","God commanded Israel to celebrate Passover every year as a lasting ordinance, commemorating how He passed over their homes when He struck Egypt.","Exodus 12:14"],t.M)
B.anw=A.a(s([B.aD4,B.aBi,B.aEa,B.aAF,B.aEb,B.aBA,B.aCy,B.aFE,B.aFF,B.aCI]),t.J)
B.aIK=new A.c(B.ak,["ten_plagues","The Ten Plagues","Medium",!1,30,6,B.ahs,B.anw],t.M)
B.aTW=new A.c(B.v,["After the death of Egypt's firstborn, Pharaoh finally drove Israel out. But as the Israelites camped by the sea, Pharaoh had a change of heart. He hardened his heart once more and sent his entire army \u2014 600 chariots and all of Egypt's finest horsemen \u2014 to drag Israel back into slavery.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUi=new A.c(B.v,['The people of Israel looked up and saw the Egyptian army bearing down on them. The sea was before them, the army behind them. They cried out in terror against Moses. But Moses declared, "Do not be afraid. Stand firm and you will see the deliverance the Lord will bring you today." God moved the pillar of cloud between the Israelites and the Egyptians through the night.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSw=new A.c(B.v,["God told Moses to stretch out his hand over the sea. A strong east wind blew all night and drove the water back, dividing the sea into two walls of water. The Israelites walked through on dry ground with the water like a wall on their right and their left. When the Egyptians pursued them into the sea, God looked down from the pillar of fire and threw their army into confusion.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSO=new A.c(B.v,["At dawn, Moses stretched his hand out again, and the waters rushed back over the Egyptians \u2014 every chariot, every horseman, every soldier. Not one survived. Israel saw the mighty power God had displayed, and the people feared the Lord and trusted in Him. Moses led all Israel in a great song of praise, and Miriam took up a tambourine and led all the women in dancing.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.akL=A.a(s([B.aTW,B.aUi,B.aSw,B.aSO]),t.o)
B.akR=A.a(s(["He was angry they had taken Egyptian gold",u.bU,"He wanted to make a new peace treaty","He was deceived by his magicians"]),t.s)
B.aGM=new A.c(B.l,["Why did Pharaoh change his mind and chase after the Israelites?",B.akR,u.bU,'When Pharaoh was told that Israel had left, he and his officials changed their minds saying, "What have we done? We have let the Israelites go and have lost their services!"',"Exodus 14:5"],t.M)
B.aqY=A.a(s(["A great mountain","A river that appeared suddenly","A pillar of cloud and fire","An army of angels visible to both sides"]),t.s)
B.aGd=new A.c(B.l,["What stood between the Egyptians and Israelites at night by the sea?",B.aqY,"A pillar of cloud and fire","The angel of God and the pillar of cloud moved from in front of Israel to behind them, coming between the two camps \u2014 giving light to Israel but bringing darkness to Egypt.","Exodus 14:19-20"],t.M)
B.ap4=A.a(s(["Strike the water with his staff","Stretch out his hand over the sea","Blow the trumpet three times","Pour salt into the water"]),t.s)
B.aEi=new A.c(B.l,["What did God tell Moses to do to part the Red Sea?",B.ap4,"Stretch out his hand over the sea","God told Moses to raise his staff and stretch out his hand over the sea to divide the water so the Israelites could walk through it on dry ground.","Exodus 14:16"],t.M)
B.alN=A.a(s(["A supernatural command with no physical cause","A strong east wind that blew all night","An earthquake that split the seabed","The angel of the Lord pushing the water aside"]),t.s)
B.aDc=new A.c(B.l,["What force drove back the waters of the Red Sea?",B.alN,"A strong east wind that blew all night","God drove the sea back with a strong east wind that blew all night, turning the sea into dry land.","Exodus 14:21"],t.M)
B.acM=A.a(s(["Shallow water barely ankle deep","A path of large flat stones","Dry ground","Sand carried there by the wind"]),t.s)
B.aAM=new A.c(B.l,["What did the Israelites walk on when they crossed through the parted Red Sea?",B.acM,"Dry ground","The Israelites went through the sea on dry ground, with the water forming a wall on their right and on their left.","Exodus 14:22"],t.M)
B.aaD=A.a(s(["Immediately when the last Israelite crossed","At midnight","At dawn \u2014 the morning watch","When Moses spoke a prayer"]),t.s)
B.aBx=new A.c(B.l,["When did the waters of the Red Sea return and cover the Egyptian army?",B.aaD,"At dawn \u2014 the morning watch","During the morning watch, God looked down on the Egyptian army and threw them into confusion; Moses stretched out his hand at dawn and the sea returned.","Exodus 14:24-27"],t.M)
B.ame=A.a(s(["They turned back and escaped","They were taken prisoner","They were all drowned","They were blinded and wandered in the desert"]),t.s)
B.aCX=new A.c(B.l,["What happened to the Egyptian army in the Red Sea?",B.ame,"They were all drowned","The water rushed back and covered the chariots and horsemen \u2014 the entire army of Pharaoh that had followed Israel into the sea. Not one of them survived.","Exodus 14:28"],t.M)
B.a8H=A.a(s(["A harp","A lyre","A trumpet","A tambourine \u2014 timbrel"]),t.s)
B.aCg=new A.c(B.l,["What instrument did Miriam play as she led the women in worship after crossing the sea?",B.a8H,"A tambourine \u2014 timbrel","Miriam the prophetess, Aaron's sister, took a tambourine in her hand, and all the women followed her with tambourines and dancing.","Exodus 15:20"],t.M)
B.ahT=A.a(s(["Zipporah, Moses' wife","Jochebed, Moses' mother","Miriam, Moses' sister","The wife of Aaron"]),t.s)
B.aC5=new A.c(B.l,["Who led the women of Israel in song and dancing at the Red Sea?",B.ahT,"Miriam, Moses' sister","Miriam the prophetess, sister of Moses and Aaron, led all the women with tambourines and dancing after the great deliverance at the sea.","Exodus 15:20-21"],t.M)
B.akA=A.a(s(["A call to rebuild the nation",u.x,"A warning to surrounding nations","A promise to return to Egypt"]),t.s)
B.aBB=new A.c(B.l,["What was the central theme of Moses' song after crossing the Red Sea?",B.akA,u.x,'Moses\' song begins "The Lord is my strength and my defense; He has become my salvation" \u2014 a triumphant praise to God for His mighty victory over Egypt.',"Exodus 15:2"],t.M)
B.afC=A.a(s([B.aGM,B.aGd,B.aEi,B.aDc,B.aAM,B.aBx,B.aCX,B.aCg,B.aC5,B.aBB]),t.J)
B.aJh=new A.c(B.ak,["red_sea_crossing","Crossing the Red Sea and the Song of Miriam","Medium",!0,30,6,B.akL,B.afC],t.M)
B.aSL=new A.c(B.v,["Three days after their great victory at the sea, the Israelites found no water. At Marah they found water, but it was too bitter to drink. The people grumbled. God showed Moses a piece of wood; when he threw it into the water, it became sweet. God was testing whether Israel would trust Him and follow His ways.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTH=new A.c(B.v,['In the Desert of Sin, the people grumbled again, longing for Egypt\'s food. God responded with miraculous provision \u2014 quail covered the camp at evening, and in the morning a thin white flaky substance covered the ground like frost. The people asked, "What is it?" \u2014 and Moses told them it was the bread God had given them. They called it manna.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUd=new A.c(B.v,["At Mount Sinai, God spoke directly to Moses and gave Israel the Ten Commandments \u2014 the foundation of His covenant with His people. But while Moses was on the mountain for forty days, the people below grew impatient. They pressured Aaron into making a golden calf and worshipped it, a catastrophic act of idolatry that brought serious judgment.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUb=new A.c(B.v,["From Sinai, Israel journeyed to the border of Canaan. Moses sent twelve spies to explore the land. Ten came back with a fearful report \u2014 the people are giants, we are like grasshoppers! Only Joshua and Caleb urged Israel to trust God and enter. The people's unbelief led to forty years of wandering in the wilderness \u2014 one year for each day the spies had explored the land.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.asm=A.a(s([B.aSL,B.aTH,B.aUd,B.aUb]),t.o)
B.agl=A.a(s(["Moses' staff","Holy ash from the altar","A piece of wood \u2014 a tree","Salt from the desert"]),t.s)
B.aDw=new A.c(B.l,["What did God use to make the bitter water at Marah sweet?",B.agl,"A piece of wood \u2014 a tree","God showed Moses a piece of wood; when Moses threw it into the bitter water, the water became sweet and drinkable.","Exodus 15:25"],t.M)
B.arI=A.a(s(["Yellow like corn","Brown like dried fruit","White like coriander seed","Clear like ice crystals"]),t.s)
B.aH1=new A.c(B.l,["What did manna look like when the Israelites first saw it?",B.arI,"White like coriander seed","Manna was white like coriander seed and tasted like wafers made with honey, appearing on the ground like frost each morning.","Exodus 16:31"],t.M)
B.a7v=A.a(s(["Doves","Partridge","Quail","Wild goats"]),t.s)
B.aGr=new A.c(B.l,["What meat did God provide for the Israelites in the wilderness besides manna?",B.a7v,"Quail","In the evening quail came and covered the camp, and in the morning manna appeared \u2014 God provided both bread and meat for Israel in the desert.","Exodus 16:13"],t.M)
B.asa=A.a(s(["Korah the Levite","Bezalel the craftsman","Aaron, Moses' brother","The elders of Israel"]),t.s)
B.aEW=new A.c(B.l,["Who made the golden calf while Moses was on Mount Sinai?",B.asa,"Aaron, Moses' brother","Aaron gave in to the people's pressure, collected their gold earrings, fashioned them into a golden calf, and declared a festival to the Lord \u2014 a terrible act of idolatry.","Exodus 32:2-5"],t.M)
B.aq1=A.a(s(["Buried it in the desert","Threw it in the sea",u.cJ,"Melted it and used the gold for the tabernacle"]),t.s)
B.aDC=new A.c(B.l,["What did Moses do to the golden calf when he came down from the mountain?",B.aq1,u.cJ,"Moses burned the golden calf in fire, ground it to powder, scattered it on the water, and made the Israelites drink it \u2014 showing the utter worthlessness of their idol.","Exodus 32:20"],t.M)
B.aaS=A.a(s(["Five","Seven","Ten","Twelve"]),t.s)
B.aFV=new A.c(B.l,["How many commandments were written on the stone tablets at Mount Sinai?",B.aaS,"Ten","God wrote the Ten Commandments on two stone tablets, forming the foundation of His covenant with Israel.","Exodus 34:28"],t.M)
B.a4g=A.a(s(["7","10","12","14"]),t.s)
B.aG2=new A.c(B.l,["How many spies did Moses send to explore the land of Canaan?",B.a4g,"12","Moses sent twelve spies \u2014 one leader from each of the twelve tribes of Israel \u2014 to explore the land of Canaan for forty days.","Numbers 13:2"],t.M)
B.amp=A.a(s(["Moses and Aaron","Caleb and Joshua","Shammua and Shaphat","Igal and Palti"]),t.s)
B.aHe=new A.c(B.l,["Which two spies brought back a faithful, encouraging report about entering the Promised Land?",B.amp,"Caleb and Joshua","Caleb and Joshua urged the people to go up and take the land immediately, trusting God \u2014 unlike the other ten spies who spread a fearful report.","Numbers 13:30, Numbers 14:6-9"],t.M)
B.ajI=A.a(s(["Because they worshipped the golden calf","Because they grumbled about the manna",u.fV,"Because Moses disobeyed God at Sinai"]),t.s)
B.aEe=new A.c(B.l,["Why did God sentence Israel to wander in the wilderness for 40 years?",B.ajI,u.fV,"Israel wept and refused to enter Canaan, fearing the powerful inhabitants. God declared they would wander one year for each day the spies explored \u2014 40 years total.","Numbers 14:33-34"],t.M)
B.aba=A.a(s(["Mount Zion","Mount Nebo","Mount Carmel","Mount Sinai"]),t.s)
B.aCM=new A.c(B.l,["Where did Moses receive the Ten Commandments from God?",B.aba,"Mount Sinai","God called Moses up to Mount Sinai where He wrote the Ten Commandments on two stone tablets and gave Israel the Law of the covenant.","Exodus 19:20, Exodus 31:18"],t.M)
B.a63=A.a(s([B.aDw,B.aH1,B.aGr,B.aEW,B.aDC,B.aFV,B.aG2,B.aHe,B.aEe,B.aCM]),t.J)
B.aIS=new A.c(B.ak,["wilderness_wandering","Wandering in the Wilderness","Hard",!0,25,7,B.asm,B.a63],t.M)
B.acu=A.a(s([B.aIF,B.aJf,B.aIK,B.aJh,B.aIS]),t.J)
B.aAf=new A.c(B.e4,["exodus_journey","The Exodus Journey","Experience the epic story of Israel \u2014 from slavery in Egypt, through Moses' calling, the ten plagues, the parting of the Red Sea, to the wilderness journey toward the Promised Land.",B.acu],t.R)
B.aT4=new A.c(B.v,["God had rejected Saul as king of Israel because of his disobedience. He sent the prophet Samuel on a secret mission to the small town of Bethlehem, to the household of a man named Jesse. God had chosen one of Jesse's sons to be the next king \u2014 but He did not choose the way men choose. Where humans look at outward appearance, God looks at the heart.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUe=new A.c(B.v,['Jesse brought seven of his sons before Samuel one by one. Each time Samuel saw a tall, impressive young man, he thought surely this was God\'s anointed \u2014 but God said no to each one. Finally Samuel asked Jesse: "Are these all the sons you have?" Jesse answered that the youngest was out in the fields tending the sheep. David was summoned, and the moment he arrived, God said to Samuel: "Rise and anoint him; this is the one."',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSb=new A.c(B.v,["Samuel took the horn of oil and anointed David in the presence of his brothers, and from that day on the Spirit of the Lord came powerfully upon David. Though anointed king, David did not immediately take the throne. He continued his humble work as a shepherd and became known at the royal court as a skilled musician \u2014 his playing on the harp brought relief to King Saul when an evil spirit tormented him.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.amg=A.a(s([B.aT4,B.aUe,B.aSb]),t.o)
B.ae_=A.a(s(["Nathan the prophet","Elijah","Samuel","Gad the seer"]),t.s)
B.aBR=new A.c(B.l,["Who was sent by God to anoint David as the next king of Israel?",B.ae_,"Samuel","God instructed the prophet Samuel to travel to Bethlehem to the house of Jesse, where God had chosen the next king. Samuel anointed David with oil in the presence of his brothers.","1 Samuel 16:1, 12-13"],t.M)
B.abD=A.a(s(["Hebron","Jerusalem","Bethlehem","Gibeah"]),t.s)
B.aFz=new A.c(B.l,["In which town did Jesse and David's family live?",B.abD,"Bethlehem","Jesse and his family lived in Bethlehem in Judah. Samuel went there to anoint the next king. Bethlehem later became known as the City of David, and is also the birthplace of Jesus Christ.","1 Samuel 16:1, 4"],t.M)
B.apS=A.a(s(["Training as a soldier","Studying the Scriptures with the elders","Tending the sheep in the fields","Preparing a feast for Samuel's arrival"]),t.s)
B.aES=new A.c(B.l,["What was David doing when Samuel came to Jesse's house?",B.apS,"Tending the sheep in the fields","When Samuel asked Jesse if these were all his sons, Jesse replied that the youngest was out tending the sheep. David was summoned from the fields and anointed as king that same day.","1 Samuel 16:11"],t.M)
B.afS=A.a(s(["5","6","7","8"]),t.s)
B.aAu=new A.c(B.l,["How many of Jesse's sons were presented to Samuel before David was called?",B.afS,"7","Jesse presented seven of his sons to Samuel, but God rejected all of them. Only then did Samuel ask if there were any more sons, and David \u2014 the eighth son \u2014 was called from the fields.","1 Samuel 16:10-11"],t.M)
B.a8u=A.a(s(['"He is worthy but not chosen."',u.p,'"He will make a great warrior but not a king."','"He is too proud to lead my people."']),t.s)
B.aBs=new A.c(B.l,["What does God tell Samuel when he saw Jesse's eldest son Eliab and thought he must be God's chosen?",B.a8u,u.p,"God told Samuel not to consider outward appearance or height, because the Lord does not look at the things people look at. People look at the outward appearance, but the Lord looks at the heart.","1 Samuel 16:7"],t.M)
B.a8Y=A.a(s(["Boaz","Jesse","Obed","Salmon"]),t.s)
B.aDG=new A.c(B.l,["What was the name of David's father?",B.a8Y,"Jesse","David was the son of Jesse, an Ephrathite from Bethlehem in Judah. Jesse had eight sons, and David was the youngest. Jesse was the grandson of Boaz and Ruth.","1 Samuel 16:1, Ruth 4:17"],t.M)
B.arx=A.a(s(["The firstborn","The middle son","The second youngest","The youngest"]),t.s)
B.aDO=new A.c(B.l,["Among his brothers, what was David's birth order?",B.arx,"The youngest","David was the youngest of Jesse's eight sons. His older brothers looked down on him, and even his own father did not initially think to call him when Samuel came \u2014 David was considered the least likely candidate.","1 Samuel 16:11, 17:14"],t.M)
B.a6x=A.a(s(["Trumpet","Lyre (harp)","Flute","Cymbals"]),t.s)
B.aFA=new A.c(B.l,["What musical instrument did David play that soothed King Saul?",B.a6x,"Lyre (harp)","David was known as a skilled musician and played the lyre (harp) beautifully. Saul's servants recommended David to the king, and whenever an evil spirit tormented Saul, David would play and relief would come.","1 Samuel 16:16, 23"],t.M)
B.adg=A.a(s(["Tribe of Benjamin","Tribe of Levi","Tribe of Judah","Tribe of Ephraim"]),t.s)
B.aG_=new A.c(B.l,["From which tribe of Israel was David descended?",B.adg,"Tribe of Judah","David was from the tribe of Judah, born in Bethlehem of Judah. This fulfilled the ancient prophecy in Genesis 49:10 that the scepter would not depart from Judah. Jesus Christ was also born from the tribe of Judah and the line of David.","1 Samuel 17:12, Genesis 49:10"],t.M)
B.akw=A.a(s(["He was immediately crowned king in Jerusalem",u.pa,"An angel appeared to him in a vision","He was given the sword of Goliath as a sign"]),t.s)
B.aBo=new A.c(B.l,["What happened to David from the moment he was anointed by Samuel?",B.akw,u.pa,"From the day Samuel anointed David, the Spirit of the Lord came powerfully upon David. This divine empowerment equipped David for the great tasks God had prepared for him, including facing Goliath.","1 Samuel 16:13"],t.M)
B.am6=A.a(s([B.aBR,B.aFz,B.aES,B.aAu,B.aBs,B.aDG,B.aDO,B.aFA,B.aG_,B.aBo]),t.J)
B.aIR=new A.c(B.ak,["shepherd_to_king","From Shepherd to Anointed King","Easy",!1,30,6,B.amg,B.am6],t.M)
B.aU5=new A.c(B.v,["The Philistines gathered their army for war against Israel in the Valley of Elah. Among them was a terrifying champion named Goliath of Gath \u2014 a giant of a man, standing over nine feet tall, dressed head to toe in bronze armor. For forty days, morning and evening, Goliath strode out and bellowed his challenge: send someone to fight me one on one, and the losing side will serve the other.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aU1=new A.c(B.v,["The Israelite army trembled with fear, and no one dared to accept the challenge. David arrived at the camp to bring supplies to his brothers and heard Goliath's taunting. While all the soldiers shrank back in terror, David was outraged that this uncircumcised Philistine was defying the armies of the living God. He volunteered to fight, despite being mocked by his own brothers and doubted by King Saul.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSI=new A.c(B.v,['King Saul offered David his armor and sword, but David tried them on and said he was not used to them. He set them aside and chose his own familiar weapons \u2014 a sling and five smooth stones picked from a stream. As David approached, Goliath sneered and cursed him by his gods. David answered: "You come against me with sword and spear and javelin, but I come against you in the name of the Lord Almighty."',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.ao3=A.a(s([B.aU5,B.aU1,B.aSI]),t.o)
B.afM=A.a(s(["7 days","20 days","40 days","30 days"]),t.s)
B.aB3=new A.c(B.l,["For how many days did Goliath come out and challenge the Israelites before David arrived?",B.afM,"40 days","Goliath came forward every morning and evening for forty days, challenging the Israelites to send a champion to fight him in single combat. The number forty is significant throughout Scripture as a period of testing.","1 Samuel 17:16"],t.M)
B.aaJ=A.a(s(["A sword and shield","Saul's armor and spear","A sling and a stone","A bow and arrow"]),t.s)
B.aFM=new A.c(B.l,["What weapons did David use to fight Goliath?",B.aaJ,"A sling and a stone","David took his shepherd's staff, chose five smooth stones from a stream, and used his sling to fight Goliath. He reached into his bag, took out a stone, and slung it, striking Goliath on the forehead.","1 Samuel 17:40, 49"],t.M)
B.alR=A.a(s(["Amalekite","Moabite","Philistine","Canaanite"]),t.s)
B.aH7=new A.c(B.l,["What was Goliath's nationality?",B.alR,"Philistine","Goliath was from Gath, one of the five principal cities of the Philistines. The Philistines were the primary military enemies of Israel during the period of the judges and the early monarchy.","1 Samuel 17:4"],t.M)
B.a5b=A.a(s(["1","3","5","7"]),t.s)
B.aFZ=new A.c(B.l,["How many smooth stones did David pick up before facing Goliath?",B.a5b,"5","David chose five smooth stones from a stream and put them in the pouch of his shepherd's bag. He only needed one \u2014 but taking five may reflect his readiness to also face Goliath's four brothers, who are mentioned later in Scripture.","1 Samuel 17:40"],t.M)
B.aqI=A.a(s(["His shepherd's staff","A second stone from his sling","Goliath's own sword","A sword given by Saul"]),t.s)
B.aGi=new A.c(B.l,["After Goliath fell, what did David use to kill him and cut off his head?",B.aqI,"Goliath's own sword","David ran to where Goliath had fallen, drew the giant's own sword from its sheath, and cut off his head. David had no sword of his own, so he used Goliath's weapon to finish the battle.","1 Samuel 17:51"],t.M)
B.aow=A.a(s(["6 feet tall","7 feet tall","About 9 feet tall","Over 12 feet tall"]),t.s)
B.aHd=new A.c(B.l,["Approximately how tall was Goliath according to Scripture?",B.aow,"About 9 feet tall",'Goliath\'s height is recorded as "six cubits and a span." Using standard cubit measurements, this translates to approximately 9 feet 9 inches (nearly 3 meters) \u2014 an extraordinary and terrifying height.',"1 Samuel 17:4"],t.M)
B.aiT=A.a(s(["The Valley of Jezreel","The Valley of Elah","The Valley of Aijalon","The Kidron Valley"]),t.s)
B.aCz=new A.c(B.l,["In which valley did the battle between David and Goliath take place?",B.aiT,"The Valley of Elah","The Philistines and Israelites faced each other across the Valley of Elah, with the Philistines on one hill and Israel on another. It was in this valley that David defeated Goliath.","1 Samuel 17:2-3"],t.M)
B.aqR=A.a(s(['"The God of Israel will deliver you into my hand today."',u.gA,'"This day I will avenge the honor of all Israel."','"The battle belongs to the one who has the stronger arm."']),t.s)
B.aFN=new A.c(B.l,["What did David declare as he approached Goliath on the battlefield?",B.aqR,u.gA,'David said to Goliath: "You come against me with sword and spear and javelin, but I come against you in the name of the Lord Almighty, the God of the armies of Israel, whom you have defied." This declaration of faith is one of Scripture\'s most memorable.',"1 Samuel 17:45"],t.M)
B.am2=A.a(s(["A chariot and two horses","His own armor and weapons","Three thousand soldiers as backup","A generous reward and his daughter's hand"]),t.s)
B.aCK=new A.c(B.l,["What did King Saul offer David before sending him to fight Goliath?",B.am2,"His own armor and weapons","Saul dressed David in his own tunic, coat of armor, and bronze helmet, and fastened a sword to him. But David said he could not go in them because he was not used to them, and he took them off.","1 Samuel 17:38-39"],t.M)
B.aqk=A.a(s(["They encouraged him to be brave","They begged him to fight on their behalf",u.cy,"They warned him about Goliath's great strength"]),t.s)
B.aAs=new A.c(B.l,["How did David's brothers react when they heard him asking about Goliath and the reward?",B.aqk,u.cy,"David's eldest brother Eliab heard him talking to the soldiers and burned with anger at David. He accused David of being conceited and wicked, saying he had only come to watch the battle.","1 Samuel 17:28"],t.M)
B.ars=A.a(s([B.aB3,B.aFM,B.aH7,B.aFZ,B.aGi,B.aHd,B.aCz,B.aFN,B.aCK,B.aAs]),t.J)
B.aJ9=new A.c(B.ak,["david_goliath","David and Goliath","Easy",!1,30,6,B.ao3,B.ars],t.M)
B.aTp=new A.c(B.v,["After David's victory over Goliath, a deep and remarkable friendship formed between David and Saul's son Jonathan. Jonathan loved David as himself, and the two made a covenant of friendship. Jonathan gave David his robe, tunic, sword, bow, and belt \u2014 a symbolic act that many scholars see as Jonathan recognizing David's right to the throne that Jonathan himself stood to inherit.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTO=new A.c(B.v,["As David's fame grew, Saul became consumed with jealousy and sought to kill him. Jonathan repeatedly risked his own life to protect David, warning him of his father's murderous intentions. The two devised a signal system using arrows to secretly communicate whether it was safe for David to return. When Jonathan shot the arrows and sent the boy away, David came out of hiding to say goodbye, and the two wept together, knowing they might never meet again.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSM=new A.c(B.v,['Jonathan and his father Saul were both killed in battle against the Philistines at Mount Gilboa. When the news reached David, he mourned deeply and composed the Song of the Bow \u2014 a beautiful lament for both Saul and Jonathan. Of Jonathan, David sang: "Your love for me was wonderful, more wonderful than that of women." This friendship between David and Jonathan became one of the greatest examples of loyal, selfless love in all of Scripture.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aS8=new A.c(B.v,["Years later, when David was established as king, he remembered his covenant with Jonathan and asked: \"Is there anyone still left of the house of Saul to whom I can show kindness for Jonathan's sake?\" He discovered that Jonathan had a son named Mephibosheth, who was crippled in both feet. David brought him to Jerusalem, restored all the land of Saul to him, and had him eat at the royal table always \u2014 as one of the king's own sons.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aor=A.a(s([B.aTp,B.aTO,B.aSM,B.aS8]),t.o)
B.a9P=A.a(s(["David","Samuel","Saul","Abner"]),t.s)
B.aFL=new A.c(B.l,["Who was Jonathan's father?",B.a9P,"Saul","Jonathan was the son of King Saul, the first king of Israel. Despite his father's hatred of David, Jonathan remained David's closest and most loyal friend throughout his life.","1 Samuel 14:1"],t.M)
B.ao_=A.a(s(["His crown and royal signet ring","His robe, tunic, sword, bow, and belt","A scroll containing the law","Fifty servants and three chariots"]),t.s)
B.aFe=new A.c(B.l,["What did Jonathan give David as a sign of their covenant friendship?",B.ao_,"His robe, tunic, sword, bow, and belt","Jonathan took off the robe he was wearing and gave it to David, along with his tunic, sword, bow, and belt. This symbolic gesture showed Jonathan's love and is often interpreted as recognizing David's future kingship.","1 Samuel 18:3-4"],t.M)
B.aga=A.a(s(["Greater than a father's love","More wonderful than the love of women","Equal to the love of a son","Like the love of God for His people"]),t.s)
B.aGw=new A.c(B.l,["How does the Bible describe the depth of Jonathan's love for David?",B.aga,"More wonderful than the love of women",'In his lament over Jonathan\'s death, David said: "I grieve for you, Jonathan my brother; you were very dear to me. Your love for me was wonderful, more wonderful than that of women." This describes the depth of their covenant friendship.',"2 Samuel 1:26"],t.M)
B.akl=A.a(s(["Ishbosheth","Mephibosheth","Merab","Abner"]),t.s)
B.aEv=new A.c(B.l,["What was the name of Jonathan's crippled son whom David later showed kindness to?",B.akl,"Mephibosheth","Mephibosheth was Jonathan's son, who had been dropped by his nurse when he was five years old and became crippled in both feet. King David honored his covenant with Jonathan by showing great kindness to Mephibosheth.","2 Samuel 4:4, 9:6"],t.M)
B.aaY=A.a(s(["By sending a trusted servant with a letter",u.gz,"By leaving a marked stone at their meeting place","By appearing to him in a dream"]),t.s)
B.aH2=new A.c(B.l,["How did Jonathan secretly warn David that his life was in danger from Saul?",B.aaY,u.gz,'Jonathan and David arranged a signal using arrows. Jonathan would shoot arrows and send a boy to retrieve them. If Jonathan shouted "the arrows are on this side of you," it meant safety. If he shouted "the arrows are beyond you," it meant danger and David must flee.',"1 Samuel 20:20-22, 36-38"],t.M)
B.ai6=A.a(s(["Abner","Ishbosheth","Jonathan","Mephibosheth"]),t.s)
B.aBI=new A.c(B.l,["Who was the rightful heir to Saul's throne before David?",B.ai6,"Jonathan","As Saul's eldest son, Jonathan was the natural heir to the throne of Israel. His friendship with David and his recognition of David's anointing meant he voluntarily surrendered his claim, making their friendship all the more remarkable.","1 Samuel 18:1-4, 23:17"],t.M)
B.ac3=A.a(s(["On the plains of Megiddo","At the fortress of Jerusalem","At Mount Gilboa","In the Valley of Elah"]),t.s)
B.aGG=new A.c(B.l,["Where were Saul and Jonathan killed in battle?",B.ac3,"At Mount Gilboa","Saul and his sons, including Jonathan, fell in battle against the Philistines at Mount Gilboa. Saul was badly wounded by archers and fell on his own sword. Jonathan died fighting alongside him.","1 Samuel 31:1-4, 2 Samuel 1:6"],t.M)
B.amQ=A.a(s(["Psalm 23","The Song of the Bow","Psalm 51","A thanksgiving prayer"]),t.s)
B.aFc=new A.c(B.l,["What did David compose when he heard about the deaths of Saul and Jonathan?",B.amQ,"The Song of the Bow","David composed a lament called the Song of the Bow and ordered it to be taught to the people of Judah. It is recorded in 2 Samuel 1 and mourns the deaths of both Saul and Jonathan.","2 Samuel 1:17-18"],t.M)
B.a9S=A.a(s(["A military alliance against the Philistines","A promise that Jonathan would be David's commander",u.gH,"An agreement to share the throne equally"]),t.s)
B.aFn=new A.c(B.l,["What covenant did David and Jonathan make together?",B.a9S,u.gH,"Jonathan and David made a covenant of friendship, and Jonathan made David swear an oath by his love for him. The covenant included showing kindness to each other's families forever, which David later honored with Mephibosheth.","1 Samuel 20:14-17, 42"],t.M)
B.aot=A.a(s(["He named his firstborn son Jonathan","He built a memorial in Jonathan's honor",u.co,"He declared a national day of mourning each year"]),t.s)
B.aCo=new A.c(B.l,["What did David do to honor his covenant with Jonathan after becoming king?",B.aot,u.co,"David restored all the land of Saul to Mephibosheth and commanded that he always eat at the king's table, treating him like one of his own sons. This fulfilled the covenant David had made with Jonathan.","2 Samuel 9:7-13"],t.M)
B.am7=A.a(s([B.aFL,B.aFe,B.aGw,B.aEv,B.aH2,B.aBI,B.aGG,B.aFc,B.aFn,B.aCo]),t.J)
B.aJ5=new A.c(B.ak,["david_and_jonathan","David and Jonathan","Medium",!1,30,6,B.aor,B.am7],t.M)
B.aSl=new A.c(B.v,["After the deaths of Saul and Jonathan, David inquired of the Lord and was told to go up to Hebron, where the men of Judah came and anointed him king over the house of Judah. For seven years and six months David ruled from Hebron while a civil war raged between his supporters and those loyal to Saul's surviving son Ishbosheth. Eventually all the tribes of Israel came to David in Hebron and anointed him king over all Israel.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUx=new A.c(B.v,["David captured the stronghold of Jerusalem from the Jebusites and made it his royal city \u2014 the City of David. He then brought the Ark of the Covenant to Jerusalem in a great celebration, dancing before the Lord with all his might. Jerusalem became not only the political capital of Israel but the spiritual center of the nation, the city where God had chosen to place His name.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUD=new A.c(B.v,["David desired to build a permanent temple for God, but the prophet Nathan brought a message from the Lord: David was a man of war and had shed much blood. Instead, God made an extraordinary covenant with David \u2014 his son would build the temple, and God would establish David's throne forever. This Davidic Covenant became one of the most important promises in all of Scripture, pointing ultimately to Jesus Christ, the eternal Son of David.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aT9=new A.c(B.v,["David's reign was not without failure. His greatest sin came when he committed adultery with Bathsheba and arranged for her husband Uriah to be killed in battle. The prophet Nathan confronted David boldly, and David repented with deep sorrow \u2014 Psalm 51 captures his anguished prayer. Despite his failures, David remained a man after God's own heart, and he reigned over all Israel for forty years, leaving behind a legacy of Psalms, worship, and a kingdom prepared for his son Solomon.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.arn=A.a(s([B.aSl,B.aUx,B.aUD,B.aT9]),t.o)
B.acG=A.a(s(["Jerusalem","Bethlehem","Hebron","Gibeah"]),t.s)
B.aCS=new A.c(B.l,["Where was David first anointed king, before becoming king over all Israel?",B.acG,"Hebron","After Saul's death, David inquired of God and went up to Hebron, where the men of Judah anointed him king over the house of Judah. He reigned there for seven and a half years before becoming king over all Israel.","2 Samuel 2:1-4, 5:5"],t.M)
B.aaO=A.a(s(["The bronze altar from Gibeon","The Ark of the Covenant","The tabernacle of Moses","The stone tablets of the law"]),t.s)
B.aD_=new A.c(B.l,["What sacred object did David bring to Jerusalem in a great procession?",B.aaO,"The Ark of the Covenant","David brought the Ark of the Covenant to Jerusalem with great celebration. He danced before the Lord with all his might, wearing a linen ephod. The Ark represented the presence of God among His people.","2 Samuel 6:12-15"],t.M)
B.aqf=A.a(s(["He was not from the tribe of Levi","He had not received the necessary training",u.jD,"He had failed to keep the Law of Moses"]),t.s)
B.aBu=new A.c(B.l,["Why did God tell David he could not build the temple?",B.aqf,u.jD,"God told David through the prophet Nathan \u2014 and later David himself explains \u2014 that David could not build the temple because he had shed much blood and fought many wars. Instead, God designated David's son Solomon, a man of peace, to build it.","1 Chronicles 22:8, 2 Samuel 7:5-13"],t.M)
B.aem=A.a(s(["Nathan","Solomon","Joab","Absalom"]),t.s)
B.aFD=new A.c(B.l,["Who would build the temple according to God's promise to David?",B.aem,"Solomon",'God promised David that his son Solomon would build the temple. God said: "He is the one who will build a house for my Name, and I will establish the throne of his kingdom forever." Solomon indeed built the magnificent first temple in Jerusalem.',"2 Samuel 7:13, 1 Kings 6:1"],t.M)
B.a6o=A.a(s(["The Proverbs","The Psalms","The Lamentations","The Song of Songs"]),t.s)
B.aFa=new A.c(B.l,["What are the collection of songs and poems David is famous for writing?",B.a6o,"The Psalms",'David wrote approximately half of the 150 Psalms in the Bible, including some of the most beloved \u2014 Psalm 23 ("The Lord is my shepherd"), Psalm 51 (his prayer of repentance), and Psalm 22 (a messianic psalm). He is called the "sweet psalmist of Israel."',"2 Samuel 23:1, Psalm titles"],t.M)
B.aaR=A.a(s(["20 years","33 years","40 years","47 years"]),t.s)
B.aFG=new A.c(B.l,["How many total years did David reign as king of Israel?",B.aaR,"40 years","David reigned for a total of forty years \u2014 seven years and six months in Hebron over Judah, and thirty-three years in Jerusalem over all Israel and Judah.","2 Samuel 5:4-5, 1 Kings 2:11"],t.M)
B.a8T=A.a(s(["Bethlehem","Hebron","Shechem","Jerusalem"]),t.s)
B.aEp=new A.c(B.l,["Which city did David capture from the Jebusites to make his royal capital?",B.a8T,"Jerusalem","David captured the fortress of Zion from the Jebusites \u2014 the stronghold later called the City of David. He made Jerusalem his capital and it became the most important city in Israel's history.","2 Samuel 5:6-9"],t.M)
B.a8R=A.a(s(["Bathsheba","Abigail","Michal","Ahinoam"]),t.s)
B.aD2=new A.c(B.l,["Who was David's first wife?",B.a8R,"Michal","Michal, the daughter of King Saul, was David's first wife. Saul had given her to David after David killed two hundred Philistines as a bride price. She later despised David for dancing before the Ark of the Lord.","1 Samuel 18:27, 2 Samuel 6:16"],t.M)
B.agv=A.a(s(["Samuel","Elijah","Nathan","Gad"]),t.s)
B.aAR=new A.c(B.l,["Which prophet confronted David about his sin with Bathsheba and the murder of Uriah?",B.agv,"Nathan",'The prophet Nathan came to David and told him a parable about a rich man who stole a poor man\'s lamb, then revealed: "You are the man!" David confessed his sin, and Psalm 51 captures his prayer of repentance.',"2 Samuel 12:1-13"],t.M)
B.a9n=A.a(s(["It would last one thousand years","It would be established forever","It would pass only to sons who obeyed the law","It would be the most powerful throne on earth"]),t.s)
B.aGK=new A.c(B.l,["What did God promise about David's throne as part of the Davidic Covenant?",B.a9n,"It would be established forever",'God promised David through Nathan: "Your house and your kingdom will endure forever before me; your throne will be established forever." This Davidic Covenant is fulfilled ultimately in Jesus Christ, who is called the Son of David and reigns eternally.',"2 Samuel 7:16"],t.M)
B.abn=A.a(s([B.aCS,B.aD_,B.aBu,B.aFD,B.aFa,B.aFG,B.aEp,B.aD2,B.aAR,B.aGK]),t.J)
B.aJ7=new A.c(B.ak,["david_king","David Becomes King","Medium",!0,30,6,B.arn,B.abn],t.M)
B.a8W=A.a(s([B.aIR,B.aJ9,B.aJ5,B.aJ7]),t.J)
B.aAn=new A.c(B.e4,["life_of_david","The Life of David","From humble shepherd boy to the greatest king of Israel \u2014 journey through David's life of faith, failure, war, and worship.",B.a8W],t.R)
B.aSs=new A.c(B.v,["Saul of Tarsus was a feared name among early followers of Jesus. Armed with letters of authority from the high priest, he hunted down believers in Jerusalem and beyond, dragging them from their homes and throwing them into prison. His zeal for Jewish law was unmatched, and he saw the followers of 'The Way' as dangerous heretics who had to be silenced.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUy=new A.c(B.v,['As Saul traveled the dusty road to Damascus, intent on arresting more Christians, a light from heaven suddenly blazed around him \u2014 brighter than the midday sun. He fell to the ground, and a voice thundered: "Saul, Saul, why do you persecute me?" Trembling, Saul asked, "Who are you, Lord?" The answer changed everything: "I am Jesus, whom you are persecuting."',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTI=new A.c(B.v,["Saul rose from the ground to find he could not see. His companions led him by the hand into Damascus, where he spent three days without sight, neither eating nor drinking. In the city lived a disciple named Ananias, whom God called in a vision and instructed to find Saul. Though afraid of Saul's reputation, Ananias obeyed, placed his hands on Saul, and said, \"Brother Saul, receive your sight.\" Immediately, something like scales fell from Saul's eyes.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUk=new A.c(B.v,["Filled with the Holy Spirit and restored in sight, Saul was baptized at once. The man who had come to Damascus to arrest Christians now began preaching in the synagogues that Jesus is the Son of God. The transformation was so dramatic that those who heard him were astonished \u2014 this was the same man who had caused such havoc in Jerusalem! From that day forward, Saul \u2014 also known as Paul \u2014 would become the most tireless missionary the church has ever known.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aps=A.a(s([B.aSs,B.aUy,B.aTI,B.aUk]),t.o)
B.aam=A.a(s(["To preach in the synagogues","To arrest followers of Jesus","To meet the high priest","To study under a new teacher"]),t.s)
B.aG6=new A.c(B.l,["What was Saul's original purpose in traveling to Damascus?",B.aam,"To arrest followers of Jesus","Saul traveled to Damascus with letters from the high priest authorizing him to arrest any followers of the Way and bring them back to Jerusalem.","Acts 9:1-2"],t.M)
B.aqJ=A.a(s(["An angel with a sword","A pillar of fire","A blinding light from heaven","A vision of the temple"]),t.s)
B.aFB=new A.c(B.l,["What appeared to Saul on the road to Damascus?",B.aqJ,"A blinding light from heaven","A light from heaven, brighter than the sun, suddenly flashed around Saul, causing him to fall to the ground.","Acts 9:3"],t.M)
B.arO=A.a(s(["1 day","3 days","7 days","40 days"]),t.s)
B.aBT=new A.c(B.l,["How long was Saul blind after his encounter with Jesus?",B.arO,"3 days","Saul was blind for three days, during which time he neither ate nor drank, waiting in Damascus.","Acts 9:9"],t.M)
B.a8P=A.a(s(["Barnabas","Stephen","Peter","Ananias"]),t.s)
B.aCf=new A.c(B.l,["Who did God send to restore Saul's sight?",B.a8P,"Ananias","God appeared to a disciple in Damascus named Ananias in a vision, directing him to go to Saul and lay hands on him so his sight would be restored.","Acts 9:10-12"],t.M)
B.a8O=A.a(s(["Barnabas","Silas","Paul","Timothy"]),t.s)
B.aGc=new A.c(B.l,["What is the other name by which Saul is widely known?",B.a8O,"Paul","Saul of Tarsus was also known by his Roman name Paul, which is predominantly used throughout the book of Acts and his letters.","Acts 13:9"],t.M)
B.acA=A.a(s(["James","Philip","Stephen","Barnabas"]),t.s)
B.aGl=new A.c(B.l,["Saul gave approval to the killing of which early Christian martyr?",B.acA,"Stephen","When Stephen was stoned to death, Saul stood nearby giving his approval and watched over the cloaks of those who stoned him.","Acts 7:58-8:1"],t.M)
B.akH=A.a(s(["Returned to Jerusalem","Was baptized","Wrote a letter to the churches","Preached in the synagogue"]),t.s)
B.aHb=new A.c(B.l,["What did Saul do immediately after his sight was restored by Ananias?",B.akH,"Was baptized","After receiving his sight and being filled with the Holy Spirit, Saul got up and was baptized right away.","Acts 9:18"],t.M)
B.aew=A.a(s(["Nicodemus","Caiaphas","Gamaliel","Annas"]),t.s)
B.aC8=new A.c(B.l,["Under which respected Jewish teacher had Saul been educated?",B.aew,"Gamaliel","Paul himself testified that he was educated under Gamaliel, a highly honored teacher of the law, and was thoroughly trained in the law of the ancestors.","Acts 22:3"],t.M)
B.acE=A.a(s(["Jerusalem","Antioch","Corinth","Tarsus"]),t.s)
B.aEm=new A.c(B.l,["What city was Saul originally from?",B.acE,"Tarsus","Saul was a native of Tarsus in Cilicia, a significant city in what is now southern Turkey.","Acts 9:11"],t.M)
B.acO=A.a(s(["Judah","Levi","Benjamin","Ephraim"]),t.s)
B.aCB=new A.c(B.l,["From which tribe of Israel was Paul descended?",B.acO,"Benjamin","Paul identified himself as a member of the tribe of Benjamin, a Hebrew of Hebrews, and a Pharisee.","Philippians 3:5"],t.M)
B.adF=A.a(s([B.aG6,B.aFB,B.aBT,B.aCf,B.aGc,B.aGl,B.aHb,B.aC8,B.aEm,B.aCB]),t.J)
B.aIP=new A.c(B.ak,["road_to_damascus","The Road to Damascus","Easy",!1,30,6,B.aps,B.adF],t.M)
B.aSt=new A.c(B.v,['In the church at Antioch, while believers worshiped and fasted, the Holy Spirit spoke clearly: "Set apart for me Barnabas and Saul for the work to which I have called them." After prayer and fasting, the community laid hands on them and sent them off. This moment marked the beginning of organized Christian mission \u2014 the church deliberately commissioning and sending out its own to carry the gospel far beyond its walls.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUa=new A.c(B.v,["Paul and Barnabas, accompanied by John Mark as their helper, sailed first to Cyprus \u2014 Barnabas's home island. There they encountered a sorcerer named Bar-Jesus, also called Elymas, who tried to turn the proconsul Sergius Paulus away from the faith. Paul, filled with the Spirit, confronted him sharply, and the man was struck blind. Witnessing this, the proconsul believed, amazed at the teaching about the Lord.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTj=new A.c(B.v,["From Cyprus the missionaries sailed on to Asia Minor, today's Turkey. In Pisidian Antioch, Paul preached powerfully in the synagogue, but Jewish leaders stirred up opposition and expelled them from the region. They pressed on to Iconium, then to Lystra, where they healed a man lame from birth \u2014 and the locals mistook them for gods! But opposition followed, and in Lystra Paul was stoned and left for dead, only to rise and continue his mission.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTm=new A.c(B.v,["After strengthening the disciples and appointing elders in every church they had planted, Paul and Barnabas retraced their steps and sailed back to Antioch in Syria. There they gathered the church together and reported all that God had done through them \u2014 how He had opened a door of faith to the Gentiles. This first journey had proved that the gospel was truly for all nations, not just the Jews.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.abz=A.a(s([B.aSt,B.aUa,B.aTj,B.aTm]),t.o)
B.acF=A.a(s(["Jerusalem","Antioch","Damascus","Rome"]),t.s)
B.aDV=new A.c(B.l,["From which city were Paul and Barnabas officially commissioned for their first journey?",B.acF,"Antioch","The church at Antioch in Syria, directed by the Holy Spirit, set apart Barnabas and Saul and sent them off on their first missionary journey.","Acts 13:1-3"],t.M)
B.agB=A.a(s(["Silas","Timothy","Barnabas","Luke"]),t.s)
B.aCc=new A.c(B.l,["Who was Paul's primary companion on the first missionary journey?",B.agB,"Barnabas","Barnabas was chosen alongside Saul by the Holy Spirit and accompanied him throughout the first missionary journey.","Acts 13:2"],t.M)
B.ac5=A.a(s(["Iconium","Lystra","Derbe","Perga"]),t.s)
B.aBq=new A.c(B.l,["In which city was Paul stoned and left for dead during the first journey?",B.ac5,"Lystra","Jewish opponents from Antioch and Iconium won the crowd over and stoned Paul in Lystra, dragging him outside the city thinking he was dead.","Acts 14:19"],t.M)
B.a9y=A.a(s(["Crete","Malta","Cyprus","Rhodes"]),t.s)
B.aD1=new A.c(B.l,["Which island did Paul and Barnabas visit first on their missionary journey?",B.a9y,"Cyprus","Paul and Barnabas sailed from Seleucia to Cyprus as their first stop, where Barnabas himself was originally from.","Acts 13:4"],t.M)
B.anm=A.a(s(["Planting churches only among Jews","Bringing the gospel to Gentiles","Establishing schools for children","Collecting funds for Jerusalem"]),t.s)
B.aAt=new A.c(B.l,["What was a key distinguishing focus of Paul's first missionary journey?",B.anm,"Bringing the gospel to Gentiles","A significant outcome of the first journey was reaching Gentiles, which Paul and Barnabas reported to the Antioch church upon returning.","Acts 14:27"],t.M)
B.amJ=A.a(s(["A hostile synagogue leader","A young helper who later left the team","The proconsul of Cyprus","A Gentile convert from Lystra"]),t.s)
B.aBp=new A.c(B.l,["Who was John Mark in relation to the first missionary journey?",B.amJ,"A young helper who later left the team","John Mark joined Paul and Barnabas as a helper but departed from them at Pamphylia and did not continue with them to the work.","Acts 13:5, 13"],t.M)
B.abO=A.a(s(["Simon Magus","Elymas","Demetrius","Alexander"]),t.s)
B.aG3=new A.c(B.l,["What was the name of the sorcerer who opposed Paul on the island of Cyprus?",B.abO,"Elymas","Elymas, also called Bar-Jesus, was a Jewish sorcerer and false prophet who tried to turn the proconsul Sergius Paulus away from the faith.","Acts 13:8"],t.M)
B.afW=A.a(s(["He was imprisoned","He was struck blind","He repented and was baptized","He fled the island"]),t.s)
B.aEs=new A.c(B.l,["What happened to Elymas the sorcerer after Paul confronted him?",B.afW,"He was struck blind","Paul declared that the hand of the Lord was against Elymas, and immediately mist and darkness came over him and he groped around for someone to lead him.","Acts 13:11"],t.M)
B.aiE=A.a(s(["Ephesus","Corinth","Pisidian Antioch","Thessalonica"]),t.s)
B.aGk=new A.c(B.l,["Which city did Paul and Barnabas travel to after leaving Cyprus on the mainland?",B.aiE,"Pisidian Antioch","After Cyprus, Paul and his companions sailed to Perga and then traveled on to Pisidian Antioch, where Paul preached in the synagogue.","Acts 13:14"],t.M)
B.amb=A.a(s(["That they had collected a great offering for the poor",u.cU,"That the Roman emperor had become favorable to Christians","That all of Asia Minor had been baptized"]),t.s)
B.aGO=new A.c(B.l,["What did Paul and Barnabas report to the church in Antioch upon returning?",B.amb,u.cU,"On their return, Paul and Barnabas gathered the church and reported all that God had done through them, especially how He had opened the door of faith to the Gentiles.","Acts 14:27"],t.M)
B.ap0=A.a(s([B.aDV,B.aCc,B.aBq,B.aD1,B.aAt,B.aBp,B.aG3,B.aEs,B.aGk,B.aGO]),t.J)
B.aIO=new A.c(B.ak,["first_journey","Paul's First Missionary Journey","Medium",!1,30,6,B.abz,B.ap0],t.M)
B.aUj=new A.c(B.v,["After the Jerusalem Council settled the question of Gentile salvation, Paul proposed returning to visit the churches from the first journey. When Paul and Barnabas sharply disagreed over taking John Mark again, they parted ways. Paul chose Silas as his new partner, and they set off through Syria and Cilicia. In Lystra they met a young disciple named Timothy, whose reputation was excellent. Paul wanted Timothy to join them, and Timothy became one of Paul's most trusted companions.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTV=new A.c(B.v,['The Spirit of Jesus prevented Paul from entering Asia or Bithynia, redirecting the team to Troas on the Aegean coast. There, in a night vision, Paul saw a man from Macedonia calling out, "Come over to Macedonia and help us!" Immediately the team concluded that God was calling them to preach the gospel in Europe. They crossed the sea and arrived at Philippi \u2014 a Roman colony and the leading city of Macedonia.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUw=new A.c(B.v,['In Philippi, by a riverside, they met Lydia \u2014 a dealer in purple cloth \u2014 whose heart the Lord opened, and she and her household were baptized. But trouble came: after Paul cast a spirit out of a slave girl, her owners had Paul and Silas beaten and thrown into prison. At midnight, the missionaries prayed and sang hymns. Suddenly a great earthquake shook the prison foundations, every door flew open, and the chains fell off every prisoner. The terrified jailer, thinking the prisoners had escaped, was about to kill himself when Paul cried out, "We are all here!"',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aU7=new A.c(B.v,['The jailer rushed in trembling and asked Paul and Silas, "What must I do to be saved?" They replied, "Believe in the Lord Jesus, and you will be saved \u2014 you and your household." The jailer and his family were baptized that same night. From Philippi, Paul preached through Thessalonica, Berea, Athens \u2014 where he saw an altar inscribed "To an Unknown God" \u2014 and finally settled in Corinth for eighteen months, where he met fellow tentmakers Aquila and Priscilla.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.adJ=A.a(s([B.aUj,B.aTV,B.aUw,B.aU7]),t.o)
B.a8Q=A.a(s(["Barnabas","Timothy","Silas","Luke"]),t.s)
B.aGt=new A.c(B.l,["Who was Paul's main traveling companion on the second missionary journey?",B.a8Q,"Silas","After the disagreement with Barnabas over John Mark, Paul chose Silas as his new companion and they left Antioch together.","Acts 15:40"],t.M)
B.a8m=A.a(s(["Antioch","Philippi","Lystra","Derbe"]),t.s)
B.aDs=new A.c(B.l,["In which city did Timothy join Paul's missionary team?",B.a8m,"Lystra","Timothy, a disciple well spoken of by the believers in Lystra and Iconium, joined Paul when the team came through Lystra.","Acts 16:1-3"],t.M)
B.ad8=A.a(s(["An angel standing over the Aegean Sea","A man from Macedonia pleading for help","A vision of the Roman Emperor welcoming him","A burning bush on the coast of Troas"]),t.s)
B.aEC=new A.c(B.l,["What vision directed Paul to go to Macedonia?",B.ad8,"A man from Macedonia pleading for help",'During the night Paul had a vision of a man from Macedonia standing and begging him, "Come over to Macedonia and help us."',"Acts 16:9"],t.M)
B.aqO=A.a(s(["Athens","Corinth","Thessalonica","Philippi"]),t.s)
B.aCs=new A.c(B.l,["What was the first European city Paul preached in during the second journey?",B.aqO,"Philippi","After crossing from Troas to Macedonia, Paul's team went to Philippi, a leading city of the district of Macedonia and a Roman colony.","Acts 16:12"],t.M)
B.acd=A.a(s(["A weaver of fine linen","A seller of purple cloth","A potter who made jars","A baker in the marketplace"]),t.s)
B.aCt=new A.c(B.l,["What was the occupation of Lydia, the first recorded European convert?",B.acd,"A seller of purple cloth","Lydia was from the city of Thyatira and was a dealer in purple cloth. The Lord opened her heart to respond to Paul's message.","Acts 16:14"],t.M)
B.akQ=A.a(s(["An angel appeared and carried them out",u.hS,"The prison walls turned to water","A great fire consumed the chains"]),t.s)
B.aEf=new A.c(B.l,["What miraculous event occurred while Paul and Silas were in the Philippian prison?",B.akQ,u.hS,"About midnight, while Paul and Silas were praying and singing, a violent earthquake shook the prison foundations, all the doors flew open, and everyone's chains came loose.","Acts 16:26"],t.M)
B.acR=A.a(s(["A statue of Caesar calling himself god",u.lK,"A temple where Christians were secretly meeting","A marketplace where all idols had been destroyed"]),t.s)
B.aBE=new A.c(B.l,["What unusual thing did Paul observe in Athens?",B.acR,u.lK,'While walking around Athens, Paul found an altar with the inscription "To an Unknown God," which he used as a starting point to preach about Jesus.',"Acts 17:23"],t.M)
B.adE=A.a(s(["3 months","6 months","18 months","3 years"]),t.s)
B.aBv=new A.c(B.l,["How long did Paul remain in Corinth on his second journey?",B.adE,"18 months","Paul stayed in Corinth for a year and a half, teaching the word of God among the people there.","Acts 18:11"],t.M)
B.agH=A.a(s(["They were all from Tarsus","They were all tentmakers","They had all studied under Gamaliel","They had all been imprisoned for their faith"]),t.s)
B.aG9=new A.c(B.l,["What did Paul have in common with Aquila and Priscilla that led to their close friendship?",B.agH,"They were all tentmakers","Because he was a tentmaker as they were, Paul stayed and worked with Aquila and Priscilla in Corinth.","Acts 18:3"],t.M)
B.alA=A.a(s(["Barnabas wanted to go to Rome instead",u.gP,"The Jerusalem Council assigned them different regions","Barnabas fell ill and could not travel"]),t.s)
B.aAz=new A.c(B.l,["Why did Paul and Barnabas separate before the second journey began?",B.alA,u.gP,"Barnabas wanted to take John Mark, but Paul did not think it wise to take someone who had deserted them on the first journey, causing such a sharp disagreement that they parted.","Acts 15:37-39"],t.M)
B.agU=A.a(s([B.aGt,B.aDs,B.aEC,B.aCs,B.aCt,B.aEf,B.aBE,B.aBv,B.aG9,B.aAz]),t.J)
B.aIJ=new A.c(B.ak,["second_journey","Paul's Second Missionary Journey","Medium",!0,30,6,B.adJ,B.agU],t.M)
B.aT1=new A.c(B.v,["Paul's third journey took him to Ephesus, the great commercial city on the Aegean coast, where he stayed longer than anywhere else in his travels. For about three years he taught daily in the lecture hall of Tyrannus, so that all the Jews and Greeks in the province of Asia heard the word of the Lord. His ministry was accompanied by extraordinary miracles \u2014 even handkerchiefs and aprons that had touched him were brought to the sick and they were healed.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTX=new A.c(B.v,['Ephesus was home to the magnificent temple of Artemis, one of the seven wonders of the ancient world. A silversmith named Demetrius, who made silver shrines of Artemis, gathered his fellow craftsmen and stirred up a riot. "This Paul has persuaded large numbers of people that man-made gods are no gods at all," he cried. His real concern was financial \u2014 the gospel was costing him business. The city erupted into uproar, with crowds shouting "Great is Artemis of the Ephesians!" for two solid hours.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUr=new A.c(B.v,["After the riot settled, Paul traveled through Macedonia and Greece before making his way back to Jerusalem. In Troas, during a long farewell gathering that stretched past midnight, a young man named Eutychus fell asleep in a third-story window and plunged to his death. Paul went down, threw himself on the young man, and embraced him \u2014 and life returned to him. The community was overjoyed and greatly comforted.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSv=new A.c(B.v,['In Miletus, Paul called the elders of the Ephesian church to meet him for a final farewell. With great emotion he reminded them of his faithful service among them and warned that after his departure, savage wolves would come and distort the truth. "I consider my life worth nothing to me," he declared, "my only aim is to finish the race and complete the task the Lord Jesus has given me." He knelt and prayed with them all, and there was much weeping.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.akS=A.a(s([B.aT1,B.aTX,B.aUr,B.aSv]),t.o)
B.arT=A.a(s(["6 months","1 year","About 3 years","5 years"]),t.s)
B.aBw=new A.c(B.l,["Approximately how long did Paul stay and minister in Ephesus?",B.arT,"About 3 years","Paul spent approximately three years in Ephesus, longer than any other city in his travels, teaching in the hall of Tyrannus so the whole province of Asia heard the gospel.","Acts 20:31"],t.M)
B.anK=A.a(s(["The high priest's messenger","Demetrius the silversmith","Alexander the metalworker","The city treasurer"]),t.s)
B.aGx=new A.c(B.l,["Who instigated the riot against Paul in Ephesus?",B.anK,"Demetrius the silversmith","Demetrius, a silversmith who made silver shrines of Artemis, gathered his fellow craftsmen and stirred up a riot against Paul.","Acts 19:24"],t.M)
B.afP=A.a(s(["Paul had desecrated the temple of Artemis",u.k4,"Paul had healed a rival of Demetrius","Paul refused to pay the required temple tax"]),t.s)
B.aE6=new A.c(B.l,["What was the underlying reason for the riot in Ephesus?",B.afP,u.k4,"Demetrius warned that Paul's teaching that man-made gods are not gods had persuaded many, which was threatening their trade in Artemis shrines.","Acts 19:26-27"],t.M)
B.a69=A.a(s(["Trophimus","Tychicus","Eutychus","Epaphras"]),t.s)
B.aAA=new A.c(B.l,["Who fell from a window during Paul's long night meeting in Troas?",B.a69,"Eutychus","A young man named Eutychus, who was sitting in a window, sank into a deep sleep as Paul talked on and fell from the third floor.","Acts 20:9"],t.M)
B.an6=A.a(s(["He was badly injured but survived","He remained in a coma for three days","Paul raised him from the dead","He was healed after the congregation prayed"]),t.s)
B.aBM=new A.c(B.l,["What happened to Eutychus after he fell from the window?",B.an6,"Paul raised him from the dead","Eutychus was picked up dead, but Paul went down, threw himself on him, and announced that life was in him \u2014 he was raised.","Acts 20:10"],t.M)
B.a6y=A.a(s(["All the believers in Macedonia","The seven churches of Asia","The elders of the church in Ephesus","His co-workers Silas and Timothy"]),t.s)
B.aCW=new A.c(B.l,["Who did Paul summon to Miletus for a final farewell address?",B.a6y,"The elders of the church in Ephesus","From Miletus, Paul sent to Ephesus and called for the elders of the church, delivering to them his heartfelt farewell speech.","Acts 20:17"],t.M)
B.acg=A.a(s(["Roman soldiers would arrest them all",u.ak,"A great earthquake would destroy Ephesus","Famine would drive them away from the city"]),t.s)
B.aBf=new A.c(B.l,["What danger did Paul warn the Ephesian elders would come after his departure?",B.acg,u.ak,"Paul warned that after he left, savage wolves would come in among them and not spare the flock, and even from among their own number people would arise and distort the truth.","Acts 20:29-30"],t.M)
B.ap1=A.a(s([u.i,"He hoped to live long enough to see Rome","He wished he could stay in Ephesus forever","He believed he would escape all harm"]),t.s)
B.aGb=new A.c(B.l,["What did Paul say about his own life in his farewell speech at Miletus?",B.ap1,u.i,"Paul declared that he considered his life worth nothing to himself, as his only aim was to finish the race and complete the task of testifying to the gospel of God's grace.","Acts 20:24"],t.M)
B.ahH=A.a(s(["Galatians","Romans","1 Corinthians","Colossians"]),t.s)
B.aBD=new A.c(B.l,["Which of Paul's letters was written from Ephesus during the third journey?",B.ahH,"1 Corinthians","Paul wrote 1 Corinthians while in Ephesus, mentioning that he planned to stay there until Pentecost.","1 Corinthians 16:8"],t.M)
B.a6z=A.a(s(["Carpentry","Tentmaking","Fishing","Pottery"]),t.s)
B.aAy=new A.c(B.l,["What trade did Paul practice to support himself during his missionary work?",B.a6z,"Tentmaking","Paul was a tentmaker by trade and used this skill to earn his own living rather than being a burden to the churches he served.","Acts 18:3"],t.M)
B.aeM=A.a(s([B.aBw,B.aGx,B.aE6,B.aAA,B.aBM,B.aCW,B.aBf,B.aGb,B.aBD,B.aAy]),t.J)
B.aIY=new A.c(B.ak,["third_journey","Paul's Third Missionary Journey","Hard",!0,25,7,B.akS,B.aeM],t.M)
B.aTo=new A.c(B.v,['Paul\'s return to Jerusalem ended in arrest. A mob seized him in the temple, accusing him of defiling the holy place. Roman soldiers rescued him from the crowd, but he remained under Roman custody. He was transferred to Caesarea, where he stood before Governor Felix, then Festus, and finally King Agrippa \u2014 each time defending his faith and his encounter with the risen Jesus. Before Agrippa, Paul made such a powerful case that the king replied, "Do you think that in such a short time you can persuade me to be a Christian?"',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTu=new A.c(B.v,["To secure a fair hearing and escape Jewish plots, Paul exercised his right as a Roman citizen and appealed to Caesar. This meant a voyage to Rome. The journey was treacherous \u2014 a massive storm battered the ship for two weeks. An angel assured Paul that he must stand before Caesar and that God had granted the lives of all 276 people on board. The ship ran aground near the island of Malta and broke apart, but every person reached shore safely, just as God had promised.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUA=new A.c(B.v,["On Malta, the islanders showed extraordinary kindness. As Paul gathered firewood, a viper fastened itself to his hand. The locals expected him to swell up and die, but Paul simply shook the snake off into the fire and suffered no ill effects. They changed their minds and said he was a god. Paul also healed the father of the leading official on the island, and the rest of the sick on Malta came and were healed.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aS5=new A.c(B.v,["Paul eventually reached Rome and lived there under house arrest for two years, welcoming all who came to him and boldly preaching the kingdom of God. During this time of imprisonment he wrote letters full of joy and deep theology \u2014 to the Philippians, Ephesians, Colossians, and to Philemon \u2014 letters that would shape Christian thought for centuries. From a prison cell, the man who had once imprisoned Christians wrote of contentment, peace, and the surpassing greatness of knowing Christ Jesus.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aso=A.a(s([B.aTo,B.aTu,B.aUA,B.aS5]),t.o)
B.ah5=A.a(s(["Timothy","Barnabas","Silas","Luke"]),t.s)
B.aAx=new A.c(B.l,["Who was Paul's companion who was with him when they were imprisoned in Philippi?",B.ah5,"Silas","Silas was imprisoned alongside Paul in Philippi after they cast a fortune-telling spirit out of a slave girl.","Acts 16:25"],t.M)
B.afB=A.a(s(["Sleeping soundly despite their chains","Praying and singing hymns to God","Writing letters to the churches","Planning their escape route"]),t.s)
B.aD3=new A.c(B.l,["What were Paul and Silas doing at midnight while in the Philippian jail?",B.afB,"Praying and singing hymns to God","About midnight Paul and Silas were praying and singing hymns to God, and the other prisoners were listening to them.","Acts 16:25"],t.M)
B.ant=A.a(s(["A fire destroyed the prison walls",u.M,"An angel appeared and led them out","A flood filled the prison and washed away the bars"]),t.s)
B.aBr=new A.c(B.l,["What happened in the Philippian prison that led to the jailer's conversion?",B.ant,u.M,"A violent earthquake shook the foundations of the prison, all the doors flew open, and everyone's chains came loose.","Acts 16:26"],t.M)
B.a4I=A.a(s(["Who gave you the power to do these miracles?","What must I do to be saved?","Will you heal my family as you have healed others?","How can I join your missionary team?"]),t.s)
B.aC2=new A.c(B.l,["What question did the Philippian jailer ask Paul and Silas?",B.a4I,"What must I do to be saved?",'The terrified jailer fell trembling before Paul and Silas and asked, "Sirs, what must I do to be saved?"',"Acts 16:30"],t.M)
B.aa2=A.a(s(["1 Corinthians","Galatians","Philippians","1 Thessalonians"]),t.s)
B.aEl=new A.c(B.l,['Which of the following is one of Paul\'s "prison epistles" written during his Roman imprisonment?',B.aa2,"Philippians",'Philippians is one of the four "prison epistles" Paul wrote during his Roman imprisonment, along with Ephesians, Colossians, and Philemon.',"Philippians 1:13"],t.M)
B.a9B=A.a(s(["Cyprus","Crete","Malta","Rhodes"]),t.s)
B.aGI=new A.c(B.l,["On which island was Paul shipwrecked while sailing to Rome?",B.a9B,"Malta","After the ship ran aground and broke apart in a storm, Paul and all 276 people on board reached the shore of the island of Malta.","Acts 28:1"],t.M)
B.asi=A.a(s(["A scorpion","A viper","A wild dog","A hornet"]),t.s)
B.aAJ=new A.c(B.l,["What creature attacked Paul on the island of Malta?",B.asi,"A viper","As Paul gathered wood for a fire on Malta, a viper driven out by the heat fastened itself on his hand, but he shook it into the fire and suffered no ill effects.","Acts 28:3"],t.M)
B.aaP=A.a(s(["Felix","Festus","Agrippa","Herod"]),t.s)
B.aBL=new A.c(B.l,['Before which king did Paul say "You are almost persuading me to become a Christian" was directed back at Paul?',B.aaP,"Agrippa",'After hearing Paul\'s defense, King Agrippa said, "Do you think that in such a short time you can persuade me to be a Christian?" to which Paul replied he wished Agrippa and all present could become what he was.',"Acts 26:28"],t.M)
B.aou=A.a(s(["He bribed the governor Felix","He appealed to Caesar as a Roman citizen","The Jerusalem church sent him as an ambassador","A Roman commander ordered him to Rome"]),t.s)
B.aFI=new A.c(B.l,["How did Paul secure his transfer from Jerusalem to Rome for trial?",B.aou,"He appealed to Caesar as a Roman citizen","Paul exercised his right as a Roman citizen by appealing to Caesar, which meant his case had to be heard in Rome.","Acts 25:11"],t.M)
B.afV=A.a(s(["Contentment is a gift only given to the apostles",u.j5,"True contentment is found only in earthly peace","Contentment comes from having all your needs met"]),t.s)
B.aAH=new A.c(B.l,["What did Paul write about contentment in his letter to the Philippians?",B.afV,u.j5,"Paul wrote that he had learned the secret of contentment \u2014 to be content in all circumstances, whether in need or in plenty.","Philippians 4:11"],t.M)
B.afA=A.a(s([B.aAx,B.aD3,B.aBr,B.aC2,B.aEl,B.aGI,B.aAJ,B.aBL,B.aFI,B.aAH]),t.J)
B.aIT=new A.c(B.ak,["paul_in_prison","Paul in Prison","Hard",!0,25,7,B.aso,B.afA],t.M)
