B.aIX=new A.c(B.ak,["joseph_dreamer","The Dreamer","Easy",!1,30,6,B.aft,B.aeJ],t.M)
B.aUm=new A.c(B.v,["Joseph arrived in Egypt as a slave and was sold to Potiphar, one of Pharaoh's officials \u2014 the captain of the guard. Yet the hand of God was unmistakably on Joseph. Everything he touched prospered. Potiphar noticed that the Lord was with Joseph and that the Lord gave him success in everything he did. Potiphar's trust grew until he made Joseph overseer of his entire household, putting everything he owned into Joseph's care.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSZ=new A.c(B.v,['Joseph was well-built and handsome, and Potiphar\'s wife began to take notice. Day after day she pressured Joseph, "Come to bed with me!" Day after day Joseph refused. "How could I do this wicked thing and sin against God?" he asked. One day, when no one else was in the house, she grabbed his cloak and demanded again. Joseph fled, leaving his cloak in her hand. Furious and humiliated, she used the cloak as evidence and falsely accused Joseph of attacking her.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSN=new A.c(B.v,["Potiphar's anger burned and he had Joseph thrown into prison \u2014 the place where the king's prisoners were confined. Yet even there, the Lord was with Joseph and showed him kindness. The prison warden put Joseph in charge of all the other prisoners. Two of Pharaoh's officials \u2014 the chief cupbearer and the chief baker \u2014 were thrown into the same prison, and Joseph was assigned to attend to them.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTe=new A.c(B.v,['One morning Joseph noticed the two officials looking dejected and asked them why. "We each had a dream last night," they said, "and there is no one to interpret it." Joseph replied, "Do not interpretations belong to God? Tell me your dreams." He interpreted the cupbearer\'s dream as meaning he would be restored to his position in three days, and the baker\'s dream as meaning he would be executed. Both came true exactly as Joseph had said \u2014 but the cupbearer, restored to his place, promptly forgot all about Joseph for two full years.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.arm=A.a(s([B.aUm,B.aSZ,B.aSN,B.aTe]),t.o)
B.abY=A.a(s(["Pharaoh's chief advisor","Potiphar","The temple priest of Amun","A merchant in the marketplace"]),t.s)
B.aBY=new A.c(B.l,["To whom was Joseph sold when he arrived in Egypt?",B.abY,"Potiphar","Joseph was sold to Potiphar, one of Pharaoh's officials, by the Ishmaelite traders who had bought him from his brothers.","Genesis 39:1"],t.M)
B.as7=A.a(s(["Pharaoh's chief treasurer","Captain of Pharaoh's guard","Head of the royal stables","Chief judge of Egypt"]),t.s)
B.aAN=new A.c(B.l,["What was Potiphar's official role?",B.as7,"Captain of Pharaoh's guard","Potiphar was an Egyptian who served as one of Pharaoh's officials and the captain of the guard.","Genesis 39:1"],t.M)
B.ajJ=A.a(s(["He had been educated in all the wisdom of Egypt",u.dc,"Potiphar paid him well and he worked hard","He had natural talent for management"]),t.s)
B.aEu=new A.c(B.l,["Why did Joseph succeed in everything he did in Potiphar's house?",B.ajJ,u.dc,"Scripture repeatedly emphasizes that the key to Joseph's success was that the Lord was with him and gave him success in whatever he did.","Genesis 39:3"],t.M)
B.ahq=A.a(s(["Potiphar himself, out of jealousy","Potiphar's wife","A jealous fellow servant","The chief baker"]),t.s)
B.aBO=new A.c(B.l,["Who falsely accused Joseph and had him imprisoned?",B.ahq,"Potiphar's wife","Potiphar's wife, after Joseph repeatedly refused her advances, falsely accused him of attacking her using his cloak as false evidence.","Genesis 39:14-18"],t.M)
B.ama=A.a(s(["He was sent back to Canaan","He was sent to work in the mines","He was put in the royal prison","He was sold to another household"]),t.s)
B.aEA=new A.c(B.l,["Where was Joseph sent after being falsely accused?",B.ama,"He was put in the royal prison","Joseph was thrown into the prison where the king's prisoners were confined, but even there the Lord was with him.","Genesis 39:20"],t.M)
B.apa=A.a(s(["He guarded the outer gate",u.gm,"He served as the warden's personal scribe","He worked in the prison kitchen"]),t.s)
B.aCZ=new A.c(B.l,["What role did Joseph come to have in the prison?",B.apa,u.gm,"The prison warden put Joseph in charge of all those held in the prison, and the warden paid no attention to anything under Joseph's care because the Lord was with Joseph.","Genesis 39:22"],t.M)
B.a7Y=A.a(s(["Pharaoh's dreams about cattle and grain","The prison warden's recurring nightmares",u.ai,"His own prophetic dreams about the future"]),t.s)
B.aGJ=new A.c(B.l,["Whose dreams did Joseph interpret while he was in prison?",B.a7Y,u.ai,"Two of Pharaoh's officials \u2014 the chief cupbearer and the chief baker \u2014 were imprisoned and each had a dream on the same night that Joseph interpreted.","Genesis 40:5-8"],t.M)
B.alW=A.a(s(["He was executed","He remained in prison indefinitely",u.fK,"He was sent as a slave to another country"]),t.s)
B.aFQ=new A.c(B.l,["What happened to the chief cupbearer after Joseph interpreted his dream?",B.alW,u.fK,"Just as Joseph had interpreted, within three days Pharaoh restored the chief cupbearer to his position and he once again put the cup in Pharaoh's hand.","Genesis 40:21"],t.M)
B.aak=A.a(s(["He was released and returned to his hometown","He was given a promotion in the palace","He was executed","He remained in prison for years"]),t.s)
B.aE9=new A.c(B.l,["What happened to the chief baker after Joseph interpreted his dream?",B.aak,"He was executed","Joseph interpreted the baker's dream as meaning he would be hanged within three days, and this came true exactly as predicted.","Genesis 40:22"],t.M)
B.arw=A.a(s(["3 months","1 year","2 years","7 years"]),t.s)
B.aH_=new A.c(B.l,["How long did the chief cupbearer forget about Joseph after being restored?",B.arw,"2 years","The chief cupbearer did not remember Joseph and forgot him entirely for two full years, until Pharaoh had his disturbing dreams.","Genesis 41:1"],t.M)
B.a6K=A.a(s([B.aBY,B.aAN,B.aEu,B.aBO,B.aEA,B.aCZ,B.aGJ,B.aFQ,B.aE9,B.aH_]),t.J)
B.aIZ=new A.c(B.ak,["joseph_slavery","Sold into Slavery","Medium",!1,30,6,B.arm,B.a6K],t.M)
B.aU_=new A.c(B.v,['Two years after the cupbearer\'s restoration, Pharaoh had two deeply troubling dreams that no one in all of Egypt could interpret. The cupbearer finally remembered Joseph and told Pharaoh about the dream interpreter in the prison. Joseph was quickly brought before Pharaoh \u2014 he shaved, changed his clothes, and stood before the most powerful man on earth. "I cannot interpret dreams," Joseph said humbly, "but God will give Pharaoh the answer he desires."',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aRZ=new A.c(B.v,["Pharaoh described his dreams: seven fat, healthy cows devoured by seven ugly, gaunt cows \u2014 and still the thin ones looked just as they had before. Then seven full, healthy heads of grain were swallowed up by seven thin, scorched heads. Joseph explained that the two dreams were one message from God: seven years of great abundance would come throughout Egypt, followed by seven years of severe famine that would wipe out all the abundance. The famine would be so devastating that the plenty would be forgotten.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUf=new A.c(B.v,['Joseph advised Pharaoh to appoint a wise man to oversee a massive grain storage operation during the years of plenty. Pharaoh turned to his officials and said, "Can we find anyone like this man, one in whom is the spirit of God?" He said to Joseph: "Since God has made all this known to you, there is no one so discerning and wise as you. You shall be in charge of my palace, and all my people are to submit to your orders." Pharaoh placed his own signet ring on Joseph\'s finger, dressed him in fine linen, and put a gold chain around his neck.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aT8=new A.c(B.v,['Joseph was thirty years old when he entered Pharaoh\'s service. He was given an Egyptian name \u2014 Zaphenath-Paneah \u2014 and an Egyptian wife, Asenath. During the seven years of abundance, Joseph collected enormous quantities of grain and stored it throughout Egypt. Two sons were born to him: he named the firstborn Manasseh, saying "God has made me forget all my trouble," and the second Ephraim, saying "God has made me fruitful in the land of my suffering."',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aec=A.a(s([B.aU_,B.aRZ,B.aUf,B.aT8]),t.o)
B.aaN=A.a(s(["Seven stars falling from the sky","Seven fat cows eaten by seven thin cows","Seven jars of grain spilling onto the Nile","Seven priests bowing before a foreign god"]),t.s)
B.aD6=new A.c(B.l,["What did Pharaoh see in his first dream?",B.aaN,"Seven fat cows eaten by seven thin cows","In the first dream, Pharaoh saw seven sleek, fat cows come up from the Nile, followed by seven ugly, gaunt cows that devoured the fat ones.","Genesis 41:2-4"],t.M)
B.a6U=A.a(s(["Seven lampstands being extinguished by wind","A great river drying up completely",u.nH,"Seven mountains crumbling into the sea"]),t.s)
B.aGo=new A.c(B.l,["What did Pharaoh's second dream involve?",B.a6U,u.nH,"In the second dream, seven full, healthy heads of grain grew on a single stalk but were swallowed up by seven thin, scorched heads.","Genesis 41:5-7"],t.M)
B.aoI=A.a(s(["Egypt would conquer its enemies, then face a revolt","The Nile would flood for seven years, then dry up",u.ir,"Seven pharaohs would rule before Egypt was destroyed"]),t.s)
B.aBC=new A.c(B.l,["What did Joseph say Pharaoh's two dreams meant?",B.aoI,u.ir,"Joseph explained that both dreams carried one message: God was showing Pharaoh what He was about to do \u2014 seven years of great abundance throughout Egypt, followed by seven years of severe famine.","Genesis 41:28-30"],t.M)
B.a9d=A.a(s(["25","28","30","35"]),t.s)
B.aER=new A.c(B.l,["How old was Joseph when he stood before Pharaoh and was appointed ruler?",B.a9d,"30","Joseph was thirty years old when he entered the service of Pharaoh king of Egypt.","Genesis 41:46"],t.M)
B.ago=A.a(s(["Imhotep","Akenaten","Zaphenath-Paneah","Rameses"]),t.s)
B.aEU=new A.c(B.l,["What Egyptian name was Joseph given by Pharaoh?",B.ago,"Zaphenath-Paneah","Pharaoh gave Joseph the Egyptian name Zaphenath-Paneah when he elevated him to his position of authority.","Genesis 41:45"],t.M)
B.adV=A.a(s(["Miriam","Asenath","Zipporah","Nefertiti"]),t.s)
B.aGY=new A.c(B.l,["Who was Joseph's Egyptian wife?",B.adV,"Asenath","Pharaoh gave Joseph Asenath, the daughter of Potiphera the priest of On, to be his wife.","Genesis 41:45"],t.M)
B.ak2=A.a(s(["Gad and Asher","Perez and Zerah","Manasseh and Ephraim","Reuben and Simeon"]),t.s)
B.aCF=new A.c(B.l,["What were the names of Joseph's two sons?",B.ak2,"Manasseh and Ephraim","Joseph named his firstborn Manasseh and his second son Ephraim, names reflecting God's faithfulness in his suffering and fruitfulness.","Genesis 41:51-52"],t.M)
B.a5G=A.a(s(["Chief military commander","High priest of the temple","Second in command over all of Egypt","Royal treasurer and tax collector"]),t.s)
B.aGv=new A.c(B.l,["What was Joseph's official role in Egypt after Pharaoh promoted him?",B.a5G,"Second in command over all of Egypt","Pharaoh put Joseph in charge of the whole land of Egypt, making him second only to Pharaoh himself.","Genesis 41:40-41"],t.M)
B.abI=A.a(s(["Gold and silver for the royal treasury","Grain and food from the land","Weapons for the Egyptian army","Papyrus scrolls in the royal library"]),t.s)
B.aAT=new A.c(B.l,["What did Joseph collect and store during the seven years of plenty?",B.abI,"Grain and food from the land","Joseph traveled throughout Egypt and collected all the food produced in those seven years of abundance and stored it in the cities.","Genesis 41:48"],t.M)
B.akK=A.a(s(["A jeweled armband from the Nile","His own signet ring","A golden ring from the temple treasury","A ceremonial ring from the high priest"]),t.s)
B.aAE=new A.c(B.l,["What symbolic item did Pharaoh place on Joseph's finger when promoting him?",B.akK,"His own signet ring","Pharaoh took his signet ring from his own finger and put it on Joseph's finger, along with fine linen robes and a gold chain.","Genesis 41:42"],t.M)
B.aja=A.a(s([B.aD6,B.aGo,B.aBC,B.aER,B.aEU,B.aGY,B.aCF,B.aGv,B.aAT,B.aAE]),t.J)
B.aJ_=new A.c(B.ak,["joseph_rise","Rise in Egypt","Medium",!0,30,6,B.aec,B.aja],t.M)
B.aUt=new A.c(B.v,["When the famine struck the known world, people came to Egypt from every direction to buy grain. Among those who came were ten of Joseph's brothers \u2014 Jacob had sent them to buy grain in Egypt but kept his youngest son Benjamin home, fearing harm might come to him. Joseph recognized his brothers the moment he saw them, but they did not recognize him. The powerful Egyptian official standing before them in royal robes was their brother they had sold as a slave twenty years before.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUp=new A.c(B.v,['Joseph treated his brothers as strangers and spoke harshly to them, accusing them of being spies. He demanded that one of them remain as a hostage while the others returned home and came back with their youngest brother Benjamin to prove their story. Simeon was bound before their eyes and kept behind. As the brothers talked among themselves in their own language \u2014 not realizing Joseph understood them \u2014 they said to each other, "Surely we are being punished because of what we did to Joseph." Hearing this, Joseph turned away from them and wept.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aS7=new A.c(B.v,["Eventually, driven by hunger, the brothers returned to Egypt with Benjamin. Joseph could barely contain himself when he saw his younger brother. He rushed into a private room and wept. When he had composed himself he returned and they ate together. Then Joseph instructed his steward to hide his silver divining cup in Benjamin's sack. When the brothers were stopped and the cup was found, they were brought back to face Joseph. Judah stepped forward and offered himself in Benjamin's place, unwilling to see his father bear another loss.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUo=new A.c(B.v,['Joseph could hold back no longer. He cleared the room of all his Egyptian attendants and, with great weeping that could be heard throughout the palace, revealed himself to his brothers: "I am Joseph! Is my father still living?" The brothers were too terrified to speak. But Joseph reassured them: "Do not be distressed or angry with yourselves for selling me here, because it was to save lives that God sent me ahead of you." Jacob\'s entire family \u2014 seventy people in all \u2014 came down to Egypt and settled in the region of Goshen.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.amU=A.a(s([B.aUt,B.aUp,B.aS7,B.aUo]),t.o)
B.arj=A.a(s(["To seek Joseph whom they had sold","To buy grain during the famine","To escape from enemies in Canaan","To pay tribute to the Pharaoh"]),t.s)
B.aD9=new A.c(B.l,["Why did the brothers travel to Egypt during the famine?",B.arj,"To buy grain during the famine","When Jacob learned that there was grain in Egypt, he sent ten of his sons there to buy grain during the severe famine.","Genesis 42:1-3"],t.M)
B.ag0=A.a(s(["Reuben","Levi","Simeon","Dan"]),t.s)
B.aCV=new A.c(B.l,["Which brother did Joseph keep as a hostage on the brothers' first visit?",B.ag0,"Simeon","Joseph had Simeon taken from the brothers and bound before their eyes, to be kept in Egypt while the rest returned home to bring back Benjamin.","Genesis 42:24"],t.M)
B.ahe=A.a(s(["A gift of gold and silver","Their father Jacob himself","Their youngest brother Benjamin","A signed letter from their tribe leader"]),t.s)
B.aGF=new A.c(B.l,["What did Joseph demand the brothers bring with them on their next visit?",B.ahe,"Their youngest brother Benjamin","Joseph insisted that the brothers could not see his face again unless their youngest brother Benjamin came with them to Egypt.","Genesis 43:3"],t.M)
B.alM=A.a(s(["Stolen Egyptian coins","A royal document","Joseph's silver divining cup","A piece of Pharaoh's jewelry"]),t.s)
B.aF8=new A.c(B.l,["What was secretly placed in Benjamin's sack to frame him?",B.alM,"Joseph's silver divining cup","Joseph instructed his steward to put his silver divining cup in the mouth of Benjamin's sack as a test of his brothers' character.","Genesis 44:2"],t.M)
B.ag_=A.a(s(["Reuben","Judah","Zebulun","Naphtali"]),t.s)
B.aCT=new A.c(B.l,["Which brother stepped forward and offered to take Benjamin's place in slavery?",B.ag_,"Judah","Judah came forward and pleaded passionately for Benjamin's release, offering himself as a slave in Benjamin's place so that his father would not die of grief.","Genesis 44:33"],t.M)
B.anB=A.a(s(['"You are forgiven \u2014 go and sin no more!"',u.lb,'"God has told me who you are \u2014 bow before me!"','"I have been waiting for this day of judgment!"']),t.s)
B.aAZ=new A.c(B.l,["What did Joseph say when he finally revealed himself to his brothers?",B.anB,u.lb,'Unable to control himself any longer, Joseph wept aloud and declared, "I am Joseph! Is my father still living?" \u2014 the brothers were too terrified to answer.',"Genesis 45:3"],t.M)
B.a4o=A.a(s(["The Nile Delta","The Valley of the Kings","Goshen","Memphis"]),t.s)
B.aCJ=new A.c(B.l,["In which region of Egypt did Jacob's family settle?",B.a4o,"Goshen","Joseph instructed his brothers to bring Jacob and their families to Egypt and settle in the region of Goshen, the best part of the land.","Genesis 45:10"],t.M)
B.a7q=A.a(s(["40","50","60","70"]),t.s)
B.aEM=new A.c(B.l,["How many members of Jacob's family came to settle in Egypt?",B.a7q,"70","All those who went to Egypt with Jacob \u2014 those who were his direct descendants, not counting his sons' wives \u2014 numbered seventy in all.","Genesis 46:27"],t.M)
B.ai3=A.a(s(['"You are guilty but I will have mercy on you this once"',u.mi,'"Your punishment will come from God, not from me"','"What is done is done and cannot be changed"']),t.s)
B.aFT=new A.c(B.l,["What did Joseph say to comfort his brothers about what they had done to him?",B.ai3,u.mi,"After Jacob's death, when the brothers feared Joseph's revenge, he reassured them: \"You intended to harm me, but God intended it for good to accomplish what is now being done, the saving of many lives.\"","Genesis 50:20"],t.M)
B.ahk=A.a(s(["110","120","125","130"]),t.s)
B.aFC=new A.c(B.l,["How old was Jacob when he went down to Egypt to be reunited with Joseph?",B.ahk,"130",'When Pharaoh asked Jacob his age, Jacob replied, "The years of my pilgrimage are a hundred and thirty."',"Genesis 47:9"],t.M)
B.ai2=A.a(s([B.aD9,B.aCV,B.aGF,B.aF8,B.aCT,B.aAZ,B.aCJ,B.aEM,B.aFT,B.aFC]),t.J)
B.aID=new A.c(B.ak,["joseph_reunion","Reunion with Brothers","Hard",!0,25,7,B.amU,B.ai2],t.M)
B.aqw=A.a(s([B.aIX,B.aIZ,B.aJ_,B.aID]),t.J)
B.aAe=new A.c(B.e4,["life_of_joseph","The Life of Joseph","From his father's favorite son to a slave in Egypt to the most powerful man after Pharaoh \u2014 discover how God turned betrayal and suffering into salvation for an entire nation.",B.aqw],t.R)
B.aTF=new A.c(B.v,["During the reign of King Ahab, Israel had turned away from God and began worshipping Baal. Ahab, influenced by his wife Jezebel, built altars to Baal and led the nation into deep idolatry. God's prophet Elijah stood alone against this tide of wickedness, declaring a drought on the land until further notice.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aT3=new A.c(B.v,["After three years of drought, Elijah issued a bold challenge to King Ahab. He called for all of Israel to assemble on Mount Carmel, along with the 450 prophets of Baal. There, Elijah proposed a contest: each side would prepare a sacrifice, and the God who answered by fire would be declared the true God.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aT0=new A.c(B.v,["The prophets of Baal cried out all morning, dancing around their altar, cutting themselves with swords and shouting. But no answer came. Elijah mocked them, suggesting perhaps Baal was asleep, traveling, or deep in thought. Then Elijah repaired the altar of the Lord, placed his offering on it, and drenched everything with water three times.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aS4=new A.c(B.v,["When Elijah prayed a simple, sincere prayer to the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, fire fell from heaven and consumed the sacrifice, the wood, the stones, the soil, and even licked up the water. The people fell on their faces and cried out in worship. The contest was over \u2014 God had answered definitively.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.a5C=A.a(s([B.aTF,B.aT3,B.aT0,B.aS4]),t.o)
B.acD=A.a(s(["Jeroboam","Ahab","Saul","Rehoboam"]),t.s)
B.aDg=new A.c(B.l,["Who was the wicked king of Israel during Elijah's time?",B.acD,"Ahab","King Ahab son of Omri did more evil in the sight of the Lord than any before him, including setting up altars for Baal.","1 Kings 16:30-33"],t.M)
B.a9R=A.a(s(["Delilah","Athaliah","Jezebel","Herodias"]),t.s)
B.aDN=new A.c(B.l,["Who was King Ahab's wicked wife who promoted Baal worship in Israel?",B.a9R,"Jezebel","Jezebel was a Phoenician princess who married Ahab and actively promoted the worship of Baal, even killing the Lord's prophets.","1 Kings 18:4"],t.M)
B.abL=A.a(s(["Mount Sinai","Mount Zion","Mount Horeb","Mount Carmel"]),t.s)
B.aH9=new A.c(B.l,["On which mountain did Elijah challenge the prophets of Baal?",B.abL,"Mount Carmel","Elijah summoned all Israel and the 450 prophets of Baal to Mount Carmel for the great contest.","1 Kings 18:19"],t.M)
B.agm=A.a(s(["250","400","450","500"]),t.s)
B.aEk=new A.c(B.l,["How many prophets of Baal gathered on Mount Carmel?",B.agm,"450","There were 450 prophets of Baal gathered on Mount Carmel, along with 400 prophets of Asherah.","1 Kings 18:19"],t.M)
B.ak9=A.a(s(["Predict the weather",u.g,"Part the Jordan River","Make it rain"]),t.s)
B.aGW=new A.c(B.l,["What did Elijah challenge the prophets of Baal to do?",B.ak9,u.g,"Elijah proposed that each side prepare a bull on wood but light no fire \u2014 the God who answered by fire would be declared the true God.","1 Kings 18:23-24"],t.M)
B.aqA=A.a(s(["Prayed silently","Fasted and wept","Danced, shouted, and cut themselves","Built a bigger altar"]),t.s)
B.aCr=new A.c(B.l,["What did the prophets of Baal do all day trying to get their god to respond?",B.aqA,"Danced, shouted, and cut themselves","The prophets of Baal danced around the altar, shouted, and slashed themselves with swords and spears from morning until evening, but no answer came.","1 Kings 18:26-28"],t.M)
B.adj=A.a(s(["That Baal never existed","That Baal was sleeping or traveling","That Baal had gone to another country forever","That Baal was angry at his prophets"]),t.s)
B.aE1=new A.c(B.l,["What did Elijah mock, suggesting about Baal when there was no answer?",B.adj,"That Baal was sleeping or traveling","Elijah taunted them saying perhaps Baal was deep in thought, busy, traveling, or sleeping and needed to be wakened.","1 Kings 18:27"],t.M)
B.aeU=A.a(s(["Oil","Wine","Water","Salt"]),t.s)
B.aCQ=new A.c(B.l,["What did Elijah pour over his altar and sacrifice before praying?",B.aeU,"Water","Elijah had water poured over the sacrifice and the wood three times, filling even the trench around the altar, making the miracle of fire all the more dramatic.","1 Kings 18:33-35"],t.M)
B.aj0=A.a(s(["Rain fell heavily","An earthquake shook the mountain",u.mL,"A loud voice spoke from the sky"]),t.s)
B.aG5=new A.c(B.l,["What happened when Elijah prayed to God on Mount Carmel?",B.aj0,u.mL,"The fire of the Lord fell and consumed the burnt offering, the wood, the stones, the soil, and licked up all the water in the trench.","1 Kings 18:38"],t.M)
B.aeg=A.a(s(["Elijah is the greatest prophet!","The Lord, He is God!","Baal has been defeated!","Let us sacrifice to Elijah!"]),t.s)
B.aGs=new A.c(B.l,["What did the people cry out when they saw God's fire fall on Mount Carmel?",B.aeg,"The Lord, He is God!",'When all the people saw God\'s fire, they fell prostrate and cried out, "The Lord \u2014 He is God! The Lord \u2014 He is God!"',"1 Kings 18:39"],t.M)
B.a7K=A.a(s([B.aDg,B.aDN,B.aH9,B.aEk,B.aGW,B.aCr,B.aE1,B.aCQ,B.aG5,B.aGs]),t.J)
B.aJ6=new A.c(B.ak,["prophets_of_baal","Elijah vs the Prophets of Baal","Medium",!1,30,6,B.a5C,B.a7K],t.M)
B.aTU=new A.c(B.v,["Despite his great victory on Mount Carmel, Elijah's courage quickly fled when Queen Jezebel sent a message threatening to kill him within a day. Overcome with fear, Elijah ran into the wilderness of Judah, leaving his servant behind. He sat under a broom tree, exhausted and defeated in spirit.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTY=new A.c(B.v,["Under the broom tree, Elijah prayed that he might die, saying he was no better than his ancestors. But God was not done with him. An angel touched him and provided freshly baked bread and a jar of water. Twice the angel came, telling him to eat, for the journey ahead was too great for him.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUu=new A.c(B.v,['Strengthened by that heavenly food, Elijah traveled forty days and forty nights until he reached Horeb, the mountain of God. He took shelter in a cave. God asked him, "What are you doing here, Elijah?" Elijah poured out his heart \u2014 he felt utterly alone, as though he were the last faithful person in all of Israel.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTP=new A.c(B.v,["God told Elijah to stand on the mountain. A great wind tore the mountains apart, then an earthquake shook the ground, then fire blazed \u2014 but God was not in any of these dramatic displays. After the fire came a still small voice, a gentle whisper. It was in that quiet moment that God spoke to Elijah with new purpose and a new assignment.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.abQ=A.a(s([B.aTU,B.aTY,B.aUu,B.aTP]),t.o)
B.a5M=A.a(s(["King Ahab","Jezebel","The army of Israel","The people of Samaria"]),t.s)
B.aDq=new A.c(B.l,["Who threatened to kill Elijah after the defeat of Baal's prophets?",B.a5M,"Jezebel","Jezebel sent a messenger to Elijah swearing she would take his life within a day, just as he had killed her prophets.","1 Kings 19:2"],t.M)
B.ad5=A.a(s(["Egypt","The wilderness near Beersheba","Nineveh","The Jordan River"]),t.s)
B.aB_=new A.c(B.l,["Where did Elijah flee to after Jezebel's threat?",B.ad5,"The wilderness near Beersheba","Elijah ran for his life to Beersheba in Judah, left his servant there, and went a day's journey into the wilderness.","1 Kings 19:3-4"],t.M)
B.aj1=A.a(s(["To be taken to heaven immediately","Strength to fight Jezebel","To die","A new mission"]),t.s)
B.aEE=new A.c(B.l,["What did Elijah ask God for while sitting under the broom tree?",B.aj1,"To die",'In despair, Elijah prayed, "I have had enough, Lord. Take my life; I am no better than my ancestors."',"1 Kings 19:4"],t.M)
B.a5W=A.a(s(["A fellow prophet","King Ahab's servant","An angel","Elisha"]),t.s)
B.aB1=new A.c(B.l,["Who brought Elijah food and water in the wilderness?",B.a5W,"An angel","An angel of the Lord touched Elijah twice, providing freshly baked bread over hot coals and a jar of water.","1 Kings 19:5-7"],t.M)
B.ar9=A.a(s(["7 days and nights","14 days and nights","30 days and nights","40 days and nights"]),t.s)
B.aF7=new A.c(B.l,["How many days and nights did Elijah travel to reach Horeb?",B.ar9,"40 days and nights","Strengthened by the angelic food, Elijah traveled forty days and forty nights until he reached Horeb, the mountain of God.","1 Kings 19:8"],t.M)
B.asp=A.a(s(["Under a tree","In a cave","In a tent","By a river"]),t.s)
B.aGQ=new A.c(B.l,["Where did Elijah shelter when he arrived at Mount Horeb?",B.asp,"In a cave","Elijah arrived at Horeb and spent the night in a cave, where God came to him and asked what he was doing there.","1 Kings 19:9"],t.M)
B.apE=A.a(s(["Rain, thunder, and flood","Wind, earthquake, and fire","Hail, lightning, and fog","Drought, famine, and darkness"]),t.s)
B.aFu=new A.c(B.l,["What natural phenomena occurred on the mountain before God spoke \u2014 but God was NOT in them?",B.apE,"Wind, earthquake, and fire","A great wind, an earthquake, and a fire all occurred, but the Lord was not in any of them \u2014 He spoke after the fire in a gentle whisper.","1 Kings 19:11-12"],t.M)
B.a7u=A.a(s(["In a thunderous voice","Through a vision in the night",u.nM,"Through a burning bush"]),t.s)
B.aFd=new A.c(B.l,["How did God speak to Elijah on Mount Horeb?",B.a7u,u.nM,"After the dramatic wind, earthquake, and fire, God spoke to Elijah in a still small voice, a sound of sheer silence.","1 Kings 19:12"],t.M)
B.apo=A.a(s(["1,000","3,000","5,000","7,000"]),t.s)
B.aAI=new A.c(B.l,["How many faithful Israelites did God say had not bowed to Baal?",B.apo,"7,000","God told Elijah He had reserved 7,000 in Israel who had not bowed the knee to Baal or kissed his image.","1 Kings 19:18"],t.M)
B.a6v=A.a(s(["Return to Jezreel and confront Ahab","Anoint Hazael, Jehu, and Elisha","Build an altar at Horeb","Prophesy the end of Ahab's dynasty"]),t.s)
B.aBh=new A.c(B.l,["What task did God give Elijah next after speaking to him at Horeb?",B.a6v,"Anoint Hazael, Jehu, and Elisha","God commanded Elijah to go and anoint Hazael as king over Syria, Jehu as king over Israel, and Elisha son of Shaphat as prophet in his place.","1 Kings 19:15-16"],t.M)
B.abx=A.a(s([B.aDq,B.aB_,B.aEE,B.aB1,B.aF7,B.aGQ,B.aFu,B.aFd,B.aAI,B.aBh]),t.J)
B.aIE=new A.c(B.ak,["still_small_voice","The Still Small Voice","Easy",!1,30,6,B.abQ,B.abx],t.M)
B.aTx=new A.c(B.v,['The time came for God to take Elijah up into heaven. Elijah and his faithful successor Elisha set out from Gilgal together. Though Elijah urged Elisha three times to stay behind \u2014 first at Bethel, then at Jericho, then at the Jordan \u2014 Elisha refused to leave his master\'s side, declaring each time, "As the Lord lives and as you live, I will not leave you."',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSC=new A.c(B.v,["Fifty prophets from Jericho watched from a distance as the two men reached the Jordan River. Elijah took his cloak, rolled it up, and struck the water. The water divided to the right and to the left, and the two crossed over on dry ground \u2014 a miracle echoing the great crossing of Moses.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSd=new A.c(B.v,["On the other side, Elijah asked Elisha what he could do for him before he was taken away. Elisha boldly asked for a double portion of Elijah's spirit. Elijah said that was a difficult thing, but if Elisha saw him being taken, the request would be granted. Then, as they walked and talked, a chariot of fire and horses of fire appeared and separated them.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSn=new A.c(B.v,['Elijah went up to heaven in a whirlwind. Elisha saw it and cried out, "My father! My father! The chariots and horsemen of Israel!" When Elijah was gone, Elisha picked up the cloak that had fallen from him. He returned to the Jordan, struck the water with Elijah\'s cloak, and the water parted again \u2014 the double portion had been granted.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.agV=A.a(s([B.aTx,B.aSC,B.aSd,B.aSn]),t.o)
B.aoa=A.a(s(["The Nile","The Euphrates","The Jordan","The Kishon"]),t.s)
B.aCN=new A.c(B.l,["What river did Elijah part with his rolled-up cloak?",B.aoa,"The Jordan","Elijah took his cloak, rolled it up and struck the Jordan River, which divided so both men could cross on dry ground.","2 Kings 2:8"],t.M)
B.aeW=A.a(s(["His staff and sandals","A double portion of his spirit","Wisdom to lead Israel","A long life"]),t.s)
B.aBP=new A.c(B.l,["What did Elisha ask Elijah for before he was taken?",B.aeW,"A double portion of his spirit","Elisha asked for a double portion of Elijah's spirit \u2014 the inheritance request of a firstborn son \u2014 to carry on the prophetic ministry powerfully.","2 Kings 2:9"],t.M)
B.aao=A.a(s(["On a white cloud",u.nC,"Through a pillar of light","By a strong wind that lifted him up"]),t.s)
B.aF9=new A.c(B.l,["How was Elijah taken up into heaven?",B.aao,u.nC,"A chariot of fire and horses of fire appeared and separated Elijah and Elisha, and Elijah went up to heaven in a whirlwind.","2 Kings 2:11"],t.M)
B.ade=A.a(s(["Lord, do not take him from me!",u.lr,"God of Elijah, where are You now?","Elijah, come back to us!"]),t.s)
B.aAY=new A.c(B.l,["What did Elisha cry out as Elijah was taken to heaven?",B.ade,u.lr,'Elisha tore his own clothes and cried out, "My father! My father! The chariots and horsemen of Israel!" \u2014 a title of deep honor for Elijah.',"2 Kings 2:12"],t.M)
B.agh=A.a(s(["Elijah's sandals","Elijah's staff","Elijah's cloak \u2014 his mantle","A scroll Elijah left behind"]),t.s)
B.aEH=new A.c(B.l,["What did Elisha pick up after Elijah was taken?",B.agh,"Elijah's cloak \u2014 his mantle","Elisha picked up the cloak that had fallen from Elijah, which symbolized the transfer of prophetic authority.","2 Kings 2:13"],t.M)
B.ajj=A.a(s(["Wore it to Jericho","Burned it as an offering","Struck the water and it parted","Wrapped it around a sick man to heal him"]),t.s)
B.aDh=new A.c(B.l,["What did Elisha do with Elijah's cloak at the Jordan River?",B.ajj,"Struck the water and it parted","Elisha struck the Jordan with Elijah's cloak and the water divided, confirming he had received the double portion of Elijah's spirit.","2 Kings 2:14"],t.M)
B.abV=A.a(s(["The king's soldiers","The elders of Israel","50 prophets from Jericho","Elisha's family"]),t.s)
B.aCD=new A.c(B.l,["Who watched from a distance as Elijah and Elisha crossed the Jordan?",B.abV,"50 prophets from Jericho","Fifty men from the company of the prophets stood at a distance watching as Elijah and Elisha crossed the Jordan River.","2 Kings 2:7"],t.M)
B.a6S=A.a(s(["Once","Twice","Three times","Four times"]),t.s)
B.aE0=new A.c(B.l,["How many times did Elijah tell Elisha to stay behind on their final journey?",B.a6S,"Three times","Elijah told Elisha to stay at Gilgal, then at Bethel, then at Jericho \u2014 but each time Elisha refused to leave.","2 Kings 2:2-6"],t.M)
B.a51=A.a(s(["Fire fell on his altar","He spoke in Elijah's voice","The Jordan parted when he struck it","Jezebel feared him immediately"]),t.s)
B.aFj=new A.c(B.l,["What confirmed that Elisha had truly received Elijah's spirit?",B.a51,"The Jordan parted when he struck it","When the Jordan River divided at Elisha's strike with Elijah's cloak, the company of prophets recognized that the spirit of Elijah rested on Elisha.","2 Kings 2:14-15"],t.M)
B.aal=A.a(s(["Enoch","Elijah","Moses","Isaiah"]),t.s)
B.aGZ=new A.c(B.l,["Which Old Testament prophet never experienced physical death?",B.aal,"Elijah","Elijah was taken up alive to heaven in a whirlwind, making him one of only two people in the Bible who did not die \u2014 the other being Enoch.","2 Kings 2:11"],t.M)
B.a7f=A.a(s([B.aCN,B.aBP,B.aF9,B.aAY,B.aEH,B.aDh,B.aCD,B.aE0,B.aFj,B.aGZ]),t.J)
B.aJ4=new A.c(B.ak,["chariot_of_fire","Elijah's Chariot of Fire","Medium",!0,30,6,B.agV,B.a7f],t.M)
B.aTN=new A.c(B.v,["Elisha began his ministry with compassion and supernatural power. In Jericho, he healed a spring of bitter, unusable water by throwing salt into it. His ministry demonstrated that God's power was not just for dramatic confrontations but for the everyday needs of the people \u2014 widows, soldiers, and foreigners alike.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSy=new A.c(B.v,["A widow in desperate debt came to Elisha with only a small jar of oil. Elisha told her to borrow as many empty jars as she could, then pour from her single jar. Miraculously the oil kept flowing, filling every jar she had borrowed \u2014 enough to sell and pay all her debts and live on the rest.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSf=new A.c(B.v,["A wealthy Shunammite woman showed Elisha great hospitality, so God blessed her with a son. Years later the child died suddenly. The woman rode to Elisha in great distress. Elisha came and stretched himself over the dead boy twice; the child sneezed seven times and opened his eyes. God had raised him from the dead.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTR=new A.c(B.v,["Naaman, commander of the Syrian army, suffered from leprosy. He came to Elisha seeking healing. Though proud and offended by Elisha's simple instructions, Naaman's servants persuaded him to obey. He dipped seven times in the Jordan River and his skin became clean like a little child's. God's grace extended beyond the borders of Israel.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.af0=A.a(s([B.aTN,B.aSy,B.aSf,B.aTR]),t.o)
B.aqa=A.a(s(["Oil","A stone","Salt","A branch"]),t.s)
B.aD8=new A.c(B.l,["What did Elisha throw into the spring to heal the bitter, undrinkable waters of Jericho?",B.aqa,"Salt","Elisha threw salt into the spring and declared the Lord had healed the water \u2014 the spring has been wholesome ever since.","2 Kings 2:20-22"],t.M)
B.aih=A.a(s(["Gehazi","Hazael","Ben-Hadad","Naaman"]),t.s)
B.aDL=new A.c(B.l,["Who was the foreign military commander healed of leprosy through Elisha?",B.aih,"Naaman","Naaman was the commander of the army of the king of Aram who came to Elisha and was healed of his leprosy.","2 Kings 5:1"],t.M)
B.ao9=A.a(s(["The Nile","The Euphrates","The Abana","The Jordan"]),t.s)
B.aFw=new A.c(B.l,["In which river was Naaman told to wash in order to be healed of leprosy?",B.ao9,"The Jordan","Elisha instructed Naaman to wash seven times in the Jordan River, and his flesh would be restored.","2 Kings 5:10"],t.M)
B.amn=A.a(s(["Once","Three times","Five times","7 times"]),t.s)
B.aDE=new A.c(B.l,["How many times did Naaman dip in the river to be healed?",B.amn,"7 times","Naaman dipped himself seven times in the Jordan, as Elisha had instructed, and his flesh was restored and became clean like a young boy's.","2 Kings 5:14"],t.M)
B.apL=A.a(s(["The city's cisterns",u.j8,"A large clay pot in the temple","The jars of her neighbors only"]),t.s)
B.aBW=new A.c(B.l,["What did the widow's miraculous oil fill when Elisha performed his miracle?",B.apL,u.j8,"Elisha told the widow to borrow as many empty vessels as she could; the oil from her small jar kept flowing until every borrowed vessel was full.","2 Kings 4:3-6"],t.M)
B.a9q=A.a(s(["The widow of Zarephath's son","The Shunammite woman's son","The commander's son","Elisha's servant's son"]),t.s)
B.aCb=new A.c(B.l,["Whose son did Elisha raise from the dead?",B.a9q,"The Shunammite woman's son","The Shunammite woman, who had shown great hospitality to Elisha, saw her son die suddenly; Elisha came and raised the boy back to life.","2 Kings 4:32-35"],t.M)
B.ajo=A.a(s(["Spoiled meat with maggots","Contaminated water mixed with grain","Poisonous stew made from wild gourds","Bread made with bad flour"]),t.s)
B.aGE=new A.c(B.l,['What food did Elisha purify when someone cried out "There is death in the pot"?',B.ajo,"Poisonous stew made from wild gourds","When a man added wild gourds to a stew during famine making it poisonous, Elisha threw flour into the pot and the stew became harmless.","2 Kings 4:38-41"],t.M)
B.a49=A.a(s(["50 men","100 men","200 men","500 men"]),t.s)
B.aFJ=new A.c(B.l,["How many men did Elisha feed with only 20 loaves of barley bread?",B.a49,"100 men","A man brought twenty loaves of barley bread to Elisha; though his servant questioned how it could feed 100 men, they ate and had leftovers.","2 Kings 4:42-44"],t.M)
B.ahN=A.a(s(["A great army of angels standing guard",u.oM,"A shining cloud covering the city","Lions and eagles protecting the gates"]),t.s)
B.aGp=new A.c(B.l,["What did Elisha's servant see when God opened his eyes during the Syrian siege?",B.ahN,u.oM,"When the servant was terrified by the Syrian army, Elisha prayed for his eyes to be opened; he then saw the hills full of horses and chariots of fire.","2 Kings 6:17"],t.M)
B.aah=A.a(s(["Eliezer","Jonah","Gehazi","Micaiah"]),t.s)
B.aEL=new A.c(B.l,["Who was Elisha's greedy servant who was cursed with Naaman's leprosy?",B.aah,"Gehazi","Gehazi secretly ran after Naaman and accepted gifts in Elisha's name. When Elisha confronted him, Gehazi was struck with Naaman's leprosy.","2 Kings 5:20-27"],t.M)
B.ao6=A.a(s([B.aD8,B.aDL,B.aFw,B.aDE,B.aBW,B.aCb,B.aGE,B.aFJ,B.aGp,B.aEL]),t.J)
B.aII=new A.c(B.ak,["elisha_miracles","Elisha's Miracles","Hard",!0,25,7,B.af0,B.ao6],t.M)
B.a48=A.a(s([B.aJ6,B.aIE,B.aJ4,B.aII]),t.J)
B.aAm=new A.c(B.e4,["elijah_and_elisha","Elijah and Elisha","Witness the mighty works of two of Israel's greatest prophets \u2014 from fire falling on Mount Carmel to chariots of fire in the sky.",B.a48],t.R)
B.aT_=new A.c(B.v,['Before anything existed \u2014 before light, before sound, before time itself \u2014 there was God. And in the boundless darkness, He spoke. "Let there be light." And there was light. With each passing day, the formless void was shaped into a masterpiece of unfathomable beauty.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTv=new A.c(B.v,["The skies stretched out above the waters. Dry land emerged, clothed in every kind of plant and tree. The sun, moon, and stars were set in their courses. The seas teemed with life and the skies filled with birds. Every creature upon the earth was spoken into being by the voice of God.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSp=new A.c(B.v,["Then came the crowning act of creation. From the dust of the ground, God formed man and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life. He planted a garden in Eden \u2014 a paradise of rivers and fruit-bearing trees \u2014 and placed the man there to tend it.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTZ=new A.c(B.v,["But God saw that it was not good for man to be alone. So He caused Adam to fall into a deep sleep and from his side fashioned a woman. Adam and Eve stood together in the garden, naked and unashamed, walking in perfect fellowship with their Creator.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.agW=A.a(s([B.aT_,B.aTv,B.aSp,B.aTZ]),t.o)
B.a6w=A.a(s(["The sun and moon","Light","Dry land","Animals"]),t.s)
B.aAL=new A.c(B.l,["What did God create on the first day?",B.a6w,"Light",'On the first day, God said "Let there be light," and He separated the light from the darkness, calling them day and night.',"Genesis 1:3-5"],t.M)
B.ajX=A.a(s(["The stars","Fish and birds","The sky (firmament)","Trees and plants"]),t.s)
B.aD7=new A.c(B.l,["What did God create on the second day?",B.ajX,"The sky (firmament)","On the second day, God made the firmament (expanse) to separate the waters above from the waters below, and He called it Heaven.","Genesis 1:6-8"],t.M)
B.af4=A.a(s(["Second day","Third day","Fourth day","Fifth day"]),t.s)
B.aEy=new A.c(B.l,["On which day did God create vegetation, plants, and trees?",B.af4,"Third day","On the third day, God gathered the waters to reveal dry land, and then commanded the earth to bring forth grass, herbs, and fruit trees.","Genesis 1:9-13"],t.M)
B.alL=A.a(s(["Birds and fish","Sun, moon, and stars","Land animals","Man and woman"]),t.s)
