B.aIH=new A.c(B.ak,["in_the_beginning","In the Beginning","Easy",!1,30,6,B.agW,B.arL],t.M)
B.aTy=new A.c(B.v,['In the garden of Eden, all was perfect \u2014 every need provided, every joy abundant. But among the creatures God had made, the serpent was the most cunning. It slithered toward Eve with a question designed to plant the seed of doubt: "Did God really say you must not eat from any tree in the garden?"',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aS_=new A.c(B.v,['Eve corrected the serpent, explaining they could eat from every tree except one \u2014 the tree in the middle of the garden. But the serpent twisted the truth: "You will not surely die. God knows that when you eat of it, your eyes will be opened and you will be like God." The fruit looked delightful, and the promise of wisdom was too tempting to resist.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSW=new A.c(B.v,["She took the fruit and ate. She gave some to Adam, who was with her, and he ate as well. In that instant, innocence shattered. Their eyes were opened, and for the first time they felt shame. They sewed fig leaves together to cover themselves and hid among the trees when they heard God walking in the garden.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUz=new A.c(B.v,['God called out, "Where are you?" \u2014 not because He did not know, but because He wanted them to confess. Instead, Adam blamed Eve, and Eve blamed the serpent. The consequences were swift and severe: pain, toil, and death entered the world. God clothed them in garments of skin and drove them from Eden, posting cherubim and a flaming sword to guard the way to the tree of life.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.a8a=A.a(s([B.aTy,B.aS_,B.aSW,B.aUz]),t.o)
B.art=A.a(s(["A lion","A serpent","An eagle","A raven"]),t.s)
B.aEg=new A.c(B.l,["Which creature tempted Eve to eat the forbidden fruit?",B.art,"A serpent","The Bible says the serpent was more cunning than any beast of the field that the Lord God had made, and it deceived Eve.","Genesis 3:1"],t.M)
B.aqc=A.a(s(["God does not exist","You will not surely die","The fruit is poisonous","Adam has already eaten"]),t.s)
B.aB4=new A.c(B.l,["What lie did the serpent tell Eve?",B.aqc,"You will not surely die",'The serpent directly contradicted God\'s warning by telling Eve, "You will not surely die," and claimed the fruit would make them like God.',"Genesis 3:4"],t.M)
B.a9v=A.a(s(["They ran from the garden",u.oH,"They prayed for forgiveness","They blamed the serpent"]),t.s)
B.aDd=new A.c(B.l,["What did Adam and Eve do immediately after eating the forbidden fruit?",B.a9v,u.oH,"After eating the fruit, their eyes were opened and they knew they were naked, so they sewed fig leaves together to make coverings.","Genesis 3:7"],t.M)
B.acY=A.a(s(["They confessed their sin","They hid among the trees","They offered a sacrifice","They ate more fruit"]),t.s)
B.aCe=new A.c(B.l,["What did Adam and Eve do when they heard God walking in the garden?",B.acY,"They hid among the trees","Adam and Eve heard the sound of the Lord God walking in the garden in the cool of the day, and they hid themselves among the trees.","Genesis 3:8"],t.M)
B.aie=A.a(s(["The serpent","Himself","The woman God gave him","No one"]),t.s)
B.aDj=new A.c(B.l,["Who did Adam blame when God confronted him?",B.aie,"The woman God gave him",'Adam said, "The woman whom You gave to be with me, she gave me of the tree, and I ate," blaming both Eve and indirectly God Himself.',"Genesis 3:12"],t.M)
B.a7A=A.a(s(["It would lose its voice","It would crawl on its belly and eat dust","It would be cast into fire","It would become invisible"]),t.s)
B.aDU=new A.c(B.l,["What curse did God place on the serpent?",B.a7A,"It would crawl on its belly and eat dust",'God cursed the serpent above all livestock and beasts: "On your belly you shall go, and dust you shall eat all the days of your life."',"Genesis 3:14"],t.M)
B.a9c=A.a(s(["She would never have children","Greatly multiplied pain in childbearing","She would become mortal immediately","She would lose her sight"]),t.s)
B.aCm=new A.c(B.l,["What consequence of the fall was specifically given to Eve?",B.a9c,"Greatly multiplied pain in childbearing",'God told Eve, "I will greatly multiply your sorrow and your conception; in pain you shall bring forth children."',"Genesis 3:16"],t.M)
B.agk=A.a(s(["Fig leaves","Animal skins","Wool","Linen"]),t.s)
B.aBy=new A.c(B.l,["What did God use to make garments for Adam and Eve?",B.agk,"Animal skins","The Lord God made tunics of skin for Adam and Eve and clothed them, which was the first shedding of blood as a covering for sin.","Genesis 3:21"],t.M)
B.a9t=A.a(s(["A wall of fire","An angel with a key","Cherubim and a flaming sword","A great river"]),t.s)
B.aGh=new A.c(B.l,["What did God place at the east of the garden of Eden to guard the way to the tree of life?",B.a9t,"Cherubim and a flaming sword","God placed cherubim at the east of the garden of Eden, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to guard the way to the tree of life.","Genesis 3:24"],t.M)
B.ajw=A.a(s(["Thorns and thistles","Weeds and poison","Only bitter fruit","Nothing at all"]),t.s)
B.aFf=new A.c(B.l,["What was the ground cursed to produce because of Adam's sin?",B.ajw,"Thorns and thistles",'God told Adam, "Cursed is the ground for your sake... both thorns and thistles it shall bring forth for you."',"Genesis 3:17-18"],t.M)
B.al3=A.a(s([B.aEg,B.aB4,B.aDd,B.aCe,B.aDj,B.aDU,B.aCm,B.aBy,B.aGh,B.aFf]),t.J)
B.aJ8=new A.c(B.ak,["the_fall_of_man","The Fall of Man","Medium",!1,30,6,B.a8a,B.al3],t.M)
B.aU0=new A.c(B.v,["Outside the garden, life was harder but it went on. Eve bore two sons \u2014 Cain, the firstborn, and Abel, his younger brother. As they grew, each found his own path: Cain worked the soil as a farmer, while Abel tended flocks as a shepherd. In time, both brothers brought offerings to the Lord.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSj=new A.c(B.v,["Abel brought the firstborn of his flock and their fat portions \u2014 the very best he had. Cain brought an offering of the fruit of the ground. The Lord looked with favor on Abel and his offering, but He did not regard Cain's. Anger twisted Cain's face, and jealousy took root in his heart.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSB=new A.c(B.v,['God warned Cain: "Why are you angry? If you do well, will you not be accepted? But if you do not, sin is crouching at the door. Its desire is for you, but you must rule over it." Cain ignored the warning. He lured his brother into the field and rose up against Abel and killed him \u2014 the first murder in human history.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUs=new A.c(B.v,['When God asked, "Where is Abel your brother?" Cain replied with cold defiance: "Am I my brother\'s keeper?" But Abel\'s blood cried out from the ground. God cursed Cain to be a restless wanderer, and the ground would no longer yield its strength for him. Yet even in judgment, God showed mercy \u2014 He placed a mark on Cain so that no one who found him would kill him.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.a8z=A.a(s([B.aU0,B.aSj,B.aSB,B.aUs]),t.o)
B.agA=A.a(s(["Shepherd","Farmer","Hunter","Carpenter"]),t.s)
B.aC7=new A.c(B.l,["What was Cain's occupation?",B.agA,"Farmer","Cain was a tiller of the ground \u2014 he worked the soil and brought an offering of its produce to the Lord.","Genesis 4:2"],t.M)
B.ajS=A.a(s(["Farmer","Builder","Keeper of sheep","Fisherman"]),t.s)
B.aBn=new A.c(B.l,["What was Abel's occupation?",B.ajS,"Keeper of sheep","Abel was a keeper of sheep. He tended flocks and brought an offering from the firstborn of his flock.","Genesis 4:2"],t.M)
B.aoj=A.a(s(["Fruit of the ground","Firstborn of his flock","Gold and silver","Grain and wine"]),t.s)
B.aCj=new A.c(B.l,["What offering did Abel bring to the Lord?",B.aoj,"Firstborn of his flock","Abel brought of the firstborn of his flock and of their fat. The Lord respected Abel and his offering.","Genesis 4:4"],t.M)
B.am5=A.a(s(["Abel stole from him","God accepted Abel's offering but not his","He lost his crops to drought","Adam favored Abel over him"]),t.s)
B.aFb=new A.c(B.l,["Why was Cain angry?",B.am5,"God accepted Abel's offering but not his","The Lord respected Abel's offering but did not respect Cain's, which made Cain very angry and his face fell.","Genesis 4:4-5"],t.M)
B.abw=A.a(s(["A wild beast","Sin","Death","An angel"]),t.s)
B.aEx=new A.c(B.l,['What did God say was "crouching at the door" for Cain?',B.abw,"Sin","God warned Cain that if he did not do well, sin was crouching at the door, and its desire was for him, but he must rule over it.","Genesis 4:7"],t.M)
B.ast=A.a(s(["He is in the field",u.pl,"A wild animal took him","He went to another land"]),t.s)
B.aH6=new A.c(B.l,["What did Cain say when God asked where Abel was?",B.ast,u.pl,'Cain lied to God and responded with the now-famous deflection, "I do not know. Am I my brother\'s keeper?"',"Genesis 4:9"],t.M)
B.akE=A.a(s(["Staining the altar","Crying out from the ground","Flowing into the river","Turning the soil red"]),t.s)
B.aDT=new A.c(B.l,["What did God say Abel's blood was doing?",B.akE,"Crying out from the ground",'God said to Cain, "The voice of your brother\'s blood cries out to Me from the ground."',"Genesis 4:10"],t.M)
B.a7X=A.a(s(["Immediate death",u.hC,"To serve Abel's children","To be cast into darkness"]),t.s)
B.aEY=new A.c(B.l,["What was Cain's punishment from God?",B.a7X,u.hC,"God told Cain he would be a fugitive and a vagabond on the earth, and the ground would no longer yield its strength for him.","Genesis 4:11-12"],t.M)
B.acz=A.a(s(["A shield of light","A mark","An angelic guard","A ring of fire"]),t.s)
B.aBH=new A.c(B.l,["What did God place on Cain to protect him?",B.acz,"A mark","The Lord set a mark on Cain so that anyone who found him would not kill him, showing mercy even in judgment.","Genesis 4:15"],t.M)
B.acx=A.a(s(["The land of Nod","The land of Canaan","Back to Eden","The land of Shinar"]),t.s)
B.aC4=new A.c(B.l,["Where did Cain go to live after being sent away?",B.acx,"The land of Nod","Cain went out from the presence of the Lord and dwelt in the land of Nod, east of Eden.","Genesis 4:16"],t.M)
B.ank=A.a(s([B.aC7,B.aBn,B.aCj,B.aFb,B.aEx,B.aH6,B.aDT,B.aEY,B.aBH,B.aC4]),t.J)
B.aJi=new A.c(B.ak,["cain_and_abel","Cain and Abel","Medium",!1,30,6,B.a8z,B.ank],t.M)
B.aSJ=new A.c(B.v,["Generations passed, and humanity multiplied across the earth. But with growth came great wickedness \u2014 every inclination of the human heart was evil continually. The violence and corruption grieved God to His very heart. Yet in the midst of a fallen world, one man stood apart: Noah. He was righteous, blameless among his generation, and he walked faithfully with God.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUv=new A.c(B.v,["God revealed His plan to Noah: a great flood would cleanse the earth of its wickedness. But Noah and his family would be spared. God commanded him to build an enormous ark \u2014 300 cubits long, 50 cubits wide, and 30 cubits high \u2014 with three decks and rooms throughout, sealed with pitch inside and out.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTQ=new A.c(B.v,["Noah obeyed. He loaded the ark with his wife, his three sons \u2014 Shem, Ham, and Japheth \u2014 and their wives. Animals came two by two, male and female, of every kind. Of the clean animals, seven pairs were taken. Then God shut the door. The fountains of the great deep burst open, the windows of heaven were opened, and rain fell upon the earth for forty days and forty nights.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSo=new A.c(B.v,["The waters rose until every mountain was covered. Every living thing on dry land perished \u2014 only Noah and those with him in the ark survived. After 150 days, the waters began to recede. Noah sent out a dove, and when it returned with a fresh olive leaf, he knew the earth was drying. When they finally stepped onto dry ground, Noah built an altar and worshiped the Lord. God set a rainbow in the sky as an everlasting sign of His covenant: never again would a flood destroy all life on earth.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.an5=A.a(s([B.aSJ,B.aUv,B.aTQ,B.aSo]),t.o)
B.a9h=A.a(s(["To water the crops","Because of the wickedness of mankind","To test Noah's faith","To reshape the continents"]),t.s)
B.aAG=new A.c(B.l,["Why did God decide to send a flood upon the earth?",B.a9h,"Because of the wickedness of mankind","God saw that the wickedness of man was great on the earth, and every intent of the thoughts of his heart was only evil continually.","Genesis 6:5-7"],t.M)
B.a9r=A.a(s(["A mighty warrior","A just man, perfect in his generations","The wisest man alive","A wealthy landowner"]),t.s)
B.aCh=new A.c(B.l,["How was Noah described in the Bible?",B.a9r,"A just man, perfect in his generations","Noah was a just man, perfect in his generations. Noah walked with God.","Genesis 6:9"],t.M)
B.a5_=A.a(s(["200 x 40 x 20","300 x 50 x 30","450 x 75 x 45","100 x 25 x 15"]),t.s)
B.aEI=new A.c(B.l,["What were the dimensions of the ark in cubits (length x width x height)?",B.a5_,"300 x 50 x 30","God told Noah to make the ark 300 cubits long, 50 cubits wide, and 30 cubits high.","Genesis 6:15"],t.M)
B.aDD=new A.c(B.l,["How many decks (stories) did the ark have?",B.zr,"Three","God instructed Noah to make the ark with lower, second, and third decks \u2014 three stories in total.","Genesis 6:16"],t.M)
B.as2=A.a(s(["Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob","Shem, Ham, and Japheth","Cain, Abel, and Seth","Reuben, Simeon, and Levi"]),t.s)
B.aFt=new A.c(B.l,["What were the names of Noah's three sons?",B.as2,"Shem, Ham, and Japheth","Noah had three sons: Shem, Ham, and Japheth, and all three entered the ark with their wives.","Genesis 6:10"],t.M)
B.a70=A.a(s(["7 days and 7 nights","40 days and 40 nights","100 days and 100 nights","150 days and 150 nights"]),t.s)
B.aED=new A.c(B.l,["How long did it rain during the flood?",B.a70,"40 days and 40 nights","The rain was upon the earth forty days and forty nights, flooding the entire world.","Genesis 7:12"],t.M)
B.aoP=A.a(s(["One pair","Two pairs","Seven pairs","Ten pairs"]),t.s)
B.aGq=new A.c(B.l,["How many pairs of each clean animal did Noah take on the ark?",B.aoP,"Seven pairs","God told Noah to take seven pairs of every clean animal, male and female, onto the ark.","Genesis 7:2"],t.M)
B.a5Q=A.a(s(["A dove","A raven","A sparrow","An eagle"]),t.s)
B.aH0=new A.c(B.l,["What bird did Noah first send out from the ark to test for dry land?",B.a5Q,"A raven","Noah first sent out a raven, which went back and forth until the waters had dried up from the earth.","Genesis 8:7"],t.M)
B.ak3=A.a(s(["A branch of cedar","A freshly plucked olive leaf","A piece of dry grass","Nothing"]),t.s)
B.aDl=new A.c(B.l,["What did the dove bring back to Noah the second time it was sent out?",B.ak3,"A freshly plucked olive leaf","The dove came back to Noah in the evening, and in her mouth was a freshly plucked olive leaf, so Noah knew the waters had receded.","Genesis 8:11"],t.M)
B.anv=A.a(s(["A bright star","A rainbow","A pillar of cloud","A ring of fire"]),t.s)
B.aBX=new A.c(B.l,["What sign did God set in the sky as a covenant that He would never again flood the entire earth?",B.anv,"A rainbow",'God said, "I set My rainbow in the cloud, and it shall be for the sign of the covenant between Me and the earth."',"Genesis 9:13"],t.M)
B.afs=A.a(s([B.aAG,B.aCh,B.aEI,B.aDD,B.aFt,B.aED,B.aGq,B.aH0,B.aDl,B.aBX]),t.J)
B.aJ0=new A.c(B.ak,["noah_and_the_great_flood","Noah and the Great Flood","Hard",!1,30,6,B.an5,B.afs],t.M)
