B.aAi=new A.c(B.e4,["creation_and_fall","Creation and The Fall","Journey through the earliest chapters of Scripture \u2014 from the dawn of creation to the flood that reset the world. Witness God's perfect design, humanity's tragic rebellion, the first murder, and the covenant of the rainbow.",B.ar0],t.R)
B.aRX=new A.c(B.v,["In the bustling city of Ur of the Chaldeans, a man named Abram heard the voice of God calling him to leave everything he knew behind. The Lord promised to make him into a great nation and to bless all the families of the earth through him.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTg=new A.c(B.v,["Abram obeyed, taking his wife Sarai and his nephew Lot on a journey of faith into the unknown land of Canaan. Though he did not know what lay ahead, he trusted the One who called him.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTr=new A.c(B.v,["When famine struck the land of Canaan, Abram journeyed to Egypt. There, fear led him to deceive Pharaoh about Sarai, calling her his sister. Yet God protected them and brought them safely back to Canaan.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSk=new A.c(B.v,["As Abram's and Lot's flocks grew, strife arose between their herdsmen. Abram generously gave Lot the first choice of land, and Lot chose the fertile plains near Sodom, while Abram remained in Canaan where God renewed His promise.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.arW=A.a(s([B.aRX,B.aTg,B.aTr,B.aSk]),t.o)
B.agf=A.a(s(["Ur of the Chaldeans","Babylon","Nineveh","Haran"]),t.s)
B.aDe=new A.c(B.l,["From what city did God call Abram to leave?",B.agf,"Ur of the Chaldeans","Abram originally came from Ur of the Chaldeans. His father Terah had first moved the family from Ur to Haran, and from Haran God called Abram onward to Canaan.","Genesis 11:31"],t.M)
B.agx=A.a(s(["Sarai","Hagar","Rebekah","Keturah"]),t.s)
B.aAD=new A.c(B.l,["Who was Abram's wife?",B.agx,"Sarai","Sarai was Abram's wife who accompanied him on the journey from Haran to Canaan. Her name was later changed to Sarah by God.","Genesis 11:29"],t.M)
B.adI=A.a(s(["His nephew Lot","His brother Nahor","His cousin Eliezer","His father Terah"]),t.s)
B.aC0=new A.c(B.l,["Which relative traveled with Abram to Canaan?",B.adI,"His nephew Lot","Lot, the son of Abram's deceased brother Haran, accompanied Abram and Sarai on their journey to the land of Canaan.","Genesis 12:4-5"],t.M)
B.acZ=A.a(s(["A great nation","A mighty warrior","A wealthy merchant","A powerful king"]),t.s)
B.aGm=new A.c(B.l,["What did God promise to make Abram into?",B.acZ,"A great nation",'God promised Abram, "I will make you into a great nation, and I will bless you; I will make your name great, and you will be a blessing."',"Genesis 12:2"],t.M)
B.afI=A.a(s(["There was a famine in the land","He was fleeing from enemies","God told him to go","He wanted to trade goods"]),t.s)
B.aBN=new A.c(B.l,["Why did Abram go down to Egypt?",B.afI,"There was a famine in the land","A severe famine in the land of Canaan drove Abram to travel to Egypt to find food and sustenance for his family and livestock.","Genesis 12:10"],t.M)
B.any=A.a(s(["That she was his sister","That she was his servant","That she was a princess","That she was his cousin"]),t.s)
B.aCa=new A.c(B.l,["What did Abram tell the Egyptians about Sarai?",B.any,"That she was his sister","Fearing the Egyptians would kill him to take his beautiful wife, Abram asked Sarai to say she was his sister. She was in fact his half-sister, but this was still a deception.","Genesis 12:11-13"],t.M)
B.adB=A.a(s([u.hE,"God commanded them to part ways","Lot wanted to return to Ur","They had a personal disagreement"]),t.s)
B.aCC=new A.c(B.l,["Why did Abram and Lot separate?",B.adB,u.hE,"Both Abram and Lot had become so wealthy in livestock that the land could not support them dwelling together, and quarreling broke out between their herdsmen.","Genesis 13:5-7"],t.M)
B.aiw=A.a(s(["The plain of the Jordan","The hills of Hebron","The desert of Negev","The valley of Shechem"]),t.s)
B.aGL=new A.c(B.l,["What region did Lot choose when he separated from Abram?",B.aiw,"The plain of the Jordan","Lot looked out and saw that the whole plain of the Jordan toward Zoar was well-watered like the garden of the Lord, so he chose that region for himself.","Genesis 13:10-11"],t.M)
B.a7n=A.a(s(["75 years old","65 years old","80 years old","99 years old"]),t.s)
B.aBz=new A.c(B.l,["How old was Abram when he departed from Haran?",B.a7n,"75 years old","The Bible records that Abram was seventy-five years old when he set out from Haran to journey to the land of Canaan at God's command.","Genesis 12:4"],t.M)
B.agD=A.a(s(["Sodom","Jericho","Beersheba","Bethel"]),t.s)
B.aE5=new A.c(B.l,["Near which city did Lot settle after separating from Abram?",B.agD,"Sodom","After choosing the plain of the Jordan, Lot pitched his tents near Sodom, even though the men of Sodom were exceedingly wicked sinners against the Lord.","Genesis 13:12-13"],t.M)
B.a8s=A.a(s([B.aDe,B.aAD,B.aC0,B.aGm,B.aBN,B.aCa,B.aCC,B.aGL,B.aBz,B.aE5]),t.J)
B.aJ2=new A.c(B.ak,["call_of_abram","The Call of Abram","Easy",!1,30,6,B.arW,B.a8s],t.M)
B.aSF=new A.c(B.v,["After Abram's victory in rescuing Lot from captivity, the word of the Lord came to him in a vision, saying, \"Do not be afraid, Abram. I am your shield, your very great reward.\" But Abram wondered how God's promises could come true when he remained childless.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSK=new A.c(B.v,["God led Abram outside and told him to count the stars, declaring that his descendants would be just as countless. Abram believed the Lord, and it was credited to him as righteousness. Then God made a solemn covenant with Abram, sealing His promise with a sacred ceremony.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aU2=new A.c(B.v,["Years passed with no child, and Sarai grew impatient. She gave her Egyptian servant Hagar to Abram, and Hagar bore a son named Ishmael. But this was not the child of promise that God had planned.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTz=new A.c(B.v,["When Abram was ninety-nine years old, God appeared to him again, changing his name to Abraham \u2014 father of many nations \u2014 and Sarai's name to Sarah. God established circumcision as the sign of His everlasting covenant and promised that Sarah herself would bear a son.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.alF=A.a(s([B.aSF,B.aSK,B.aU2,B.aTz]),t.o)
B.aiy=A.a(s(["The stars in the sky","The sand on the seashore","The dust of the earth","The leaves on the trees"]),t.s)
B.aBU=new A.c(B.l,["What did God tell Abram to look at when promising him many descendants?",B.aiy,"The stars in the sky",'God brought Abram outside and said, "Look up at the sky and count the stars \u2014 if indeed you can count them. So shall your offspring be."',"Genesis 15:5"],t.M)
B.ak6=A.a(s(["He believed the Lord","He offered a sacrifice","He obeyed God's commands","He gave tithes to Melchizedek"]),t.s)
B.aH4=new A.c(B.l,["What was credited to Abram as righteousness?",B.ak6,"He believed the Lord","Abram believed the Lord when He promised countless descendants, and God credited that faith to him as righteousness.","Genesis 15:6"],t.M)
B.anD=A.a(s([u.u,"Two lambs and a bull","Seven rams and seven ewes","A bull and two goats"]),t.s)
B.aCP=new A.c(B.l,["What animals did God instruct Abram to bring for the covenant ceremony?",B.anD,u.u,"God told Abram to bring a three-year-old heifer, a three-year-old female goat, a three-year-old ram, a turtledove, and a young pigeon for the covenant ceremony.","Genesis 15:9"],t.M)
B.aca=A.a(s(["Sarai's Egyptian servant","Abram's second wife from Canaan","Lot's daughter","A priestess of Pharaoh"]),t.s)
B.aGu=new A.c(B.l,["Who was Hagar?",B.aca,"Sarai's Egyptian servant","Hagar was an Egyptian maidservant who belonged to Sarai. When Sarai could not conceive, she gave Hagar to Abram to bear a child on her behalf.","Genesis 16:1"],t.M)
B.acc=A.a(s(["Ishmael","Isaac","Esau","Midian"]),t.s)
B.aCw=new A.c(B.l,["What was the name of Hagar's son with Abram?",B.acc,"Ishmael",'The angel of the Lord told Hagar to name her son Ishmael, meaning "God hears," because the Lord had heard her misery.',"Genesis 16:11"],t.M)
