B.aBa=new A.c(B.l,["What does the name Abraham mean?",B.a9g,"Father of many nations",'God changed Abram\'s name (meaning "exalted father") to Abraham (meaning "father of many nations") as part of the covenant promise.',"Genesis 17:5"],t.M)
B.aad=A.a(s(["Circumcision","A rainbow","An altar of stones","A burnt offering"]),t.s)
B.aCY=new A.c(B.l,["What was the sign of the covenant God made with Abraham?",B.aad,"Circumcision","God established circumcision as the sign of the everlasting covenant between Himself and Abraham and all his descendants.","Genesis 17:10-11"],t.M)
B.agw=A.a(s(["Sarah","Hannah","Miriam","Ruth"]),t.s)
B.aF2=new A.c(B.l,["What was Sarai's name changed to?",B.agw,"Sarah",'God said to Abraham, "As for Sarai your wife, you are no longer to call her Sarai; her name will be Sarah," meaning princess.',"Genesis 17:15"],t.M)
B.ags=A.a(s(["86 years old","75 years old","99 years old","100 years old"]),t.s)
B.aCi=new A.c(B.l,["How old was Abram when Ishmael was born?",B.ags,"86 years old","The Bible records that Abram was eighty-six years old when Hagar bore him Ishmael.","Genesis 16:16"],t.M)
B.abE=A.a(s(["99 years old","86 years old","100 years old","75 years old"]),t.s)
B.aAC=new A.c(B.l,["How old was Abraham when he was circumcised?",B.abE,"99 years old","Abraham was ninety-nine years old when he was circumcised in the flesh of his foreskin, on the very day God commanded it.","Genesis 17:24"],t.M)
B.apw=A.a(s([B.aBU,B.aH4,B.aCP,B.aGu,B.aCw,B.aBa,B.aCY,B.aF2,B.aCi,B.aAC]),t.J)
B.aJb=new A.c(B.ak,["covenant_and_promises","The Covenant and Promises","Medium",!1,30,6,B.alF,B.apw],t.M)
B.aSu=new A.c(B.v,["Three visitors appeared at Abraham's tent by the oaks of Mamre. Abraham rushed to offer them hospitality, preparing a lavish meal. These were no ordinary travelers \u2014 the Lord Himself and two angels had come with a stunning announcement: Sarah would have a son within a year.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUl=new A.c(B.v,['Sarah, listening from the tent entrance, laughed in disbelief at the thought of bearing a child in her old age. But the Lord asked, "Is anything too hard for the Lord?" His promise would not be denied.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTk=new A.c(B.v,["As the visitors turned toward Sodom, the Lord revealed to Abraham His plan to judge the wicked cities. Abraham boldly interceded, bargaining with God to spare the city if even ten righteous people could be found there.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTh=new A.c(B.v,["Two angels entered Sodom and found Lot at the gate. After witnessing the city's depravity firsthand, they urged Lot and his family to flee without looking back. Fire and brimstone rained down from heaven, destroying Sodom and Gomorrah completely. But Lot's wife looked back and became a pillar of salt.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.akc=A.a(s([B.aSu,B.aUl,B.aTk,B.aTh]),t.o)
B.ah4=A.a(s(["Three","Two","Four","One"]),t.s)
B.aB5=new A.c(B.l,["How many visitors came to Abraham at the oaks of Mamre?",B.ah4,"Three","Abraham looked up and saw three men standing nearby. He hurried to meet them and bowed before them, offering them rest and food.","Genesis 18:2"],t.M)
B.agR=A.a(s(["She laughed","She wept","She prayed","She fainted"]),t.s)
B.aCR=new A.c(B.l,["What did Sarah do when she heard she would have a son?",B.agR,"She laughed",'Sarah laughed to herself, thinking, "After I am worn out and my lord is old, will I now have this pleasure?" The Lord then asked Abraham why Sarah laughed.',"Genesis 18:12-13"],t.M)
B.agY=A.a(s(["Ten","Five","Twenty","One"]),t.s)
B.aE3=new A.c(B.l,["What was the lowest number of righteous people Abraham bargained down to in order to spare Sodom?",B.agY,"Ten","Abraham progressively negotiated with God from fifty righteous people down to ten. God agreed He would not destroy Sodom if ten righteous people were found there.","Genesis 18:32"],t.M)
B.a47=A.a(s(["At the gate of Sodom","In his house","In the marketplace","By the well"]),t.s)
B.aG0=new A.c(B.l,["Where was Lot sitting when the two angels arrived in Sodom?",B.a47,"At the gate of Sodom","The two angels arrived at Sodom in the evening, and Lot was sitting in the gateway of the city. He bowed down to them and invited them to his home.","Genesis 19:1"],t.M)
B.ajR=A.a(s(["Burning sulfur (brimstone) and fire","A great flood","Hailstones and lightning","Darkness and plague"]),t.s)
B.aGA=new A.c(B.l,["What did God rain down on Sodom and Gomorrah?",B.ajR,"Burning sulfur (brimstone) and fire","The Lord rained down burning sulfur on Sodom and Gomorrah \u2014 from the Lord out of the heavens, completely destroying the cities and the entire plain.","Genesis 19:24"],t.M)
B.ad0=A.a(s(["She became a pillar of salt","She was struck by lightning","She was consumed by fire","She turned to stone"]),t.s)
B.aF_=new A.c(B.l,["What happened to Lot's wife when she looked back?",B.ad0,"She became a pillar of salt","Despite the angels' warning not to look back, Lot's wife looked behind her and was turned into a pillar of salt.","Genesis 19:26"],t.M)
B.ajt=A.a(s(["Zoar","Bethel","Hebron","Beersheba"]),t.s)
B.aGC=new A.c(B.l,["To which small town did Lot flee before Sodom was destroyed?",B.ajt,"Zoar","Lot pleaded to flee to the nearby small town of Zoar instead of the mountains. The angels granted his request, and the city was spared for his sake.","Genesis 19:20-22"],t.M)
B.adA=A.a(s(["Is anything too hard for the Lord?","Why does Sarah doubt My word?","Does Sarah not trust in God?","Has Sarah forgotten My covenant?"]),t.s)
B.aHc=new A.c(B.l,["What question did the Lord ask Abraham about Sarah's laughter?",B.adA,"Is anything too hard for the Lord?",'When Sarah laughed at the promise of a son, the Lord responded with the rhetorical question, "Is anything too hard for the Lord?"',"Genesis 18:14"],t.M)
B.a6L=A.a(s(["They struck the men with blindness","They called down fire from heaven","They caused an earthquake","They sent a strong wind"]),t.s)
B.aAU=new A.c(B.l,["How did the angels protect Lot from the men of Sodom who surrounded his house?",B.a6L,"They struck the men with blindness","The two angels reached out, pulled Lot back inside the house, and struck the men at the door with blindness so they could not find the entrance.","Genesis 19:10-11"],t.M)
B.adZ=A.a(s([B.aB5,B.aCR,B.aE3,B.aG0,B.aGA,B.aF_,B.aGC,B.aHc,B.aAU]),t.J)
B.aIW=new A.c(B.ak,["sodom_and_gomorrah","Sodom and Gomorrah","Medium",!1,30,6,B.akc,B.adZ],t.M)
B.aSc=new A.c(B.v,['At last, the impossible promise was fulfilled. Sarah conceived and bore Abraham a son in their old age, at the very time God had promised. Abraham named him Isaac, meaning "he laughs," a joyful reminder of the laughter that had greeted God\'s promise.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTL=new A.c(B.v,["As Isaac grew, tension arose between him and Ishmael. Sarah demanded that Hagar and Ishmael be sent away. Though this grieved Abraham deeply, God assured him that He would also make Ishmael into a great nation.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTt=new A.c(B.v,["Then came the greatest test of Abraham's faith. God commanded him to take Isaac \u2014 his beloved son of promise \u2014 to Mount Moriah and offer him as a burnt offering. With a heavy heart but unwavering obedience, Abraham set out on the three-day journey.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSS=new A.c(B.v,['On the mountain, as Abraham raised the knife, the angel of the Lord called out from heaven, stopping him. Abraham looked up and saw a ram caught in a thicket by its horns. God had provided the sacrifice. Abraham named that place "The Lord Will Provide," and God renewed His covenant blessings upon Abraham and his descendants forever.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.af2=A.a(s([B.aSc,B.aTL,B.aTt,B.aSS]),t.o)
B.a7c=A.a(s(["90 years old","80 years old","75 years old","100 years old"]),t.s)
B.aCk=new A.c(B.l,["How old was Sarah when Isaac was born?",B.a7c,"90 years old","Sarah was ninety years old when she bore Isaac. God had promised a son to Abraham when he was ninety-nine and Sarah was eighty-nine, and Isaac was born the following year.","Genesis 17:17, 21:1-2"],t.M)
B.aeP=A.a(s(["He laughs","God provides","Promised one","God hears"]),t.s)
B.aEF=new A.c(B.l,["What does the name Isaac mean?",B.aeP,"He laughs","The name Isaac means \"he laughs,\" reflecting both Abraham's and Sarah's laughter when God told them they would have a son in their old age.","Genesis 17:17, 21:3-6"],t.M)
B.akB=A.a(s(["The region of Moriah","Mount Sinai","The plain of Mamre","Beersheba"]),t.s)
B.aDS=new A.c(B.l,["Where did God tell Abraham to go to offer Isaac?",B.akB,"The region of Moriah",'God said, "Take your son, your only son, whom you love \u2014 Isaac \u2014 and go to the region of Moriah. Sacrifice him there as a burnt offering on a mountain I will show you."',"Genesis 22:2"],t.M)
B.ajV=A.a(s(["Three days","One day","Seven days","Forty days"]),t.s)
B.aFR=new A.c(B.l,["How many days did it take Abraham to reach the place of sacrifice?",B.ajV,"Three days","On the third day of their journey, Abraham looked up and saw the place God had told him about in the distance.","Genesis 22:4"],t.M)
B.aiM=A.a(s([u.nF,"Why are we going to this mountain?","May I carry the knife?","How long will we be gone?"]),t.s)
B.aG1=new A.c(B.l,["What did Isaac ask his father while they were walking to the place of sacrifice?",B.aiM,u.nF,'Isaac noticed they had fire and wood but no animal. He asked, "The fire and wood are here, but where is the lamb for the burnt offering?"',"Genesis 22:7"],t.M)
B.aa8=A.a(s(["God himself will provide the lamb","You will see when we arrive","The lamb is waiting at the mountain","We must trust in God's plan"]),t.s)
B.aFU=new A.c(B.l,["What did Abraham answer when Isaac asked about the lamb?",B.aa8,"God himself will provide the lamb",'Abraham answered, "God himself will provide the lamb for the burnt offering, my son." This was both a statement of faith and a prophecy that was fulfilled.',"Genesis 22:8"],t.M)
B.aj4=A.a(s(["A ram caught in a thicket","A lamb beside the altar","A young goat on the path","A dove in the bushes"]),t.s)
B.aG8=new A.c(B.l,["What animal did God provide as a substitute sacrifice for Isaac?",B.aj4,"A ram caught in a thicket","Abraham looked up and saw a ram caught by its horns in a thicket. He sacrificed the ram as a burnt offering instead of his son.","Genesis 22:13"],t.M)
B.aml=A.a(s(["The Lord Will Provide","God Is Faithful","The Mountain of Blessing","The Altar of Mercy"]),t.s)
B.aFY=new A.c(B.l,["What did Abraham name the place where God provided the ram?",B.aml,"The Lord Will Provide",'Abraham called that place "The Lord Will Provide" (Jehovah-Jireh). It became a saying: "On the mountain of the Lord it will be provided."',"Genesis 22:14"],t.M)
B.acJ=A.a(s(["Isaac","Abraham","A servant","A donkey"]),t.s)
B.aDB=new A.c(B.l,["Who carried the wood for the burnt offering up the mountain?",B.acJ,"Isaac","Abraham placed the wood for the burnt offering on his son Isaac, while he himself carried the fire and the knife as the two of them went on together.","Genesis 22:6"],t.M)
B.anY=A.a(s(["100 years old","99 years old","90 years old","86 years old"]),t.s)
B.aB8=new A.c(B.l,["How old was Abraham when Isaac was born?",B.anY,"100 years old","Abraham was one hundred years old when his son Isaac was born to him, fulfilling God's promise at the appointed time.","Genesis 21:5"],t.M)
B.acV=A.a(s([B.aCk,B.aEF,B.aDS,B.aFR,B.aG1,B.aFU,B.aG8,B.aFY,B.aDB,B.aB8]),t.J)
B.aJg=new A.c(B.ak,["sacrifice_of_isaac","The Sacrifice of Isaac","Hard",!1,30,6,B.af2,B.acV],t.M)
B.a4i=A.a(s([B.aJ2,B.aJb,B.aIW,B.aJg]),t.J)
B.aAh=new A.c(B.e4,["life_of_abraham","The Life of Abraham","Journey with Abraham, the father of faith, from his call to leave Ur through God's ultimate test on Mount Moriah. Witness how one man's obedience shaped the destiny of nations.",B.a4i],t.R)
B.aU4=new A.c(B.v,["In the third year of King Jehoiakim's reign, Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon besieged Jerusalem. God allowed Judah to fall, and the finest young men of Israel were carried off to serve in a foreign land.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aS1=new A.c(B.v,["Among the captives were four young men of extraordinary promise \u2014 Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah. The Babylonians gave them new names, seeking to strip away their identity and their God.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTs=new A.c(B.v,["But Daniel resolved in his heart that he would not defile himself with the king's food or wine. He proposed a test: ten days of vegetables and water. God honored their faithfulness and gave them health, wisdom, and favor.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aRY=new A.c(B.v,["At the end of their training, the king found Daniel and his friends ten times better than all the magicians and enchanters in his kingdom. Even in exile, God was with them.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aaq=A.a(s([B.aU4,B.aS1,B.aTs,B.aRY]),t.o)
