B.aU8=new A.c(B.v,["Years passed and kingdoms changed. Under King Darius the Mede, Daniel distinguished himself above all other administrators by his exceptional qualities. The king planned to set Daniel over the whole kingdom.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTJ=new A.c(B.v,["Jealous officials, unable to find any corruption in Daniel, devised a trap. They convinced the king to sign a decree: for thirty days, anyone who prayed to any god or human except the king would be thrown into the lions' den.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSD=new A.c(B.v,["Daniel knew the decree had been signed, yet he went home, opened his windows toward Jerusalem, and prayed three times a day \u2014 just as he had always done. The officials found him and reported him to the king.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSi=new A.c(B.v,["Though deeply distressed, King Darius was bound by his own law. Daniel was thrown into the den, and a stone was placed over its mouth. But God sent His angel to shut the lions' mouths. At dawn, the king found Daniel alive and unharmed \u2014 and those who had accused him met the fate they had planned for him.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.arq=A.a(s([B.aU8,B.aTJ,B.aSD,B.aSi]),t.o)
B.aeI=A.a(s(["Darius","Nebuchadnezzar","Cyrus","Belshazzar"]),t.s)
B.aBb=new A.c(B.l,["Which king was ruling when Daniel was thrown into the lions' den?",B.aeI,"Darius","It pleased Darius to appoint 120 satraps to rule throughout the kingdom, with Daniel as one of three administrators over them.","Daniel 6:1-2"],t.M)
B.ajv=A.a(s(["Three times","Once","Five times","Seven times"]),t.s)
B.aAK=new A.c(B.l,["How many times a day did Daniel pray?",B.ajv,"Three times","Three times a day Daniel got down on his knees and prayed, giving thanks to his God, just as he had done before.","Daniel 6:10"],t.M)
