B.aTE=new A.c(B.v,["In the wilderness of Judea, a prophet named John the Baptist called the people to repentance, baptizing them in the Jordan River. He proclaimed that one far greater was coming \u2014 one who would baptize not with water, but with the Holy Spirit and fire.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTM=new A.c(B.v,["Jesus came from Galilee to the Jordan to be baptized by John. Though John felt unworthy, Jesus insisted, saying it was fitting to fulfill all righteousness. As Jesus came up out of the water, the heavens opened and the Spirit of God descended upon Him like a dove.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTA=new A.c(B.v,['A voice from heaven declared, "This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased." This powerful moment marked the beginning of Jesus\' public ministry, affirmed by the Father and empowered by the Spirit.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUq=new A.c(B.v,["Immediately after, the Spirit led Jesus into the wilderness where He fasted for forty days and forty nights. There, Satan came to tempt Him three times, but Jesus overcame each temptation by standing firm on the Word of God.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.a92=A.a(s([B.aTE,B.aTM,B.aTA,B.aUq]),t.o)
B.ap2=A.a(s(["Peter","John the Baptist","Andrew","James"]),t.s)
B.aE2=new A.c(B.l,["Who baptized Jesus in the Jordan River?",B.ap2,"John the Baptist","John the Baptist was the prophet who baptized Jesus in the Jordan River. Though he initially objected, Jesus told him it was proper to fulfill all righteousness.","Matthew 3:13-15"],t.M)
B.aaK=A.a(s(["A flame of fire","A dove","A rushing wind","A bright cloud"]),t.s)
B.aEZ=new A.c(B.l,["In what form did the Holy Spirit descend upon Jesus after His baptism?",B.aaK,"A dove","After Jesus was baptized, the heavens opened and the Spirit of God descended upon Him like a dove, visibly confirming His identity and anointing.","Matthew 3:16"],t.M)
B.a9u=A.a(s(["Behold the Lamb of God",u.aQ,"You are the chosen one of Israel","Go and preach to all nations"]),t.s)
B.aAW=new A.c(B.l,["What did the voice from heaven say at Jesus' baptism?",B.a9u,u.aQ,"God the Father spoke audibly from heaven, affirming Jesus as His beloved Son and expressing His pleasure in Him.","Matthew 3:17"],t.M)
B.afH=A.a(s(["7 days","21 days","40 days","12 days"]),t.s)
B.aBe=new A.c(B.l,["How many days did Jesus fast in the wilderness before being tempted?",B.afH,"40 days","Jesus was led by the Spirit into the wilderness where He fasted for forty days and forty nights. After this extended fast, He was hungry and the tempter came to Him.","Matthew 4:1-2"],t.M)
B.aim=A.a(s(["Water","Stones","Sand","Dust"]),t.s)
B.aB9=new A.c(B.l,["In the first temptation, what did Satan tell Jesus to turn into bread?",B.aim,"Stones",'Satan tempted the hungry Jesus by saying, "If you are the Son of God, tell these stones to become bread." Jesus refused, quoting Scripture.',"Matthew 4:3"],t.M)
B.a6E=A.a(s(["Get behind me, Satan",u.dv,"You shall not put the Lord your God to the test","The Lord your God is one"]),t.s)
B.aDF=new A.c(B.l,["How did Jesus respond to Satan's first temptation about turning stones into bread?",B.a6E,u.dv,"Jesus quoted Deuteronomy 8:3, affirming that physical sustenance is not as important as spiritual nourishment from God's Word.","Matthew 4:4"],t.M)
B.ait=A.a(s(["The top of a mountain","The pinnacle of the temple","The banks of the Jordan","The gates of Jerusalem"]),t.s)
B.aCG=new A.c(B.l,["Where did Satan take Jesus for the second temptation?",B.ait,"The pinnacle of the temple","Satan took Jesus to the pinnacle of the temple in Jerusalem and challenged Him to throw Himself down, misquoting Scripture about angelic protection.","Matthew 4:5-6"],t.M)
B.ak_=A.a(s(["Eternal life","All the kingdoms of the world","Command over the angels","The throne of David"]),t.s)
B.aGS=new A.c(B.l,["In the third temptation, what did Satan offer Jesus in exchange for worship?",B.ak_,"All the kingdoms of the world","Satan showed Jesus all the kingdoms of the world and their splendor, offering to give them all to Jesus if He would bow down and worship him.","Matthew 4:8-9"],t.M)
B.akp=A.a(s(["Leave me alone","Away from me, Satan!","You have no power here","I rebuke you in God's name"]),t.s)
B.aCn=new A.c(B.l,["What final command did Jesus give Satan after the third temptation?",B.akp,"Away from me, Satan!",'Jesus commanded Satan to leave, saying "Away from me, Satan! For it is written: Worship the Lord your God, and serve him only."',"Matthew 4:10"],t.M)
B.aab=A.a(s(["The disciples","Angels","John the Baptist","Moses and Elijah"]),t.s)
B.aGe=new A.c(B.l,["Who came to attend to Jesus after Satan left Him in the wilderness?",B.aab,"Angels","After Satan departed, angels came and attended to Jesus, ministering to Him after His forty days of fasting and the ordeal of temptation.","Matthew 4:11"],t.M)
B.arF=A.a(s([B.aE2,B.aEZ,B.aAW,B.aBe,B.aB9,B.aDF,B.aCG,B.aGS,B.aCn,B.aGe]),t.J)
B.aJe=new A.c(B.ak,["baptism_and_temptation","Baptism and Temptation","Medium",!1,30,6,B.a92,B.arF],t.M)
B.aSG=new A.c(B.v,["Jesus began His public ministry with authority and power. On a mountainside in Galilee, He delivered the greatest sermon ever preached \u2014 the Sermon on the Mount. He taught about the Kingdom of God, blessing the poor in spirit, the meek, and the peacemakers.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTT=new A.c(B.v,["The miracles of Jesus revealed His divine authority over nature, sickness, and death. He fed five thousand people with just five loaves and two fish, walked on the stormy Sea of Galilee, and calmed a raging tempest with a single command.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTa=new A.c(B.v,["Jesus healed the blind, the lame, and the sick wherever He went. He touched the untouchable, spoke to the outcast, and showed compassion to all. His miracles were signs pointing to a greater truth \u2014 that the Kingdom of God had come near.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSz=new A.c(B.v,["Through parables and powerful teachings, Jesus challenged the religious leaders and inspired the common people. He called twelve ordinary men to be His disciples and sent them out to share the good news of the Kingdom.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.afU=A.a(s([B.aSG,B.aTT,B.aTa,B.aSz]),t.o)
B.a9m=A.a(s(["The Sermon on the Plain","The Sermon on the Mount","The Great Commission","The Olivet Discourse"]),t.s)
B.aDY=new A.c(B.l,["What is the name of the famous sermon Jesus preached on a mountainside?",B.a9m,"The Sermon on the Mount","The Sermon on the Mount is found in Matthew chapters 5 through 7. Jesus taught about the Beatitudes, prayer, loving enemies, and living as citizens of God's Kingdom.","Matthew 5:1-2"],t.M)
B.aoT=A.a(s(["The Kingdom of Heaven","Eternal life","The earth","God's favor"]),t.s)
B.aGD=new A.c(B.l,['In the Beatitudes, Jesus said "Blessed are the meek." What did He say they would inherit?',B.aoT,"The earth",'Jesus taught, "Blessed are the meek, for they will inherit the earth," promising that those who are humble and gentle will receive God\'s ultimate reward.',"Matthew 5:5"],t.M)
