B.aSh=new A.c(B.v,["After a series of unjust trials before the Jewish council and the Roman governor Pontius Pilate, Jesus was sentenced to death by crucifixion. He was mocked, beaten, and forced to carry His own cross through the streets of Jerusalem toward Golgotha.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSA=new A.c(B.v,['At the place called the Skull, Jesus was nailed to the cross between two criminals. A sign was placed above His head reading "Jesus of Nazareth, the King of the Jews." Even in His suffering, Jesus prayed for His executioners and promised paradise to a repentant thief.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSQ=new A.c(B.v,['Darkness covered the land for three hours. When Jesus breathed His last, the curtain of the temple was torn in two from top to bottom, and the earth shook. A Roman centurion declared, "Surely this man was the Son of God." Jesus was buried in a tomb belonging to Joseph of Arimathea.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTG=new A.c(B.v,["On the third day, women came to the tomb at dawn and found the stone rolled away and the tomb empty. Angels announced the most glorious news in all of history \u2014 Jesus had risen from the dead! He appeared to Mary Magdalene, to His disciples, and to many others, proving that death could not hold Him.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.adY=A.a(s([B.aSh,B.aSA,B.aSQ,B.aTG]),t.o)
B.aaU=A.a(s(["Peter","Barabbas","Simon of Cyrene","John"]),t.s)
B.aBl=new A.c(B.l,["Who was forced to carry the cross of Jesus on the way to the crucifixion?",B.aaU,"Simon of Cyrene","The Roman soldiers seized Simon of Cyrene, a man passing by from the country, and forced him to carry the cross behind Jesus on the way to Golgotha.","Matthew 27:32"],t.M)
B.apm=A.a(s(["King of Kings","Jesus of Nazareth, the King of the Jews","The Son of God","This is the Messiah"]),t.s)
