B.aAl=new A.c(B.e4,["life_of_jesus","The Life of Jesus","Journey through the extraordinary life of Jesus Christ \u2014 from His miraculous birth in Bethlehem to His glorious resurrection. Experience the teachings, miracles, and sacrifice that changed the world forever.",B.ab6],t.R)
B.aSY=new A.c(B.v,["After the death of Ehud, the Israelites once again did evil in the sight of the Lord. God allowed them to fall under the cruel hand of Jabin, king of Canaan, whose mighty general Sisera commanded nine hundred chariots of iron. For twenty long years, Israel groaned under this oppression.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSE=new A.c(B.v,["But God had not forgotten His people. In those dark days, a woman of extraordinary faith and wisdom arose. Deborah, a prophetess and the wife of Lappidoth, judged Israel from beneath a palm tree in the hill country of Ephraim. The people came to her from across the land seeking justice and the word of the Lord.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUh=new A.c(B.v,["Deborah summoned Barak son of Abinoam and delivered God's command to gather ten thousand men and march against Sisera. But Barak hesitated, declaring he would only go if Deborah went with him. She agreed but prophesied that the honor of the victory would belong not to Barak, but to a woman.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aU9=new A.c(B.v,["The Lord routed Sisera's army before Barak, and the mighty general fled on foot. He sought refuge in the tent of Jael, wife of Heber the Kenite. While Sisera slept from exhaustion, Jael drove a tent peg through his temple. That day, God subdued Jabin king of Canaan before the Israelites, and Deborah and Barak sang a triumphant song of praise.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.abJ=A.a(s([B.aSY,B.aSE,B.aUh,B.aU9]),t.o)
B.ads=A.a(s(["Oak tree","Palm tree","Fig tree","Olive tree"]),t.s)
B.aF3=new A.c(B.l,["Under what type of tree did Deborah sit when she judged Israel?",B.ads,"Palm tree","Deborah held court under the Palm of Deborah, between Ramah and Bethel in the hill country of Ephraim.","Judges 4:5"],t.M)
B.a8N=A.a(s(["Barak","Sisera","Heber","Lappidoth"]),t.s)
B.aFH=new A.c(B.l,["Who was the commander of King Jabin's army?",B.a8N,"Sisera","Sisera was the commander of the army of Jabin, king of Canaan, who reigned in Hazor.","Judges 4:2"],t.M)
B.agj=A.a(s(["Three hundred","Six hundred","Nine hundred","One thousand two hundred"]),t.s)
B.aDf=new A.c(B.l,["How many chariots of iron did Sisera command?",B.agj,"Nine hundred","Sisera had nine hundred chariots of iron, and he cruelly oppressed the Israelites for twenty years.","Judges 4:3"],t.M)
B.a9A=A.a(s(["That he receive a sign from heaven","That Deborah go with him","That he have twenty thousand soldiers","That the Philistines be defeated first"]),t.s)
B.aDK=new A.c(B.l,["What condition did Barak set before he would go to battle?",B.a9A,"That Deborah go with him","Barak told Deborah, \"If you go with me, I will go; but if you don't go with me, I won't go.\"","Judges 4:8"],t.M)
B.a7Q=A.a(s(["Barak","A woman","The angel of the Lord","The tribe of Ephraim"]),t.s)
B.aGH=new A.c(B.l,["According to Deborah's prophecy, who would receive the honor of defeating Sisera?",B.a7Q,"A woman","Deborah told Barak that because of his reluctance, the Lord would deliver Sisera into the hands of a woman.","Judges 4:9"],t.M)
B.adi=A.a(s(["Five thousand","Ten thousand","Twenty thousand","Thirty thousand"]),t.s)
B.aEB=new A.c(B.l,["How many men did Barak gather to fight Sisera at Mount Tabor?",B.adi,"Ten thousand","Barak summoned the tribes of Zebulun and Naphtali and gathered ten thousand men to march to Mount Tabor.","Judges 4:10"],t.M)
B.a9Q=A.a(s(["Deborah","Barak","Jael","Heber"]),t.s)
B.aEz=new A.c(B.l,["Who killed Sisera after he fled from the battle?",B.a9Q,"Jael","Jael, the wife of Heber the Kenite, invited Sisera into her tent and drove a tent peg through his temple while he slept.","Judges 4:21"],t.M)
B.arb=A.a(s(["A sword","A tent peg and hammer","A spear","A bow and arrow"]),t.s)
B.aDM=new A.c(B.l,["What weapon did Jael use to kill Sisera?",B.arb,"A tent peg and hammer","Jael picked up a tent peg and a hammer and drove the peg through Sisera's temple into the ground while he lay sleeping.","Judges 4:21"],t.M)
B.ap7=A.a(s(["Built an altar","Sang a song of praise","Made a burnt offering","Crossed the Jordan River"]),t.s)
B.aFX=new A.c(B.l,["What did Deborah and Barak do after the victory over Sisera?",B.ap7,"Sang a song of praise","On that day Deborah and Barak son of Abinoam sang a triumphant song praising God for the victory over their enemies.","Judges 5:1"],t.M)
B.apB=A.a(s(["Abimelech","Jabin","Eglon","Cushan-Rishathaim"]),t.s)
B.aFk=new A.c(B.l,["Who was the king of Canaan that oppressed Israel during Deborah's time?",B.apB,"Jabin","Jabin, king of Canaan, who reigned in Hazor, had cruelly oppressed the Israelites for twenty years.","Judges 4:2-3"],t.M)
B.aiP=A.a(s([B.aF3,B.aFH,B.aDf,B.aDK,B.aGH,B.aEB,B.aEz,B.aDM,B.aFX,B.aFk]),t.J)
B.aIL=new A.c(B.ak,["deborah_the_judge","Deborah the Judge","Medium",!1,30,6,B.abJ,B.aiP],t.M)
B.aTS=new A.c(B.v,["The Midianites had invaded Israel like swarms of locusts, destroying crops and livestock until the people were driven into caves and mountain strongholds. In desperation, Israel cried out to God. The angel of the Lord appeared to a young man named Gideon as he threshed wheat in a winepress, hiding from the enemy.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTb=new A.c(B.v,["The angel called Gideon a mighty warrior, but Gideon doubted. He asked for a sign and placed a wool fleece on the threshing floor. First he asked God to make only the fleece wet while the ground stayed dry, and then he reversed the test. Both times God answered, confirming His call upon Gideon's life.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aTC=new A.c(B.v,["Gideon assembled an army of thirty-two thousand men, but God said there were too many. After sending home the fearful, ten thousand remained. God reduced the army further by testing how the men drank water. Only three hundred men who lapped the water with their hands to their mouths were chosen for battle.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSR=new A.c(B.v,['With just three hundred men carrying trumpets, empty jars, and torches, Gideon surrounded the Midianite camp at night. At his signal, they blew their trumpets, smashed their jars, and held up their torches, shouting, "A sword for the Lord and for Gideon!" The Midianites turned on each other in confusion and fled, and Israel was delivered.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aoU=A.a(s([B.aTS,B.aTb,B.aTC,B.aSR]),t.o)
B.aq_=A.a(s(["Tending sheep","Threshing wheat in a winepress","Plowing a field","Drawing water from a well"]),t.s)
B.aFg=new A.c(B.l,["What was Gideon doing when the angel of the Lord appeared to him?",B.aq_,"Threshing wheat in a winepress","Gideon was threshing wheat in a winepress to keep it hidden from the Midianites when the angel appeared.","Judges 6:11"],t.M)
B.a4j=A.a(s(["A humble servant","A mighty warrior","A faithful prophet","A chosen king"]),t.s)
B.aEK=new A.c(B.l,["What did the angel of the Lord call Gideon?",B.a4j,"A mighty warrior",'The angel of the Lord greeted Gideon by saying, "The Lord is with you, mighty warrior."',"Judges 6:12"],t.M)
B.ac0=A.a(s(["A stone","A wool fleece","A piece of bread","An offering of grain"]),t.s)
B.aBm=new A.c(B.l,["What did Gideon place on the threshing floor to test God's promise?",B.ac0,"A wool fleece","Gideon placed a wool fleece on the threshing floor and asked God to make it wet with dew while the ground remained dry as a sign.","Judges 6:37"],t.M)
B.aka=A.a(s(["Ten thousand","Twenty thousand","Thirty-two thousand","Forty thousand"]),t.s)
B.aGV=new A.c(B.l,["How many men did Gideon originally gather for his army?",B.aka,"Thirty-two thousand","Gideon initially assembled thirty-two thousand men, but God said there were too many lest Israel boast that their own strength saved them.","Judges 7:3"],t.M)
B.a5F=A.a(s(["Three hundred","One thousand","Ten thousand","Twenty thousand"]),t.s)
B.aDb=new A.c(B.l,["How many soldiers remained after the fearful were sent home?",B.a5F,"Ten thousand","Twenty-two thousand men left after Gideon announced that anyone who was afraid could go home, leaving ten thousand.","Judges 7:3"],t.M)
B.aqd=A.a(s(["By their height and strength","By how they drank water","By their skill with a sword","By casting lots"]),t.s)
B.aCp=new A.c(B.l,["How did God tell Gideon to choose the final group of soldiers?",B.aqd,"By how they drank water","God told Gideon to take the men to the water. Those who lapped water with their hands to their mouths were separated from those who knelt down to drink.","Judges 7:5-6"],t.M)
B.acr=A.a(s(["One hundred","Three hundred","Five hundred","One thousand"]),t.s)
B.aDi=new A.c(B.l,["How many men were in Gideon's final army?",B.acr,"Three hundred","Only three hundred men lapped the water with their hands to their mouths, and God said He would use them to save Israel.","Judges 7:7"],t.M)
B.api=A.a(s(["Swords, shields, and spears","Trumpets, jars, and torches","Bows, arrows, and horns","Ropes, slings, and stones"]),t.s)
B.aGR=new A.c(B.l,["What three items did Gideon's men carry into battle?",B.api,"Trumpets, jars, and torches","Each of the three hundred men was given a trumpet, an empty jar, and a torch to place inside the jar.","Judges 7:16"],t.M)
B.aiO=A.a(s(["They surrendered immediately","They turned on each other in confusion","They charged at Gideon's men","They called for reinforcements"]),t.s)
B.aH3=new A.c(B.l,["What happened to the Midianites when Gideon's men blew their trumpets and smashed their jars?",B.aiO,"They turned on each other in confusion","The Lord caused the Midianites to turn their swords against each other in panic and confusion, and the entire army fled.","Judges 7:22"],t.M)
B.amA=A.a(s(["The Philistines","The Egyptians","The Midianites","The Amalekites"]),t.s)
B.aDa=new A.c(B.l,["Which people had been oppressing Israel before God called Gideon?",B.amA,"The Midianites","The Midianites had invaded and devastated Israel's land for seven years before God raised up Gideon as deliverer.","Judges 6:1-2"],t.M)
B.abg=A.a(s([B.aFg,B.aEK,B.aBm,B.aGV,B.aDb,B.aCp,B.aDi,B.aGR,B.aH3,B.aDa]),t.J)
B.aIM=new A.c(B.ak,["gideons_300","Gideon's 300","Medium",!1,30,6,B.aoU,B.abg],t.M)
B.aT6=new A.c(B.v,["In the days when the Philistines ruled over Israel, the angel of the Lord appeared to a barren woman from the tribe of Dan and her husband Manoah. The angel promised them a son who would be set apart as a Nazirite from birth. He was never to drink wine, eat anything unclean, or cut his hair, for he would begin the deliverance of Israel from the Philistines.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aS6=new A.c(B.v,["The child was born and named Samson, and the Spirit of the Lord began to stir him. As a young man, Samson encountered a young lion that came roaring toward him. The Spirit of the Lord came upon him mightily, and he tore the lion apart with his bare hands as one would tear a young goat.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aT2=new A.c(B.v,['Later, Samson found that bees had made honey in the carcass of the lion. From this he crafted a riddle for his Philistine wedding guests: "Out of the eater, something to eat; out of the strong, something sweet." When the Philistines could not solve it, they pressured his wife until she revealed the answer, igniting Samson\'s fury against them.',"Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUg=new A.c(B.v,["Samson's exploits against the Philistines became legendary. He caught three hundred foxes, tied torches to their tails, and set the Philistine fields ablaze. When the Philistines came against him, the Spirit of the Lord rushed upon him, and he struck down a thousand men with the jawbone of a donkey, declaring that God had granted this great victory.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aj5=A.a(s([B.aT6,B.aS6,B.aT2,B.aUg]),t.o)
B.acN=A.a(s(["Judah","Benjamin","Dan","Ephraim"]),t.s)
B.aFq=new A.c(B.l,["To which Israelite tribe did Samson's family belong?",B.acN,"Dan","Samson's father Manoah was from Zorah, a city of the tribe of Dan.","Judges 13:2"],t.M)
B.abK=A.a(s(["A priest","The angel of the Lord","The prophet Samuel","A Levite"]),t.s)
B.aCL=new A.c(B.l,["Who appeared to Samson's mother to announce his birth?",B.abK,"The angel of the Lord","The angel of the Lord appeared to Manoah's wife and told her she would conceive and bear a son who would be a Nazirite.","Judges 13:3"],t.M)
B.alK=A.a(s(["The Levitical vow","The Nazirite vow","The Abrahamic covenant","The priestly vow"]),t.s)
B.aFh=new A.c(B.l,["What vow was Samson set apart under from birth?",B.alK,"The Nazirite vow","Samson was to be a Nazirite, set apart to God from the womb. No razor was to touch his head.","Judges 13:5"],t.M)
B.ah8=A.a(s(["A bear","A young lion","A wild ox","A wolf"]),t.s)
B.aDX=new A.c(B.l,["What animal did Samson tear apart with his bare hands?",B.ah8,"A young lion","A young lion came roaring toward Samson, and the Spirit of the Lord came upon him so that he tore the lion apart with his bare hands.","Judges 14:5-6"],t.M)
B.a4D=A.a(s(["A serpent","A swarm of bees and honey","A bird's nest","Nothing remained"]),t.s)
B.aC9=new A.c(B.l,["What did Samson find inside the carcass of the lion when he returned to it?",B.a4D,"A swarm of bees and honey","When Samson later returned to the lion's carcass, he found a swarm of bees and honey inside it.","Judges 14:8"],t.M)
B.aa4=A.a(s(["A lion and a lamb","Honey and a lion","The sun and the moon","A sword and a shield"]),t.s)
B.aFv=new A.c(B.l,["What was the answer to Samson's riddle about the lion?",B.aa4,"Honey and a lion",'The Philistines answered: "What is sweeter than honey? What is stronger than a lion?" revealing they had learned the answer from his wife.',"Judges 14:18"],t.M)
B.a7E=A.a(s(["One hundred","Two hundred","Three hundred","Four hundred"]),t.s)
B.aDW=new A.c(B.l,["How many foxes did Samson catch to burn the Philistines' fields?",B.a7E,"Three hundred","Samson caught three hundred foxes, tied them tail to tail with torches, and released them into the Philistine grain fields.","Judges 15:4"],t.M)
B.ajL=A.a(s(["A sword","A spear","The jawbone of a donkey","A club"]),t.s)
B.aGP=new A.c(B.l,["What weapon did Samson use to strike down a thousand Philistines?",B.ajL,"The jawbone of a donkey","Samson found a fresh jawbone of a donkey, seized it, and struck down a thousand men with it.","Judges 15:15"],t.M)
B.aaj=A.a(s(["Elkanah","Manoah","Kish","Jesse"]),t.s)
B.aBg=new A.c(B.l,["What was the name of Samson's father?",B.aaj,"Manoah","Samson's father was Manoah, from the clan of the Danites in the city of Zorah.","Judges 13:2"],t.M)
B.aix=A.a(s(["An angel brought him water","It rained from heaven",u.c_,"A spring appeared beneath his feet"]),t.s)
B.aE7=new A.c(B.l,["What miraculous thing happened after Samson defeated the thousand Philistines and became very thirsty?",B.aix,u.c_,"Samson was very thirsty and cried out to the Lord. God opened a hollow place at Lehi, and water came out of it for Samson to drink.","Judges 15:19"],t.M)
