B.aJd=new A.c(B.ak,["samson_the_strong","Samson the Strong","Hard",!1,30,6,B.aj5,B.agt],t.M)
B.aSa=new A.c(B.v,["Despite his great strength, Samson had a great weakness. He fell in love with a woman named Delilah in the Valley of Sorek. The Philistine rulers saw their opportunity and each offered Delilah eleven hundred pieces of silver to discover the secret of Samson's extraordinary power.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aSe=new A.c(B.v,["Day after day, Delilah pleaded with Samson to reveal his secret. Three times he deceived her with false answers. First he claimed fresh bowstrings would weaken him, then new ropes, and then that weaving his hair into a loom would rob his strength. Each time Delilah tested his words and found them to be lies.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUc=new A.c(B.v,["Finally, worn down by her relentless nagging, Samson told Delilah the truth. No razor had ever touched his head because he was a Nazirite dedicated to God from birth. If his head were shaved, his strength would leave him. That night, Delilah lulled Samson to sleep on her lap and called for a man to shave off the seven braids of his hair.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.aUC=new A.c(B.v,["When Samson awoke, he did not know that the Lord had departed from him. The Philistines seized him, gouged out his eyes, and bound him with bronze shackles in a prison at Gaza. But as time passed, his hair began to grow again. At a great feast to their god Dagon, the Philistines brought Samson out for entertainment. Samson prayed one final time, pushed against the two central pillars, and the temple collapsed, killing more Philistines in his death than in his entire life.","Narrator"],t.w)
B.a7_=A.a(s([B.aSa,B.aSe,B.aUc,B.aUC]),t.o)
B.anO=A.a(s(["Valley of Elah","Valley of Sorek","Valley of Jezreel","Valley of Hinnom"]),t.s)
B.aBS=new A.c(B.l,["In which valley did Delilah live?",B.anO,"Valley of Sorek","Samson fell in love with a woman in the Valley of Sorek, whose name was Delilah.","Judges 16:4"],t.M)
B.ab7=A.a(s(["Five hundred pieces","Eleven hundred pieces","One thousand pieces","Three hundred pieces"]),t.s)
B.aEn=new A.c(B.l,["How much silver did each Philistine ruler offer Delilah to betray Samson?",B.ab7,"Eleven hundred pieces","Each of the rulers of the Philistines offered Delilah eleven hundred pieces of silver to entice Samson and find the source of his great strength.","Judges 16:5"],t.M)
B.agq=A.a(s(["New ropes","Seven fresh bowstrings","Weaving his hair into a loom","A golden chain"]),t.s)
B.aB6=new A.c(B.l,["What was Samson's first false answer about the source of his strength?",B.agq,"Seven fresh bowstrings","Samson first told Delilah that if he were tied with seven fresh bowstrings that had not been dried, he would become as weak as any other man.","Judges 16:7"],t.M)
B.a7x=A.a(s(["Cutting his hair","Binding him with new ropes","Pouring water over him","Touching an unclean animal"]),t.s)
B.aE8=new A.c(B.l,["What was Samson's second false answer about losing his strength?",B.a7x,"Binding him with new ropes","Samson told Delilah that if he were bound with new ropes that had never been used, he would become weak.","Judges 16:11"],t.M)
B.ara=A.a(s(["A magic bracelet he wore","His hair had never been cut","He ate special food","He wore a sacred garment"]),t.s)
B.aAS=new A.c(B.l,["What was the true secret of Samson's strength?",B.ara,"His hair had never been cut","Samson told Delilah that no razor had ever been used on his head because he was a Nazirite dedicated to God from birth. If his head were shaved, his strength would leave him.","Judges 16:17"],t.M)
B.ah1=A.a(s(["Three","Five","Seven","Twelve"]),t.s)
B.aFs=new A.c(B.l,["How many braids of hair did Samson have that were shaved off?",B.ah1,"Seven","Delilah called for someone to shave off the seven braids of Samson's hair while he slept on her lap.","Judges 16:19"],t.M)
B.a6N=A.a(s(["Put him in a cage","Gouged out his eyes","Cut off his hands","Branded his forehead"]),t.s)
B.aDH=new A.c(B.l,["What did the Philistines do to Samson after capturing him?",B.a6N,"Gouged out his eyes","The Philistines seized Samson, gouged out his eyes, and took him down to Gaza where they bound him with bronze shackles.","Judges 16:21"],t.M)
B.a8M=A.a(s(["Baal","Dagon","Molech","Ashtoreth"]),t.s)
B.aFO=new A.c(B.l,["What was the name of the false god whose temple Samson destroyed?",B.a8M,"Dagon","The Philistine rulers assembled to offer a great sacrifice to Dagon their god and to celebrate Samson's capture.","Judges 16:23"],t.M)
B.abk=A.a(s(["He set it on fire","He pushed apart the two central pillars","He pulled down the roof","He broke through the walls"]),t.s)
B.aAB=new A.c(B.l,["How did Samson destroy the temple of the Philistines?",B.abk,"He pushed apart the two central pillars","Samson reached toward the two central pillars on which the temple stood, braced himself against them, and pushed with all his might, bringing the temple down.","Judges 16:29-30"],t.M)
B.aqq=A.a(s(["It was less significant",u.f2,"It was equal to his other victories","He killed no one in his final act"]),t.s)
B.aGn=new A.c(B.l,["How did Samson's final act compare to his lifetime achievements?",B.aqq,u.f2,"Scripture records that Samson killed many more Philistines when he died than while he lived, as the temple was full of men and women and about three thousand on the roof.","Judges 16:30"],t.M)
